  "0{Deflection} 2/5 · lvl 59–60",
  "2Comparison of the most followed builds",
  "0{Source} · {Quality signal} · {10–19} · {20} · {21–30}",
  "0Mobalytics – Ahlaundoh, Warrior Leveling 1-60 (Protection 1-60 tab) · 165 (most voted Warrior guide), updated Nov 6, 5/15/31 at 60 · Shield Specialization 5 (10–14), Improved Revenge 3 (15–17), Improved Thunder Clap 2 (18–19) · Master of Defense 2 (20–21) · Last Stand 22, Improved Thunder Clap 23, Defiance 24, Vanguard 25, Defiance 26–27, Improved Bloodrage 28–29, Concussion Blow 30. Then Focused Rage 31–33, Improved Shield Wall 34, Bastion 35–39, Shield Slam 40, Cruelty 41–45, Lingering Rage 46–50, Enrage 51–55, Improved Rend 56–58, Deflection 59–60.",
  "0wowforever.be – leveling build (client 1.60.1.70707) · client data, Nov 1 · Shield Specialization 5/5 (10–14), Improved Revenge 3/3 (15–17), Improved Thunder Clap 2/3 (18–19) · Master of Defense 1/2 · Master of Defense 2/2 (21), Improved Thunder Clap 3/3 (22), Improved Bloodrage 2/2 (23–24), Vanguard (25), Defiance 3/3 (26–28), Improved Sunder Armor (29), Concussion Blow (30)",
  "0Mobalytics – KallTorak, Protection Warrior Guide (leveling + end game) · 138 , updated Nov 7; 0/0/21 at 30, 3/15/33 for 30–60, level-by-level order only in the level 60 build (endgame) · level order not read (page blocked) · not found · 0/0/21 total like wowforever.be; after Shield Slam the level 60 build goes into Cruelty, Unbridled Wrath and Enrage",
  "0Icy Veins – Protection Warrior Leveling (WoW Forever) · high reputation; WebSearch snippet Nov 1, build in image (not read) · Shield Specialization 5 points first, then Improved Revenge · not found · \"then Defiance and so on\"; Revenge at the center of the rotation; speeds up after 40 with Shield Slam",
  "0Method – Babyhoof (Protection = \"solo/grinding\" build) · updated Oct 9 (before the late-Oct hotfixes) · Shield Specialization right away, Improved Thunder Clap, Improved Bloodrage · Master of Defense + Improved Revenge \"around 20\" · Vanguard, then Bastion and Focused Rage (exact levels not given)",
  "0Zockify – Warrior Leveling · updated Oct 28, author not listed · Shield Block at 16; Improved Revenge · Master of Defense · Vanguard 25, Shield Wall 28, Concussion Blow 30; Cruelty/Enrage/Blood Craze from 41",
  "0Mobalytics – Kargoz, 1-60 Protection Warrior (community) · 15 , Oct 14, ends 5/6/40 at 60 · not read · not found · at 60 points: 40 Protection, 6 Fury, 5 Arms (same setup: \"Prot + bits\")",
  "0Mobalytics – Ahlaundoh, Warrior Leveling 1-60 (Verified, Arms) · 165 , updated Nov 6, 32/19/0 at 60 · Improved Rend 3 (10–12), Deflection, Improved Overpower, Improved Charge · Deep Wounds 3 (20–22) · Deflection 5, Spearing Strike (25), Two-Handed Weapon Specialization 3, Impale, Sweeping Strikes (30); then Bloodthrill, Weaponmaster, Improved Slam, Mortal Strike at 40, Fury from 42",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Passion · no date (after Oct 1); no level order in the text · gives 3 builds at 30: Arms 26/0/0, Fury 0/26/0, Prot 0/0/26 (26 = with Legacy Talented) · Prot: move points from Defiance to Improved Thunder Clap if you do few dungeons · Prot \"strong for AoE and loses little health\"; Arms \"classic choice, burst and stability\"",
  "3Arms (two-handed) – group / duo with healer",
  "0{Who recommends it:} Method (Babyhoof, Oct 9: \"group build\"), Icy Veins (Oct 26), Mobalytics Ahlaundoh (48 ), Maxroll (Soda, Oct 30: two-handed build \"strong in dungeons and on 2 targets but without sustain\"). Sweeping Strikes is \"the most important talent\" for Mobalytics.",
  "0• Icy Veins order (snippet): Slam at 20, Spearing Strike at 25, Sweeping Strikes at 30, Mortal Strike at 40, Weaponmaster 37–39 and 41–42.",
  "0• Method order: Cruelty (Fury) first of all, then Improved Rend, Tactical Mastery, Deep Wounds, Bloodthrill, Sweeping Strikes, Weaponmaster, Mortal Strike, Unbridled Wrath.",
  "0• Warcraft Tavern: Overpower, Sweeping Strikes, Deflection; Spearing Strike useful only against Giants/Dragonkin: skip it and max Two-Handed Weapon Specialization. Bloodthrill before Weaponmaster.",
  "0• Weapon: axes and polearms give +5% crit with Weaponmaster; mace/staff ignore 15% armor; swords have extra attack procs.",
  "0Pro: higher single-target damage. Con: no sustain, you need First Aid and/or a healer.",
  "3Fury (dual wield) – second spec from 40",
  "0Fury can't dual wield before 20, and according to Maxroll it's weak until 36 (Whirlwind); Bloodthirst arrives at 40. Mobalytics (Kargoz, video 90k views, Oct 8) and Zockify (Oct 28) use it mainly as a second spec for outdoor questing after 40 (Dual Specialization at 40).",
  "0• 30 build (Mobalytics, snippet): 0/21/0 with Cruelty, Unbridled Wrath, Lingering Rage, Enrage all 5/5 and the last point in Death Wish. Warcraft Tavern: Furious Precision, Piercing Howl, Raging Blows with Whirlwind.",
  "0• Gore Drinker () heals 1% max HP for 3 hits after Enrage/Berserker Rage/Bloodrage/Death Wish/Bloodthirst: free sustain.",
  "0• Mobalytics recommends Dwarf for Fury until 30 (snippet).",
  "3Legacy talent: Thrill of Adventure",
  "0Zockify recommends the first 5 Legacy points in {Thrill of Adventure} (recovers health after outdoor kills, less downtime): useful for a Warrior without a heal. single source, not verified in the client. Warcraft Tavern note: Legacy Points (Talented) bring talents forward up to 5 levels.",
  "3Legacy perk “Talented”",
  "0Talented gives up to 5 extra talent points: follow the {same order} 5 levels early (first talent point at 5). At level L you will have the level L+5 build.",
  "1Rotation",
  "31–9 · Battle Stance, Rage from auto-attacks",
  "0^ability_warrior_battleshout,ability_warrior_charge,ability_gouge,ability_rogue_ambush,ability_shockwave^Battle Shout -> Charge (4) -> Rend (4) -> Heroic Strike -> Hamstring (8)",
  "0Battle Shout, Charge to open (9 Rage), Rend if the mob lives at least a few ticks, then Heroic Strike with excess Rage. Thunder Clap (6) on packs, Hamstring (8) to escape. Rage comes from weapon speed, not damage: slow and heavy weapon = more Rage per hit (Warcraft Tavern, Kami).",
  "310–19 · Defensive Stance, shield, Revenge",
  "0^ability_warrior_defensivestance,ability_defend,ability_warrior_revenge,ability_warrior_sunder,spell_nature_thunderclap,ability_rogue_ambush^Defensive Stance -> Shield Block (16) -> Revenge (14) -> Sunder Armor -> Thunder Clap -> Heroic Strike",
  "0After the class quest (10) switch to 1H + shield. Open with Charge in Battle Stance (stance dance, Tactical Mastery at 14 keeps up to 10 Rage) or without Charge in Defensive until you have Vanguard. Shield Block (16) -> Revenge as soon as it procs -> Sunder Armor or Thunder Clap -> Heroic Strike with excess Rage. With Shield Specialization every Block gives 5 Rage.",
  "320–30 · Revenge + Victory Rush + Concussion Blow",
  "0^ability_warrior_charge,ability_defend,ability_warrior_revenge,ability_warrior_devastate,ability_warrior_cleave,ability_thunderbolt^Charge (from 25 in Defensive) -> Shield Block -> Revenge -> Victory Rush -> Cleave (2+) -> Concussion Blow (30)",
  "0From 25 (Vanguard) open with Charge without leaving Defensive. Cycle: Shield Block -> Revenge -> Sunder Armor/Thunder Clap -> Heroic Strike. As soon as a mob dies, use Victory Rush on the next one (heals 10%). Execute (24) requires Battle/Berserker Stance: in Protection the Stance switch usually isn't worth it ( my assessment, no source says so). Concussion Blow (30) as an emergency stun. From 40: Shield Slam on every cooldown.",
  "3AoE / multiple pulls",
  "0^ability_warrior_warcry,spell_nature_thunderclap,ability_warrior_revenge,ability_warrior_cleave,ability_warrior_shieldwall^Demoralizing Shout -> Thunder Clap -> Revenge -> Cleave -> Shield Wall (28)",
  "0Protection is the spec that handles packs best (Warcraft Tavern, Zockify): Demoralizing Shout (14) + Thunder Clap (-20% attack speed, 4 targets), then Revenge and Cleave (20) instead of Heroic Strike. Cooldowns to pull more: Intimidating Shout (22), Retaliation, Shield Wall (28), Last Stand (22).",
  "3Rage and downtime",
  "0• Normalized Rage: hits give Rage based on weapon speed and not damage, and armor no longer reduces the Rage from damage taken (Oct 8 build). Crits give +100% Rage.",
  "0• Anger Management (56) and Unbridled Wrath (60) arrive late in the wowforever.be build; before 30 the Rage comes from Block, Dodge/Parry, Bloodrage and Charge.",
  "0• The Warrior has no heal: {Victory Rush} (20+), First Aid bandages between pulls, Cooking for the XP buff. Advice shared by Maxroll, Method and Zockify.",
  "0• Don't spend all your Rage on Execute if the mob has low HP: save it for the next one (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "3Stance",
  "0• {Battle:} Charge, Overpower, Execute, Mocking Blow, Retaliation. {Defensive:} Revenge, Shield Block, Disarm, Taunt. {Berserker (30):} Whirlwind, Pummel, Intercept, Berserker Rage.",
  "0• Maxroll: stay in Battle Stance before Improved Tactical Mastery and in Defensive before Vanguard (switching for Charge brings you to 10 Rage).",
  "3Kiting and escape",
  "0Hamstring (8) and Intimidating Shout (22) to get out of wrong pulls, Shield Bash/Pummel for casters. Discouraged by most guides: pulling more mobs than you should before having Shield Block.",
  "3Stats and weapon",
  "0Leveling priority (Warcraft Tavern): Weapon DPS -> Strength/Attack Power -> Stamina -> Agility -> Armor. Protection: 1H + shield; wear the highest armor possible while meeting Strength/Stamina (Maxroll). 1H weapons (Zockify): Alliance Durgen's Crescent Axe (13), Cruel Barb (19), Hamhock's Cleaver (25); Horde Thick War Axe (12, crafted), Hammer of Orgrimmar (quest 16), Wingblade (quest 22); then Pronged Reaver (30), Glutton's Cleaver (37), Thrash Blade (quest 51). Shields: Welding Shield (quest 16), Commander's Crest (21), Bonepile Gaze (28), Aegis of the Scarlet Commander (39), Stoneshell Guard (47), Draconian Deflector (58). 2H for Arms: Copper Battle Axe (8, crafted), Corpse Chopper (16), Strike of the Hydra (26), Corpsemaker (29), Whirlwind Axe (quest 40). How to get individual items: not found (Zockify only gives level/type). Dungeons to chase (Maxroll, recommended level): Hall of Thanes 13–18, Ragefire Chasm 13–18, Ruins of Lordaeron 15–20, Shadowfang Keep 17–22, Deadmines and Wailing Caverns 18–23, Stockade and City of Dalaran 25–30, Blackfathom Deeps and Scarlet Monastery Graveyard 27–32, Gnomeregan 29–34, Excavation Site: Wetlands 31–36 (the Forever client says 26–31 from Oct 1).",
  "3New in Forever for the class",
  "0• Normalized Rage: Rage from hits by weapon speed and not damage; armor no longer reduces the Rage from damage taken, crits +100% Rage (Kami Sep 30; Blizzard Oct 1/8).",
  "0• Protection: Shield Specialization gives 5 Rage per Block and 100% chance; Master of Defense, Vanguard and Focused Rage are new; Bastion +10% damage with shield; Shield Block blocks 2 attacks for 7 s (Kami Sep 30).",
  "0• From Sep 24, Bastion and Focused Rage swapped rows; from Oct 1 Iron Will, Anticipation and Improved Bloodrage are in the first two rows and Toughness was removed (Blizzard notes).",
  "0• Tactical Mastery and Victory Rush (20) are base spells; Berserker Rage at 30 (was 32); Slam at 20; Battle Shout raid-wide from Oct 15 (Blizzard / wowforever.be).",
  "0• New Arms talents: Spearing Strike (from Oct 1 no 2H, requires Battle Stance), Bloodthrill (2 ranks since 3 Nov, 10–20%, Main Hand only), Weaponmaster; Fury: Lingering Rage, Furious Precision, Gore Drinker (Oct 1), Reckless Swings and Improved Whirlwind (3 Nov, replacing Raging Blows).",
  "0• Oct 8: Rage from warrior quests rebalanced (about 20–40% per level); Demoralizing Shout generates threat; Oct 16: Overpower works on much lower-level mobs, Slam doesn't suffer pushback.",
  "0• Dual Talent Specialization at level 40 (wowforever.be, Warcraft Tavern). Zephras Isle has new Warrior Trainers (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• Server hotfix on Oct 30 (216 talents/spells touched, unverified aggregator): impossible to know whether they affect Warrior; re-check the tooltips in-game.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): Defensive Stance +80% threat (was 30%), Defiance up to 20%, Two-Handed Weapon Specialization 2/4/6%, Slam 15 sec cooldown; Improved Tactical Mastery now 3 ranks (5/10/15 Rage), Flurry 3 ranks and no longer needs Death Wish, Bloodthirst needs Death Wish, Enrage in row 3.",
  "1Spells by level",
  "0Visit your Trainer every 2 levels: your damage comes from the Ranks.",
  "0{Battle Shout} Lvl 1\nAttack Power buff for the whole party/raid (3 min, 10 Rage). Raid-wide from Oct 15. Keep it always up.",
  "0{Heroic Strike} Lvl 1\nExtra hit on the next swing, spends excess Rage (15 Rage at Rank 1).",
  "0{Rend} Lvl 4\nBleed (10 Rage) that ignores armor; don't use it on mobs that die right away. Used in Battle and Defensive Stance.",
  "0{Charge} Lvl 4\nCharge + 1 s stun, generates 9 Rage (Rank 1); only out of combat, in Battle Stance (in Defensive after Vanguard at 25).",
  "0{Thunder Clap} Lvl 6\n20 Rage, 20% attack speed on up to 4 enemies, 6 s CD: packs and strong mobs. Battle or Defensive.",
  "0{Hamstring} Lvl 8\n-40% movement for 15 s: kiting and escaping wrong pulls.",
  "0{Bloodrage} Lvl 10\n10 Rage immediately + 10 over 10 s at the cost of health (20% base HP), 1 min CD.",
  "0{Sunder Armor} Lvl 10\nClass quest at 10 (Defensive Stance, Taunt, Sunder Armor): -armor up to 5 stacks, high threat.",
  "0{Defensive Stance} Lvl 10\nClass quest: -10% damage taken and dealt, +30% threat; the base of the Protection build. Taunt (8 s CD) from the same quest.",
  "0{Overpower} Lvl 12\nOnly after the target dodges, Battle Stance, 5 Rage. From Oct 16 it also works on mobs much lower level.",
  "0{Shield Bash} Lvl 12\nInterrupts a cast (10 Rage, 12 s CD), Battle or Defensive.",
  "0{Revenge} Lvl 14\nDefensive Stance only, after block/dodge/parry: 5 Rage, 5 s CD, your main damage in Protection.",
  "0{Demoralizing Shout} Lvl 14\nReduces enemies' Attack Power within 10 yd (10 Rage). From Oct 8 it generates threat.",
  "0{Tactical Mastery} Lvl 14\nNow a base spell: keeps up to 10 Rage when switching Stance (Improved Tactical Mastery brings it to 25).",
  "0{Shield Block} Lvl 16\n+75% Block for 7 s but only 2 attacks (Classic: 5 s, 1 attack). Defensive Stance, 10 Rage, 5 s CD: activates Revenge and gives Rage with Shield Specialization.",
  "0{Mocking Blow} Lvl 16\nForces the target to attack you for 6 s (2 min CD, Battle Stance).",
  "0{Disarm} Lvl 18\nDisarms the enemy for 10 s (Defensive Stance, 1 min CD).",
  "0{Slam} Lvl 20\nAt 20 instead of Classic's 30: 1,5 s cast, 15 Rage, 18 s CD (Improved Slam in Arms). Little used in Protection.",
  "0{Cleave} Lvl 20\nLike Heroic Strike but hits a second target: spend it on 2+ mobs.",
  "0{Victory Rush} Lvl 20\nBase spell at 20: free attack after a kill (within 20 s) that heals 10% of max health. Essential for downtime.",
  "0{Retaliation} Lvl 20\nCounterattacks every melee hit for 15 s (15 min CD, Battle Stance).",
  "0{Dual Wield} Lvl 20\nLearned at 20 (Warcraft Tavern, Zockify): useless in Protection, needed for Fury.",
  "0{Intimidating Shout} Lvl 22\nFear on up to 5 enemies (25 Rage, 3 min CD): emergency escape.",
  "0{Execute} Lvl 24\nBelow 20% target health, Battle or Berserker Stance; don't spend all your Rage if the mob is about to die.",
  "0{Challenging Shout} Lvl 26\nForces nearby enemies to attack you for 6 s (10 min CD).",
  "0{Shield Wall} Lvl 28\n-60% damage taken for 12 s (Defensive Stance, 15 min base CD).",
  "0{Berserker Stance} Lvl 30\nClass quest (see milestones): +3% crit, +10% damage taken. Berserker Rage at 30 (Classic: 32).",
  "0{Berserker Rage} Lvl 30\nImmune to Fear and Incapacitate, extra Rage from damage taken (30 s CD, Berserker Stance).",
  "0{Intercept} Lvl 30\nCharge + 3 s stun (Berserker Stance, 10 Rage, 30 s CD).",
  "0{Whirlwind} Lvl 36\nBerserker Stance, 25 Rage, 10 s CD, hits up to 4 enemies (31–60).",
  "0{Pummel} Lvl 38\nInterrupt in Berserker Stance (31–60).",
  "0{Recklessness} Lvl 50\n+100% crit and immune to Fear for 15 s, +20% damage taken (31–60).",
  "0{Last Stand} Lvl 22\nProtection talent: +30% of your maximum health for 20 sec, then you lose it; 3 min cooldown.",
  "0{Vanguard} Lvl 25\nCharge usable in Defensive Stance: open pulls without changing Stance.",
  "0{Concussion Blow} Lvl 30\n5 s stun, 10 Rage, 45 s CD; required for Shield Slam.",
  "0{Shield Slam} Lvl 40\nShield strike (damage + Block Value, 6 s CD, very high threat, 50% chance to dispel a magic effect).",
  "1Race: Human",
  "0{Human Warrior:} Ruthless +1% crit to everything (Warcraft Tavern; in the Oct 16 notes it was +2%), Will to Survive removes every stun, Perception, The Human Spirit +10% Spirit (little for Warrior). No more Sword/Mace Specialization.",
  "0{Will to Survive}\nNew. Instant, 3 min cooldown: instantly removes all Stun effects. client",
  "0{Perception}\n3 min cooldown: greatly increases stealth detection for 20 sec (including on mobs). Unchanged. client",
  "0{Ruthless}\nNew (passive): +1% critical strike with all spells and attacks. client",
  "0{The Human Spirit}\nPassive: Spirit +10%. Unchanged. client",
  "0Hunter is a new combination (). Diplomacy is now a Legacy talent for all races; Sword and Mace Specialization are removed. Priest: Divine Grace and Feedback. The Book Bag (6 slots) comes from Marshal Dughan's chain in Goldshire.",
  "3Other races for the Warrior",
  "0• {Dwarf} (Alliance): Stoneform (3 min, -10% physical damage for 8 s and cleanse of bleed/poison/disease), Artisan's Precision +1% Hit, Big Game Hunter +5% damage to Beasts (great in outdoor quests), Find Treasure. Mobalytics (snippet) recommends Dwarf for Alliance Warriors until 30 .",
  "0• {Gnome} (Alliance): Escape Artist (removes slow/root + 3 s immunity), Eureka! (8 s: reduced costs and +10% damage), Expansive Mind +5% max Rage (little use with normalized Rage), Engineering Specialization (-20% backfire).",
  "0• {Night Elf} (Alliance): Quickness: +1% Dodge (helps Revenge and Master of Defense) and +2% speed; Elune's Light +10% crit for 15 s (3 min CD); Shadowmeld now also reduces threat (2 min CD); Wisp Spirit.",
  "0• {Skyborne (High Order)} (Alliance): High Order: Wind Blessed +2% Haste, Elemental Insight +5% damage to Elementals, Walk on Air (90 s CD, slow fall), Read Ley Line (+50% HP/mana regen for 15 s, 2 min CD, 100% if Attuned). Maxroll recommends both Skyborne races.",
  "0• {Orc} (Horde): Blood Fury +10% Attack Power/Spell Power for 15 s (tooltip: 2 min CD; Oct 16 notes: 3 min ), Hardiness -20% stun duration, Shatter Curse, Command (useless). Savage removed.",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Berserking +10% attack/cast speed for 15 s (3 min CD; nerf from Classic's 30%), Beast Slaying +5% damage to Beasts, Regeneration (20% from Oct 16 ), Rapid Regeneration (channeled).",
  "0• {Tauren} (Horde): Endurance +5% Health (useful for tanks), War Stomp (0,5 s cast, 2 s stun on 5 enemies at 8 yd, 90 s CD), Plainsrunning up to +30% speed after 150 s of running and +3% mount, Cultivation (herbalism).",
  "0• {Undead} (Horde): Will of the Forsaken (2 min CD, removes Charm/Fear/Sleep), Cannibalize (7% HP and mana every 2 s for 10 s from Humanoid/Undead corpses: free heal), Touch of the Grave (30% chance to drain up to 5% max HP, 15 s CD), Underwater Breathing.",
  "0• {Skyborne Windshaper} (Horde): Windshaper: Wind Blessed, Elemental Insight, Walk on Air and Skysight (+15% speed 15 s, 30% if Charged, 2 min CD) instead of Read Ley Line.",
  "1Professions and gold",
  "2Main: gold right away",
  "0Mining + Skinning (Method: Skinning \"easy early money\", useful for the mount at 40; Mining often passive while you do quests). Mobalytics gold tier list (already used in the Mage guide): Mining and Skinning in S.",
  "2Main: more power while leveling",
  "0Mining + Blacksmithing (Zockify, Method): Weapon Stones/sharpening stone and weightstone give +2 damage for 30 min and matter a lot early; Blacksmithing also produces BoP items with Defense (Warcraft Tavern). First Aid and Cooking for everyone.",
  "2Advice for the Warrior",
  "0Main Mining + Skinning; Blacksmithing on an alt/bank or as second if you want max damage. First Aid (bandages > food, Maxroll) is the most important secondary for a Warrior; Cooking for Basic Campfire and XP buff. Leatherworking only if you want Camp Tent for Rested XP (Maxroll).\nMining + Blacksmithing in leveling: your own bars and crafted weapons and armor. Endgame Engineering + Mining (Gfinity: 'At max level, Engineering is a must'). Sources: Gfinity (Oct 6) .",
  "2Best pairs",
  "0{Pair} · {For whom} · {Why} · {Sources}",
  "0{Mining + Herbalism} · For those who want gold from lvl 1 with gathering along the route · Ore veins and herbs are in the same zones. Mining supplies Blacksmithing/Engineering, Herbalism supplies Alchemy. Both sell raw materials on AH. · wowforever.be Mining and Herbalism (updated Oct 3, 2026) list it as a pair.",
  "0{Herbalism + Alchemy} · For anyone who wants consumables and gold at 60, any class · Alchemy uses almost every herb. The Mana Well and Fermenter camps, and recurring potions, give constant demand. Cost: recipes and vials during leveling. · Warcraft Tavern (Herbalism and Alchemy, recommended pair); Gfinity for raiders (Herbalism + Alchemy) .",
  "0{Mining + Blacksmithing} · Warrior, Paladin, plate-wearing melee · Blacksmithing uses Mining bars. Anvil (140) and Master Forge (300) provide a workbench at camp. · Warcraft Tavern (pair for plate and melee); Gfinity agrees for Warrior/Paladin .",
  "0{Mining + Engineering} · PvP, utility, endgame for Warrior, Hunter, Rogue · Gfinity: 'Engineering is a must at max level' for Warrior. Reagent Bot and Anarchist's Workbench. · Warcraft Tavern (Engineering with Mining for PvP, utility and fun); Gfinity.",
  "0{Skinning + Leatherworking} · Hunter, Rogue, Shaman, Druid (leather and mail armor) · Beasts killed in quests provide leather. Leatherworking crafts your main's armor. · wowforever.be Skinning and Leatherworking (suggested combination); Gfinity agrees (unofficial sites).",
  "0{Tailoring + Enchanting} · Priest, Mage, Warlock · Tailoring gets cloth from humanoids. Enchanting recycles gear via Disenchant (no node, WT). · Warcraft Tavern (Enchanting with Tailoring); Gfinity agrees .",
  "0{Cooking + Fishing} · Everyone (secondary) · Cooking gives +5% XP from food and doesn't take primary slots. Fishing supplies cheap fish. · Warcraft Tavern (Cooking and Fishing 'Everyone'); wowforever.be Cooking and Fishing (Oct 3 and Oct 11, 2026).",
  "2How to level them while you level",
  "0• Lvl 1: pick Mining or Herbalism (gathering, no level requirement). Learn it from the Apprentice trainer in the starting zone or from the Mining for Dummies / Wild Harvest quest (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Lvl 1–5: gather along the route. If you have Mining, smelt copper at the forge up to 65 (130 Copper Ore). Don't smelt ahead more than necessary.",
  "0• Lvl 5: learn Cooking (secondary, no primary slot). Cook the food you have for +5% XP from kills (Well Fed).",
  "0• Lvl 5–10: add the second primary as a pair (Blacksmithing or Engineering with Mining; Alchemy with Herbalism; Leatherworking with Skinning). Crafting can be learned from lvl 5.",
  "0• Lvl 10: move to Journeyman for the primary (lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150). If you smelt bronze, keep 60 Copper Bar and 60 Tin Bar from the previous step.",
  "0• Lvl 20: Expert (lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225). From lvl 20 you unlock the Tier 1 camps: Lodestone (Mining), Incense Candle (Herbalism), Camp Tent (Leatherworking), Enchanted Lute (Enchanting), Mana Well (Alchemy), Sharpening Wheel (Blacksmithing), Camp Chair (Skinning). These are the camp buffs: see common.json for their effect.",
  "0• Lvl 20–30: follow the band route. Herbalism 70–115 (Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Stranglekelp), Mining 65–125 (Tin and Silver veins). When you find another player's fire (Campfire Nearby), /sit for 1 minute and grab the buff.",
  "0• Beyond 30: the 150+ band requires the Expert trainer (lvl 20, skill 125). Check the trainers in town for your primary before reaching 150.",
  "2All professions",
  "3^trade_mining^Mining · gathering",
  "0{While leveling:} Smelting up to 185: copper 1–65 (130 Copper Ore), tin 65–75 (60 Tin Ore), bronze 75–100 (60 Copper Bar + 60 Tin Bar), silver 100–125 (70 Silver Ore), iron 125–140 (35 Iron Ore), gold 155–185 (60 Gold Ore); 140–155 mining only. After 185 you level by mining: each vein gives at most 1 point. Tin no longer gives skill from 165, Silver from 175. A 225–300 path is not known (wowforever.be Mining, updated Oct 3, 2026). Smelting Pants are also useful (smelt 25% faster).",
  "0{Gold:} Sell raw ore at the Auction House: ores and bars are used by Blacksmiths, Engineers, Enchanters and Tailors (wowforever.be). Sale prices: not found in the sources read. Endgame bars (Legionite, Heavy Thorium, Azerothium) have no verified prices.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Herbalism, Blacksmithing, Engineering",
  "0{Camping:} Lodestone (Mining 20): melee Attack Power up to 90 for those sitting nearby. Tier 2 Rock Garden (140), Tier 3 Molten Foundry (300).",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 1 for gathering, skill max 75 (WT table). Apprentice trainers in the 3 starting zones per faction: Kelsey Fargo (Northshire), Sally Swiftwrench (Coldridge), Fanorran Stilloak (Shadowglen); Horde: Norzsh (Valley of Trials), Vartha Rockmane (Red Cloud Mesa), Walter Mason (Deathknell). Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150. Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (WT). Trainers for all ranks in the capitals, e.g. Geofram Bouldertoe (The Great Forge, Ironforge), Makaru (Valley of Honor, Orgrimmar). The quest 'Mining for Dummies' in the starting zones teaches Apprentice.",
  "0{Item / recipe} · {Skill} · {Why}",
  "0Lodestone · 20 (trainer) · Camp Tier 1: melee Attack Power for the group at camp",
  "0Smelt Copper / Tin / Bronze · 1–100 (smelting) · These are the skill steps up to 100 without mining. Bronze requires 60 Copper Bar and 60 Tin Bar",
  "0Rockslicer · nessuna · Lets you mine copper, tin, silver and iron even without Mining. 30 charges, drops from Rhahk'Zor (Deadmines) (WT)",
  "0Miner's Cape / Goblin Mining Helmet / Enchant Gloves - Mining (+2 and +5) · equip · They open veins earlier: with +5, a Silver Vein opens at 70 instead of 75 (wowforever.be)",
  "0Smelt Azerothium · 275 (trainer) · Endgame bar; raises skill if smelted after 275",
  "0Smelt Heavy Thorium / Molten Foundry · 300 · Requires the Molten Foundry (blueprint 300)",
  "0{New in Forever:}",
  "0• Lodestone (Mining 20): camp object with up to 90 melee Attack Power, like Blessing of Might (wowforever.be camping; Warcraft Tavern agrees).",
  "0• Rock Garden (140, blueprint) and Molten Foundry (300, blueprint): camp Tier 2 and 3. The Rock Garden spawns common ore over time; the Molten Foundry is needed for high smelts (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Perk Legacy Made of Metal: total health +5% and more ore from nodes (wowforever.be hub, from BlizzCon images: numbers not final) .",
  "0• New endgame ores: Heavy Thorium Ore, Legionite Bar, Azerothium Bar (smelt at 275, trainer) (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Scarce materials: sometimes mining yields Pyrite, Bauxite or Pitchblende (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Smelt up to 185, then mine: after 185, smelting no longer gives skill (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Don't detour for Tin after 165 or Silver after 175: they no longer give skill.",
  "0• The 225–300 path is not documented yet: check in game.",
  "3^trade_herbalism^Herbalism · gathering",
  "0{While leveling:} Skill 1–225 with herbs by band (wowforever.be Herbalism): 1–70 Peacebloom, Silverleaf, Earthroot; 70–115 Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Stranglekelp; 115–170 Bruiseweed, Wild Steelbloom, Kingsblood (from 125), Liferoot (from 150); 170–205 Fadeleaf, Goldthorn, Khadgar's Whisker (from 185); 205–225 Wintersbite, Firebloom, Purple Lotus. A 225–300 path is not known. The herbs are on the leveling route, so gather them while you do quests.",
  "0{Gold:} Sell raw herbs on AH. WT: common herbs drop in price fast, rare ones (e.g. Black Lotus) are worth more. Specific prices: not found. Alchemy is the main consumer of herbs (WT, wowforever.be).",
  "0{Pairs with:} Alchemy, Mining, Skinning",
  "0{Camping:} Incense Candle (Herbalism 20, see common.json). Tier 2 Greenhouse (140) grows herbs from seeds. Tier 3 Seed Hybridizer (300) multiplies seeds.",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 1, skill max 75. Apprentice trainers in the starting zones: Nancy Songflower (Northshire), Emrys Flintbeard (Coldridge), Eleyna Duskbreeze (Shadowglen); Horde: Zor'la (Valley of Trials), Garan Sunstrider (Red Cloud Mesa), Florence Nightshade (Deathknell). The 'Wild Harvest' quest in the first zone quests teaches Apprentice. Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150. Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (WT). Artisan trainer: not found.",
  "0Incense Candle · 20 (trainer) · Camp Tier 1 (Intellect)",
  "0Greenhouse · 140 (blueprint) · Camp Tier 2: herbs from seeds",
  "0Seed Hybridizer · 300 (blueprint) · Camp Tier 3: rarer seeds",
  "0Goldthorn Tea · not found · +15 Herbalism for a while, new: useful in the 205–225 band",
  "0Herbalist's Gloves / Enchant Gloves - Advanced Herbalism · equip · +5 Herbalism each; the two stack up to +10 (wowforever.be)",
  "0Wild Harvest (quest) · 1 · Teaches Apprentice Herbalism in the starting zones",
  "0• Goldthorn Tea: +15 Herbalism for a while, new in Forever (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Greenhouse (140) and Seed Hybridizer (300): camp Tier 2 grows herbs from seeds, Tier 3 multiplies seeds or creates rarer ones (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• Herb seeds: Commonplace, Uncommon, Unusual, Scarce Herb Seeds; Scarce materials Frilled Lichen, Rosecap, Stranglevine (wowforever.be).",
  "0• New endgame herbs: Marefoil, Demonsage, Death Lotus (wowforever.be; location and skill not known).",
  "0• Tauren Cultivation: now duplicates a nearby herb instead of giving a fixed bonus (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Profession perk Natural Talent: more resistance to magic schools, higher chance of rare lotus and more herbs per node (wowforever.be hub; numbers not final) .",
  "0• No tool required: activate Find Herbs to see herbs on the minimap (wowforever.be FAQ).",
  "0• Herbs sometimes also give seeds: don't throw them away, camp levels use them (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Tauren Cultivation requires a minimum level as of Sep 27 (wowforever.be).",
  "3^trade_alchemy^Alchemy · crafting",
  "0{While leveling:} Brackets from Kami Labs (beta data, approximate counts): 1–71 Elixir of Minor Defense (~74 crafts, Silverleaf, Peacebloom, Empty Vial); 71–100 Rage Potion (~30, recipe from Xandar Goodbeard in Loch Modan or Defias Profiteer in Westfall, 1 silver); 100–120 Holy Protection Potion (~20, recipe from Xandar or Kzixx in Duskwood); 120–165 Lesser Mana Potion (~52); 165–219 Fire Protection Potion (~55, recipe from Nandar Branson in Hillsbrad, 15 silver); 219–250 Lesser Stoneshield (~38, quest reward Liquid Stone). Steps 250–300 are listed as 'after beta', not playable in beta.",
  "0{Gold:} Kami Labs: full cost 1–225 with recipes and vials around 19g53s (beta estimate, mostly from herbs you gather). Vials: Crystal Vial 25 silver, Empty Vial 20 copper, Leaded Vial 2 silver. Recurring potions = constant demand (search snippet, ). Potion sale prices: not found.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Herbalism",
  "0{Camping:} Mana Well (20, Peacebloom + Empty Vial): mana for those sitting nearby; does not stack with Blessing of Wisdom (Kami Labs). Tier 2 Fermenter (140: Leaded Vial, Kingsblood, Swiftthistle). Tier 3 Alchemy Laboratory (300: Lich's Index Finger, Crystal Vial, 2 Dreamfoil).",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 1, skill max 75. Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150 (Kami Labs: 'learn it at skill 75', conflict, see doubts). Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Expert trainers: Dustwallow Marsh, Stranglethorn Vale, Ashenvale, Stormwind, Darnassus, Ironforge (Alliance); Thunder Bluff, Undercity, Stranglethorn, Hillsbrad, Orgrimmar (Horde) (Kami Labs). Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300. Artisan trainers: Darnassus (Alliance), Undercity (Horde) (Kami Labs).",
  "0Mana Well · 20 (trainer) · Camp Tier 1: mana for those sitting nearby",
  "0Elixir of Minor Defense · 1–71 · First cheap step: Silverleaf, Peacebloom, Empty Vial (Kami Labs)",
  "0Rage Potion · 71–100 · Recipe 1 silver from Xandar Goodbeard or Defias Profiteer. Also usable by Druids (WT)",
  "0Fire Protection Potion · 165–219 · Recipe 15 silver from Nandar Branson (Hillsbrad) (Kami Labs)",
  "0Lesser Stoneshield Potion · 219–250 · Recipe from quest reward Liquid Stone (Kami Labs)",
  "0Fermenter / Alchemy Laboratory · 140 / 300 · Camp Tier 2 and 3: stations for reagents and recipes (wowforever.be)",
  "0• Mixology: elixirs and flasks last longer and are stronger (wowforever.be hub; WT). The '2x duration and +25%' figure comes from the BlizzCon demo, not from beta data: .",
  "0• Philosopher's Stone: a piece of jewelry that grows with skill (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Healing potions moved from Alchemy to First Aid (wowforever.be First Aid, WT). WT comments also say there's no more Jewelcrafting: not verified.",
  "0• 70 new recipes out of 185 (wowforever.be Alchemy).",
  "0• Don't craft what you can't sell: you lose gold and only recover skill (search snippet, ).",
  "0• Kami Labs: the 250–300 recipes are 'after beta', verify them in game before planning.",
  "0• Herbalism as a pair: gathering herbs yourself avoids buying them on AH (search snippet, ).",
  "3^trade_blacksmithing^Blacksmithing · crafting",
  "0{While leveling:} Start with Copper Bar and Rough Stone (WT). Recipes with skill bands not found in the sources read: the details are on the wowforever.be page (462 recipes, Leveling 1–300), not read in full. Uses Mining bars, so the Mining + Blacksmithing pair is the most natural.",
  "0{Gold:} WT: 'Blacksmithing provides a real way to generate gold', by selling Rods & Keys and Bind-on-Equip items. Figures: not found. Method suggests sending BoE armor and weapons to a bank alt (see alts).",
  "0{Pairs with:} Mining, Engineering",
  "0{Camping:} Sharpening Wheel (20): Strength up to 34, like Strength of Earth Totem. Tier 2 Anvil (140): craft anywhere (5 Bronze Bar, 2 Coarse Grinding Stone, 2 Medium Leather). Tier 3 Master Forge (300): Golem Heart, 5 Thorium Bar, 2 Rugged Leather.",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 5 for crafting, skill max 75. Trainers in cities and villages (WT); names not found. Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150. Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (WT). Armorsmith and Weaponsmith specializations (3 sub-specs for Weaponsmith), quests after 200 (WT).",
  "0Sharpening Wheel · 20 · Camp Tier 1: Rough Stone + Copper Bar",
  "0Anvil · 140 · Camp Tier 2: lets you craft anywhere",
  "0Master Forge · 300 · Camp Tier 3: station for advanced projects",
  "0Strange Copper Boots / Glowing Copper Boots · not found · Better stats for hybrid classes (WT)",
  "0• Repair All: repairs all your equipment at once (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Buckles that add a socket to the belt (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Strange Copper Boots and Glowing Copper Boots: better stats for hybrid classes (WT).",
  "0• 197 new recipes out of 462 total (wowforever.be Blacksmithing).",
  "0• Choose Armorsmith or Weaponsmith based on your main: the specialization unlocks after 200 (WT).",
  "0• BoE items sell on AH only if the price beats the vendor (see common.json).",
  "3^trade_engraving^Enchanting · crafting",
  "0{While leveling:} Disenchant can be used from skill 1 but isn't in the spellbook: drag it to your bar from the Enchanting window (search snippet wow-professions, ). The material depends on the level of the disenchanted item (WT). wow-professions route for Forever: Motes of Magic and Strange Dust up to 150 (snippet, ).",
  "0{Gold:} The guides agree: farm the materials instead of buying them on AH (snippet, ). Arcane Dust is the bottleneck at every band (snippet, ). Sale prices: not found.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Tailoring",
  "0{Camping:} Enchanted Lute (20): armor, stats and resistances like Mark of the Wild (wowforever.be; effect in common.json). Tier 2 Arcane Salvager (140): 2 Vision Dust and Lesser Nether Essence. Tier 3 Arcane Forge (300). The effect of disenchanting at the Salvager is not known yet.",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 5 for crafting, skill max 75. Trainers by rank: not specifically found (WT: 'trainers in cities and villages'). Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150. Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (WT).",
  "0Enchanted Lute · 20 · Camp Tier 1: Simple Wood + Strange Dust",
  "0Arcane Salvager · 140 · Camp Tier 2: Vision Dust x2 + Lesser Nether Essence",
  "0Arcane Forge · 300 · Camp Tier 3: Maker's Spark, Large Brilliant Shard x2, Greater Eternal Essence x4",
  "0Novice's Practice Wand · 1 · Base wand; Spell Power from lvl 5 (WT)",
  "0• No gathering node: dusts, essences and shards only come from Disenchanting Green or higher gear (WT). Wowforever.be lists it among the crafts.",
  "0• Enchants for rings, shard transmutation to a higher tier, rod crafting (wowforever.be overview).",
  "0• 63 new recipes out of 239 (wowforever.be Enchanting).",
  "0• Novice's Practice Wand craftable at Enchanting 1; wands gain Spell Power from lvl 5 (WT).",
  "0• Suggested pair with Tailoring: Tailoring provides cloth from humanoids, Enchanting recycles gear (WT, Gfinity).",
  "0• Disenchanting Green or higher gear gives materials: the material depends on the item's level (WT).",
  "3^trade_engineering^Engineering · crafting",
  "0{While leveling:} 252 recipes with 1–300 bands (wowforever.be, Leveling 1–300 page, not read in full). Saf-T bombs (Dynamite, Copper Bomb) can also be used by non-Engineers (WT). Arclight Spanner: recipe that unlocks from the Engineering trainer (WT). Skill per recipe: not found.",
  "0{Gold:} Reagent Bot: vendor to buy and sell reagents at camp (WT). Gadgets and bombs: prices not found. Gadget prices: not found.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Mining",
  "0{Camping:} Reagent Bot (20): no stat buff, only a reagent vendor. Repair Bot (140): reagents, selling and repairs. Anarchist's Workbench (300): station for certain schematics (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 5 for crafting, skill max 75. Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150. Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (WT). Engineering trainer: not found. Goblin/Gnomish specialization after 200.",
  "0Reagent Bot · 20 · Camp Tier 1: reagent vendor",
  "0Repair Bot · 140 · Camp Tier 2: repairs and sells reagents",
  "0Anarchist's Workbench · 300 · Camp Tier 3: station for schematics",
  "0Saf-T Dynamite / Saf-T Copper Bomb · not found · Explosives usable by non-Engineers too (WT)",
  "0Arclight Spanner · trainer · Tool for complex recipes (WT)",
  "0• Camp: Reagent Bot (reagent vendor), Repair Bot (repairs), Anarchist's Workbench (WT, wowforever.be).",
  "0• Goblin or Gnomish specialization, with a quest chain after 200 (wowforever.be, WT).",
  "0• Gnome: Engineering Specialization reduces the chance gadgets break (WT).",
  "0• 78 new recipes out of 252 total (wowforever.be Engineering).",
  "0• Suggested pair with Mining for PvP, utility and fun (WT). For endgame Mage and Warrior: Engineering + Mining (Gfinity).",
  "0• The Reagent Bot is a reagent vendor: buys and sells at camp (WT).",
  "3^trade_leatherworking^Leatherworking · crafting",
  "0{While leveling:} Apprentice up to 75, Journeyman up to 150, Expert up to 225, Artisan up to 300 (wowforever.be Leatherworking). 1–300 path available on the wowforever.be page, not read in full. Camp Tent at skill 20 with 5 Light Leather.",
  "0{Gold:} Leather from beasts via Skinning: pair recommended by WT and wowforever.be. Figures: not found.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Skinning",
  "0{Camping:} Camp Tent (20): Rested XP. Tier 2 Tanning Rack (140): 5 Medium Leather, 3 Fine Thread, 2 Simple Wood. Tier 3 Sewing Machine (300): Undeath Engine, 5 Rugged Leather, Rune Thread.",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 5 for crafting, skill max 75. Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150. Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225. Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (WT). Trainers: not found in the sources read.",
  "0Camp Tent · 20 · Camp Tier 1: Rested XP",
  "0Tanning Rack · 140 · Camp Tier 2",
  "0Sewing Machine · 300 · Camp Tier 3",
  "0Leather/mail armor kit · not found · New in Forever (wowforever.be)",
  "0• 271 new recipes out of 556 total (wowforever.be Leatherworking).",
  "0• Armor kits for leather and mail, more riding speed, dragonscale and elemental leather sets (wowforever.be hub).",
  "0• Camp Tent: Rested XP up to 5% of a level (wowforever.be; already in common.json).",
  "0• Pair with Skinning to get free leather from beasts in quests (Gfinity: , unofficial sites).",
  "0• Camp Tent is the only camp with its own cooldown: after using it you get Boosted Rest for an hour (wowforever.be camping).",
  "3^inv_misc_pelt_wolf_01^Skinning · gathering",
  "0{While leveling:} Bands by zone (WT): 1–75 starting zones; 75–115 (lvl 10–20) Northern Barrens/Silverpine for Horde, Loch Modan/Darkshore/Westfall/Redridge for Alliance; 115–150 (lvl 20–30) Southern Barrens, Wetlands, Hillsbrad, Ashenvale, Duskwood; 150–205 (lvl 30–40) Thousand Needles, Arathi, Desolace, Alterac, Stranglethorn, Swamp of Sorrows, Riverglades, Dustwallow, Badlands; 205–260 (lvl 40–50) Feralas, Tanaris, Hinterlands, Searing Gorge, Azshara; 260–300 (lvl 50–60) Un'Goro, Blasted Lands, Felwood, Western Plaguelands, Silithus, Eastern Plaguelands. Skinning is worth it for Beasts and Dragonkin, and for some Worgen, Yeti and Owlbear (WT).",
  "0{Gold:} The extra material goes to AH (wowforever.be). Figures: not found. Pair recommended with Leatherworking; for gold without crafting, Mining + Skinning ().",
  "0{Pairs with:} Leatherworking, Mining",
  "0{Camping:} Camp Chair (20): 2% crit (in common.json). Tier 2 Field Guide (140): 2% crit + Track Beasts. Tier 3 Trapper's Workbench (300): 2% crit + one trap.",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 1 for gathering, skill max 75. Journeyman: lvl 10, skill 50, cap 150 (WT table). Expert: lvl 20, skill 125, cap 225 (trainer at 125). Artisan: lvl 35, skill 200, cap 300 (trainer at 200 WT). Artisan trainer and trainer names: not found.",
  "0Camp Chair · 20 · Camp Tier 1: 3 Light Leather, 2 Simple Wood",
  "0Field Guide · 140 · Camp Tier 2: 3 Medium Leather, 2 Slimy Murloc Scale, 1 Fine Thread",
  "0Trapper's Workbench · 300 · Camp Tier 3: 2 Simple Wood, 4 Heavy Leather, 1 Iron Bar",
  "0• Beasts of the Wild: +5% damage against Beasts and Dragonkin; higher chance of rare hides (wowforever.be hub; numbers not final) .",
  "0• Field Guide (140): Track Beasts on the minimap; Trapper's Workbench (300): one trap, which one is not known (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• Legacy Bountiful Harvest: +20% Scarce materials from Mining, Herbalism, Skinning (WT, BlizzCon demo) .",
  "0• Field Guide (Track Beasts) shows you beasts on the minimap: useful for leveling on beasts.",
  "0• No gold figures yet: don't do the math without AH prices.",
  "3^trade_tailoring^Tailoring · crafting",
  "0{While leveling:} Tailoring gets cloth from humanoids, so no gathering node is needed (wowforever.be). 1–300 path on the wowforever.be page, not read in full. Pair with Enchanting for leveling (Gfinity).",
  "0{Gold:} Cloth from leveling for enchanters. Prices: not found. The Linen Reagent Bag and bags are bag costs, not gold.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Enchanting",
  "0{Camping:} Faction Banner (20): Spirit up to 32 (in common.json). Tier 2 Spinning Wheel (140): 2 Simple Wood, 5 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 3 Fine Thread. Tier 3 Loom (300): station for patterns.",
  "0Faction Banner · 20 · Camp Tier 1: 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth, 1 Coarse Thread",
  "0Spinning Wheel · 140 · Camp Tier 2",
  "0Loom · 300 · Camp Tier 3",
  "0Linen Reagent Bag (6 slot) · not found · Starter bag from Tailoring (WT)",
  "0• Embroidery: bonuses for tailors on cloth gear (wowforever.be hub).",
  "0• More cloth from humanoids and new and reworked cloth sets (wowforever.be hub).",
  "0• 180 new recipes out of 439 total (wowforever.be Tailoring).",
  "0• 6-slot Linen Reagent Bag crafted by Tailoring (WT).",
  "0• Tailoring + Enchanting for Priest, Mage, Warlock (Gfinity: ).",
  "0• For Mage and Warlock, Herbalism + Alchemy is the endgame pair (Gfinity).",
  "3^inv_misc_food_15^Cooking · secondary",
  "0{While leveling:} Recipes by band (wowforever.be Cooking): 1–50 Brilliant Smallfish (skill 52); 50–100 Longjaw Mud Snapper (55); 100–150 Bristle Whisker Catfish (55); 150–175 Bristle Whisker Catfish (65); 175–225 Mithril Headed Trout (55). Raw fish is cheap on AH. Cooking counts from lvl 1 for the campfire and the Well Fed buff.",
  "0{Gold:} Fish is the simplest route: cheap recipes, cheap raw fish on AH (wowforever.be). Food sale figures: not found.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Fishing",
  "0{Camping:} Basic Campfire (Cooking 1, trainer): 3 items. Journeyman Campfire (blueprint Cooking 90, drops from Deadmines and Wailing Caverns): 5 items. Expert Campfire (blueprint Cooking 200): 10 items. Tier 2 Cookie's Feast (140): food with Stamina buff. Tier 3 Iron Oven (300).",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: lvl 1, skill max 75 (trainer). Journeyman: skill 75–150 (trainer). Expert: 150–225 with the Expert Cookbook (10 gold, Shandrina Ashenvale for Alliance, Wulan Desolace for Horde; on AH). Artisan: 225–300 with the Clamlette Surprise quest from lvl 35 (Dirge Quikcleave, Gadgetzan) (wowforever.be).",
  "0Basic Campfire · 1 (trainer) · First fire: every camp has one",
  "0Journeyman Campfire · 90 (blueprint) · 5 items per camp",
  "0Expert Campfire · 200 (blueprint) · 10 items per camp",
  "0Cookie's Feast · 140 (blueprint Deadmines) · Camp Tier 2: food with Stamina buff",
  "0Brilliant Smallfish / Longjaw Mud Snapper / Bristle Whisker Catfish / Mithril Headed Trout · 52 / 55 / 55 / 55 · Cheap recipes by band (wowforever.be)",
  "0• Almost all food: +5% XP from kills while you're Well Fed (wowforever.be Cooking, WT).",
  "0• Cookie's Stirring Rod (Deadmines): cooks 25% faster (wowforever.be).",
  "0• New recipes: Plated Armorfish, Savory Whimsyfin Delight, Baked Salmon and Poached Sunscale Salmon upgraded (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Cooking lights the fire at every camp (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• For Artisan: Zesty Clam Meat from the Big-mouth Clam (east coast of Tanaris) and Giant Egg from the Sandfury mobs (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Cooking and Fishing are recommended for everyone; they don't take primary profession slots (WT).",
  "3^inv_misc_bandage_01^First Aid · secondary",
  "0{While leveling:} Healing potions: Minor Healing 1 (Peacebloom), Lesser Healing 55 (Briarthorn), Healing 110 (Bruiseweed), Greater 155, Superior 215, Major 275 (manual). Remedies: Anti-Venom 80, Strong Anti-Venom 130, Potent 215; Simple Poultice 90, Clever 140, Superior 210, Powerful 280; Woolen Tourniquet 120, Leather 200, Surgical 265 (wowforever.be First Aid). Besides the herb, you need a vial and spices from the profession vendor.",
  "0{Gold:} Healing potions used repeatedly in combat: constant demand. Prices: not found.",
  "0{Camping:} First Aid Kit (Stamina up to 56, in common.json). Tier 2 Toxin Study (140). Tier 3 Plague Doctor's Laboratory (300).",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: 1–75 (trainer). Journeyman: 75–150 (trainer). Expert: 150–225 with the book 'Expert First Aid - Under Wraps' (Deneb Walker, Stromgarde Keep for Alliance; Balai Lok'Wein, Brackenwall for Horde; also on AH). Artisan: 225–300 with the Triage quest from lvl 35 (Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen, Theramore for Alliance; Doctor Gregory Victor, Hammerfall for Horde) (wowforever.be First Aid).",
  "0Minor Healing Potion · 1 (trainer) · First potion, with Peacebloom",
  "0Lesser Healing Potion · 55 · With Briarthorn",
  "0Healing Potion · 110 · With Bruiseweed",
  "0Anti-Venom · 80 · Basic poison remedy",
  "0Simple Poultice · 90 · Disease remedy",
  "0Woolen Tourniquet · 120 · Bleed remedy",
  "0Triage (quest) · Artisan, lvl 35 · Unlocks Artisan (wowforever.be)",
  "0• Creates healing potions, moved from Alchemy (wowforever.be First Aid, WT). They work in combat: useful for healers too.",
  "0• Remedies for poison, disease and bleed (new for disease and bleed, not usable in combat) (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Toxin Study (140) and Plague Doctor's Laboratory (300): camp Tier 2 and 3 for potions and poultices (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• Secondary: doesn't take one of the two primary slots, and anyone can have it (WT).",
  "0• The Expert First Aid book is also on AH (wowforever.be).",
  "3^trade_fishing^Fishing · secondary",
  "0{While leveling:} Fishing changes little; fish matters for Cooking, which turns it into food with buffs and +5% XP (wowforever.be). Artisan with the Angler Extreme quest (Nat Pagle, Dustwallow, lvl 35): four fish at fixed spots (Feralas Ahi, Misty Reed Mahi Mahi, Sar'theris Striker, Savage Coast Blue Sailfin).",
  "0{Gold:} Raw fish sold on AH or used for Cooking (wowforever.be). Figures: not found.",
  "0{Pairs with:} Cooking",
  "0{Camping:} Fish Bowl (8% to all stats, in common.json). Tier 2 Fishing Rack (140): uncommon baits and fish. Tier 3 Fishing Hut (300): rare baits and fish.",
  "0{Trainer and cap:} Apprentice: 1–75 (trainer). Journeyman: 75–150 (trainer). Expert: 150–225 with the book The Bass and You (Old Man Heming, Booty Bay). Artisan: 225–300 with the Angler Extreme quest from lvl 35 (wowforever.be Fishing).",
  "0Fish Bowl · camp · Camp Tier 1: 8% to all stats",
  "0Fishing Rack · 140 · Camp Tier 2",
  "0Fishing Hut · 300 · Camp Tier 3",
  "0Angler Extreme (quest) · Artisan, lvl 35 · Unlocks Artisan",
  "0• Fishing Rack (140) and Fishing Hut (300): camp Tier 2 and 3 for baits and uncommon and rare fish (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• Stronger fish-based food: Baked Salmon, Poached Sunscale Salmon, Plated Armorfish (wowforever.be Fishing).",
  "0• Legacy Luremaster: +25% chance of an extra fish with an active bait (WT, wowforever.be) .",
  "0• Shamans reach the fishing pools more easily with Far Sight and Water Walking; Hunters give raw fish to their pet (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Cooking + Fishing for everyone: +5% XP from food (WT).",
  "2Gold",
  "0• Gathering from the start: Mining, Herbalism and Skinning sell raw materials on AH and have no recipe costs. Common herbs drop in price fast, rare ones like Black Lotus hold their value (WT).",
  "0• Enchanting has no nodes: materials only come from Disenchanting Green or higher gear (WT). Disenchanting high-level gear gives better materials.",
  "0• Blacksmithing: Rods & Keys and Bind-on-Equip items are a direct source of gold (WT).",
  "0• Cooking: cheap recipes and cheap raw fish on AH (wowforever.be). It's not an income source: it's for XP and camps.",
  "0• Engineering: the Reagent Bot buys and sells reagents at camp, so you can clear your stock without going through the AH (WT, wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• Bank alt in the capital: Stormwind or Ironforge for the Alliance, Orgrimmar or Thunder Bluff for the Horde (Method). Mail between your characters arrives instantly; 30 copper per stack (Method).",
  "0• Legacy Bountiful Harvest (+20% Scarce from Mining, Herbalism, Skinning) increases materials to sell, but it's a BlizzCon demo perk: don't plan around it without confirmation in game (WT) .",
  "3Gold tier list and mistakes to avoid",
  "0{Mobalytics:} S = Cooking, Fishing, Mining, Herbalism, Skinning, Alchemy, Enchanting · A = Engineering, Tailoring, Blacksmithing · B = Leatherworking · C = First Aid.",
  "0• No crafting power-leveling with bag gold.",
  "0• Don’t sell anything a crate needs to the vendor.",
  "0• Never list on the Auction House below vendor price (after the fee).",
  "0• Be wary of gold/hour figures: no source has measured them seriously.",
  "0• Useful Legacy : Bountiful Harvest, Reagent Economy, Field Guide, Permanence.",
  "1Dungeon",
  "0{How to run them}",
  "0• Go in {only once}, with {all} the dungeon’s quests already in your log: that run gives almost all the XP. Repeating it without quests is worth little.",
  "0• Each player must pick up the quests themselves: many can’t be shared in the group.",
  "0• Monsters inside give only about 30–40% of original Classic XP: the real reward is the quests.",
  "0• You can enter at most 5 dungeons per hour (resets included).",
  "0• The Group finder doesn’t teleport you: find a group, then walk to the entrance. Tick {Show All Level Ranges} to also see groups slightly above or below your level.",
  "0• Bosses, quests and tips come from beta guides (Warcraft Tavern, Conquest Capped): I will update them with live game data after launch.",
  "0{Words used in the tips:} {tank} = who keeps the monsters on themselves; {healer} = who heals; {ranged} = who attacks from afar (casters, Hunters); {adds} = monsters that come with the boss; {interrupt} = stop a spell while it is being cast (Kick, Pummel, Counterspell, Earth Shock); {remove} = take off a poison, curse or magic effect with the right ability (Cure Poison, Remove Curse, Dispel Magic, Purge); {CC} = take a monster out of the fight for a while (Polymorph, Sap, Fear, Trap).",
