  "1Alt guide",
  "2Do you need an alt?",
  "0{It is not required:} the cap of 16 Legacy points per character can be reached with your main alone.",
  "0{It is worth it if you want:} more Legacy points (each new class gives 3, at levels 25, 45 and 60) · the professions your main lacks · a different dungeon role · a character that gathers materials for your main.",
  "2The best alts",
  "0How the ranking works: an alt is mostly for earning Legacy points at levels 25, 45 and 60, so what matters is how fast and safe the class is to level on its own. Each class has two grades (S best, D worst): the first from the Mobalytics leveling tier list, the second from the Timesaver beta tier list. The position is the average of the two; ties follow the order of the Conquest Capped alt guide, which puts the easiest levelers first. Mobalytics – Leveling Class Tier List · Timesaver – Best class to level (beta) · Conquest Capped – Alt Leveling",
  "2Your alt",
  "0A separate plan: pick your alt’s class, race and professions here. Your characters do not change.",
  "2Everything else",
  "3Your first alt, step by step",
  "0• Bring the main to level 25: the first Legacy point arrives and the tab unlocks. Method then recommends bringing the main to 60 before switching to alts ('in practice').",
  "0• Create the first alt with a class different from the main. Each class is worth 3 points (25, 45 and 60) only if it's new to the account . Not all race-class combinations exist (Warcraft Tavern): choose the class first.",
  "0• When you have points, open the Legacy tab (Y key, Warcraft Tavern) and spend on the alt. Suggested order: Well Rested 5 (faster Rested XP), Thrill of Adventure 5 (sustainability in the world), Talented 5 (talents from level 9, requires Well Rested at max). The remaining point goes to Field Medicine (Method).",
  "0• The minimum level to spend points is not published (WoW Forever Guides) . If the tab doesn't let you spend, try again later in leveling.",
  "0• Leave the alt in an inn or capital to accumulate rested XP: it charges at 5% of level every 8 hours, up to 150% (30 bubbles). Rested doubles kill XP while it lasts, but doesn't apply to quests and exploration (wowforever.be XP guide). Cozy Sleeping Bag counts as a rested zone even when logged out, with up to 3 Well Rested stacks of +1% each (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Do quests at your level and stay in the right zone: quests more than 5 levels below lose 10–20% XP per level of difference (wowforever.be XP guide).",
  "0• At level 20 with Leatherworking (skill 20), place the Camp Tent: rested up to 5% of level for an hour and it survives death (wowforever.be camping). Sit (/sit) for 1 minute near someone else's fire or camp to take the buffs.",
  "0• When needed, send materials and gold from the main by mail: between your characters it arrives instantly, with 30 copper per stack (Method). The rules on what to send are in bankAlt.",
  "0• When the alt reaches 25, it unlocks the second class point; at 45 and 60 the others arrive (Method).",
  "3Level your alt faster",
  "0• Rested XP: log out in an inn, capital or Cozy Sleeping Bag. The rate is 5% of level every 8 hours, cap 150%; the total XP from 1 to 60 is 4.084.700, same as Classic (wowforever.be XP guide).",
  "0• Well Rested (5 pt) is the perk with the most direct effect on speed: +4% per rank to rate and cap, up to 20% (wowforever.be, Warcraft Tavern, Method).",
  "0• Talented brings talents from level 9. Method considers it useful only for leveling: at 60 it's better to re-spec.",
  "0• Camp Tent (Leatherworking 20) gives rested up to 5%. Field Guide reduces camp feature cooldowns, so you can reuse them sooner (wowforever.be camping).",
  "0• Food: most dishes give Well Fed, i.e. +5% XP from kills for about 15 minutes (wowforever.be XP guide). Gourmand (3 pt) lengthens food buff duration by 33% (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• Groups: XP per player drops with group size and collapses if a member is much higher level (wowforever.be XP guide). Only group with characters of your level.",
  "0• Thrill of Adventure gives no XP, but restores health and mana after kills: it reduces downtime to recover (inferred from Method).",
  "3Legacy: what stays on your account",
  "0• Each completed challenge is worth 1 Legacy point. There are 65 challenges (Blizzard, Method): Classes 27 (lvl 25, 45 and 60 for each of the 9 classes); Tradeskill 18 (150, 225 and 300 in Alchemy, Blacksmithing, Enchanting, Engineering, Leatherworking, Tailoring: the non-gathering primaries, so Mining, Herbalism and Skinning give no points); PvP 12; Dungeon 3 (Novice, Experienced, Master Spelunker); Raid 3 (Hyjal, Barrow Deeps, Onyxia); Adventure 2 (Lord Valthalak questline, Explore Azeroth). Warcraft Tavern counts 62 (PvP 9, because Exalted in a battleground is worth 1 point total and not 4): difference to verify in game .",
  "0• First point: lvl 25 on your first character, or 150 skill in a non-gathering primary (Warcraft Tavern, wowforever.gg, Method). Hardcorehelper also adds map exploration: not confirmed .",
  "0• Account-wide: points are shared by all non-Hardcore characters on Battle.net (Blizzard, Warcraft Tavern, Method). An alt created after the first point inherits the points (WoW Forever Guides).",
  "0• Spending per character: each character spends points in the three trees Professions, Adventure and Resourcefulness, independently. Cap of 16 points per character at launch (Blizzard, Method; Method says the cap will increase over time). A single character can earn up to 29 (Method): the other 13 can't be spent on that character .",
  "0• Cost: each rank costs 1 point. Not stated explicitly: I derive it from Method's builds, for example Thrill of Adventure (5) takes 5 points . No gold cost to spend appears (Method only talks about the reset). The reset is done at the class trainer in the capital: 10 gold in beta (Method), final cost unknown.",
  "0• Requirements: 5-point perks require 5 points in their own tree, 10-point ones require 10 points in the tree. Some require a specific perk at max: Talented requires Well Rested (5), Dedicated Study requires Bartering (2), Performance Bonus requires Bountiful Harvest (5), Frequent Flier requires Field Guide (3), Permanence requires Gourmand (3), Reagent Economy requires The Quick and the Dead (2) (wowforever.gg).",
  "0• Past 16 points, points go into a cosmetic track. Rewards are redeemed from Innkeeper Wiley in Ratchet: Replica Ironforge Air Rifle 15 points, Spectral Bear Club/Cub 23 or 25 points , Spectral Bear Tabard 40, Reins of the Spectral Bear 55 (Warcraft Tavern, Method).",
  "0• Class and profession challenges: Method's text says 'Reach 150 skill in Alchemy for the first time'. So it's almost certainly that each class and each profession is worth once per account : a second Warrior at 25 or a second Tailoring at 150 give no new points.",
  "0{Perk} · {Effect} · {Cost} · {Notes}",
  "0{Thrill of Adventure (Adventure, max 5)} · After a non-trivial kill in the world, you recover 1% health and mana per rank over 10 s. Doesn't apply in dungeons, raids or battlegrounds. Method: 'the most consistent leveling talent'. · 5 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Well Rested (Adventure, max 5)} · Rested XP accumulates 4% faster per rank, and the cap rises 4% per rank, up to 20% (wowforever.be, Warcraft Tavern). · 5 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Talented (Adventure, max 5)} · The first talent points arrive at level 9 instead of 10; the cap stays at 51 (Warcraft Tavern). Method: re-spec at level 60. · 5 pt; requires 5 pt in Adventure and Well Rested (5) · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Field Guide (Adventure, max 3)} · Reduces camp feature cooldowns: 8% per rank, i.e. 8/17/25% (wowforever.be guide for the ranks; Warcraft Tavern says 8%). · 3 pt; requires 5 pt in Adventure · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Frequent Flier (Adventure, max 1)} · 50% discount on flight paths and 20% faster flying mounts (Warcraft Tavern). · 1 pt; 10 pt in Adventure and Field Guide (3) · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Working Overtime (Professions, max 5)} · +4% skill-up chance per rank in every tradeskill: primary, secondary and class (Warcraft Tavern, wowforever.be). Method uses it for profession leveling. · 5 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Bountiful Harvest (Professions, max 5)} · +20% Scarce materials from Mining, Herbalism and Skinning (Warcraft Tavern). It's the centerpiece of Method's gatherer alt build. · 5 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Bartering (Professions, max 2)} · Lower prices from vendors (Warcraft Tavern: -5%; wowforever guide: 5% then 10% ). · 2 pt; 5 pt in Professions · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Dedicated Study (Professions, max 1)} · +1 skill in the lowest primary or secondary, once every 23 hours . At 300 in all professions gives 2–4 Elemental Essence (Warcraft Tavern). · 1 pt; 10 pt in Professions and Bartering at max · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Master Chef (Professions, max 5)} · 10% chance per rank to get an extra result from cooking (Warcraft Tavern). · 5 pt; 5 pt in Professions · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Luremaster (Professions, max 2)} · 25% chance of an extra fish with an active bait (Warcraft Tavern) single source. · 2 pt; 5 pt in Professions · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Gourmand (Resourcefulness, max 3)} · Food buffs last 33% longer (Warcraft Tavern). · 3 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Permanence (Resourcefulness, max 2)} · Class group buffs last 50% longer, and camp rest lasts 50% longer (Warcraft Tavern). · 2 pt; 5 pt in Resourcefulness and Gourmand (3) · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Diplomat (Resourcefulness, max 5)} · +2% reputation gain per rank (Warcraft Tavern). Method pairs it with Thrill of Adventure in the leveling + reputation build. · 5 pt; 5 pt in Resourcefulness · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{The Quick and the Dead (Resourcefulness, max 2)} · +5% speed while dead. Utility spells cost no resources for 1 minute after resurrection or until combat (Warcraft Tavern). · 2 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Reagent Economy (Resourcefulness, max 1)} · Class abilities don't require vendor reagents, and Tier 1 camps are crafted without reagents (Warcraft Tavern). · 1 pt; 10 pt in Resourcefulness and The Quick and the Dead (2) · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "0{Reinforce (Resourcefulness, max 5)} · -8% durability loss on death per rank (Warcraft Tavern). Only useful if you die often. · 5 pt, no prerequisite · no: spent per character (shared points)",
  "3Professions: main -> alt",
  "0{Main} · {Alt} · {Why}",
  "0{Blacksmithing + Engineering} · {Mining + Skinning} · Gatherer alt that supplies the main. Ore and hides are mailed to the main (30 copper per stack). Method calls it a 'dedicated gatherer alt' with Bountiful Harvest, Bartering, Dedicated Study, Master Chef and Luremaster. Warcraft Tavern: a gatherer supplies a crafter. Gathering gives no Legacy points.",
  "0{Herbalism + Skinning} · {Alchemy + Leatherworking} · Crafter alt: herbs feed Alchemy, leather feeds Leatherworking. Camp Tent (Leatherworking 20) gives rested XP to the alt. Both primaries give Legacy points (150, 225 and 300 each). Pair from Warcraft Tavern .",
  "0{Mining + Blacksmithing} · {Herbalism + Alchemy} · Plate melee main (Warrior or Paladin): Blacksmithing uses Mining bars. The herbalist and alchemist alt provides potions for the main. Gfinity for class choices .",
