  "3Bank alt",
  "0• Create a bank alt for each faction, ruleset and region: mail doesn't pass between them (Method) (single source).",
  "0• Capital: Alliance Stormwind or Ironforge (Method prefers Ironforge, where AH and bank are in a straight line); Horde Orgrimmar or Thunder Bluff. Avoid Valanaar (Zephras Isle): it's not a rest zone and the Inn is far from the AH (Method).",
  "0• Class and race don't matter if you don't level it: 'any race and any class works'. If you level it, the Mage creates portals and the Rogue opens lockboxes (Method).",
  "0• Recommended profession: Enchanting. A level 1 character can disenchant high-level items; the result is random. For prices use Auctionator, Disenchant Buddy or Disenchantry (Method). Tailoring is useful for 6-slot Linen Bags in the early stages (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• What to send: Bind-on-Equip weapons and armor, cloth, ores and gems, leather, herbs, meat and food ingredients. Grays to the vendor. Whites sell on AH only if the price beats vendor + 30 copper + any lost deposit (Method rule) .",
  "0• Mail costs: 30 copper per stack. The package stays 30 days in the recipient's mailbox, then returns to the sender, where it stays another 30 days before being destroyed (Method) . Account bank: not confirmed, so don't plan for it (PC Gamer, via snippet).",
  "3Crafting alts",
  "0• Only the 6 non-gathering primaries give points: Alchemy, Blacksmithing, Enchanting, Engineering, Leatherworking, Tailoring. Each milestone of 150, 225 and 300 is worth 1 point (Blizzard, Method). Cooking, First Aid, Fishing and gathering give no points.",
  "0• Method's route to 16 points with multiple characters: level 60 (3) + two alts of different classes at 25 (2) + PvP rank 3 (1) + four professions at 225 (8, since each profession gives 150 and 225) + Novice and Experienced Spelunker (2). Method says crafting to 225 is the fastest source early on.",
  "0• Enchanting alt: materials only come from Disenchanting Green or higher gear (Warcraft Tavern). Arcane Dust is the bottleneck.",
  "0• Tailoring alt: low-level Linen Bags for storage (Warcraft Tavern, Method). Tailoring + Herbalism pair for the alt in leveling order (Mobalytics, snippet only ).",
  "0• Skill caps: Apprentice 75; Journeyman from lvl 10 (cap 150); Expert from lvl 20 (cap 225); Artisan from lvl 35 (cap 300) (Warcraft Tavern). Method says the crafting cap requires 'a minimum of 3 level 20 characters': unclear .",
  "3Mistakes to avoid",
  "0• Believing the alt is mandatory: the 16-point cap can be reached even on a single character (Blizzard, Method).",
  "0• Spending points without a plan: the reset costs 10 gold in beta, and the final cost is not known (Method).",
  "0• Keeping Talented at level 60: at that point it's better to re-spec (Method).",
  "0• Doing dungeons as a leveling plan: the dungeon XP bonus has been changed several times in beta (wowforever.be) .",
  "0• Leveling in zones too far below your level: you lose 10–20% XP per level of difference beyond 5 (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Counting on two of the same class: each class is worth once per account , so another character of the same class gives no new points.",
  "0• Sending materials to a bank alt of another faction, ruleset or region: mail doesn't pass (Method) .",
  "0• Using Valanaar as the bank capital: the Inn is far from the AH and it's not a rest zone (Method).",
  "0• Crafting without knowing who to sell to: prices are not verified and sources advise against crafting unsellable items.",
  "0• Trusting sites that sell boosts or gold for Legacy points: we don't use them as sources.",
  "3Tips",
  "0• The Legacy tab opens with Y. A new point makes the icon glow blue: to turn it off, click the challenge that gave it (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• The Legacy talent reset is at the class trainer in the capital: plan respecs before bringing an alt to 16 points.",
  "0• Method suggests spending Thrill of Adventure and Well Rested on the first alt right away: they are the two most-used perks for leveling.",
  "0• The wowforever.be Legacy calculator (16 points, shared between characters) is the reference for testing builds without spending them (wowforever.be talents).",
  "0• For profession challenges, bring an alt to 150 in a primary the main hasn't used yet: the challenge counts once per account ().",
  "0• If you make a bank alt, the class doesn't matter: pick a capital near the AH and don't level it (Method). Mage and Rogue only matter if you level them (portals and lockboxes, Method).",
  "1XP bonuses and speedrunner tips",
  "0From Kargoz’s video (91,000 views, Oct 24, co-founder of RestedXP) and the Icy Veins/Mobalytics guides.",
  "0{Food with XP bonus: +5%}\nIn Forever some foods give a Well Fed buff with extra XP. Kargoz: Roasted Boar Meat (Cooking 1) gives +5% XP ; keep your Chunk of Boar Meat and cook. The bonus applies to kill XP (about 60% of your XP).",
  "0{Cozy Sleeping Bag: +3% for 2 hours}\nSit for 3 minutes. Kargoz advises {not} to do the long chain: use another player's Sleeping Bag. The chain does, however, give two 12-slot bags (see Bags).",
  "0{Camp Tent: Rested XP}\nLeatherworking: up to 5% of a level as Rested XP, once an hour. Icy Veins lists it as the most useful Camping buff for leveling.",
  "0{Dungeon once only, for the quests}\nIn Forever, dungeon XP is in its quests. Kargoz: about 40% of the RestedXP route's XP comes from dungeons. Pick up all the quests before going in.",
  "2Golden rules",
  "0• {Green mobs are worth less than in Classic Era:} a level 16 character killing a level 13 mob gets 73 XP (83 in Era, 125 for a mob of their level). Kill mobs of your level.",
  "0• {Green quests are fine:} they give good XP and are finished quickly (Icy Veins).",
  "0• {Don’t buy equip from the Auction House:} the weapon matters most. Save up for bags.",
  "0• {Duo:} quest density is higher than in Era; leveling in a pair works very well and you can do the Elite quests.",
  "0• {Crowded launch:} the starting zones will be full. If there aren't enough mobs, push further into the zone, switch layer, or group up. At launch mobs respawn faster, most of all in the starting zones (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov).",
  "0• Buy max Rank Food and Water as soon as you can: less downtime.",
  "0• New spells no longer go onto your bars by themselves (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): after each trainer visit, drag them from the spellbook.",
  "0• Legacy Points shared between accounts on the same Battle.net (said by Kargoz in a podcast, unconfirmed).",
