  "1Waylaid Crates",
  "0Crates that {drop from mobs} from level 10 (or buy them at the Auction House). Fill them with {only one} combination of materials (e.g. 20 Copper Bar or 20 Tin Bar) and turn them in sealed.",
  "0• Apprentice and Journeyman from 10 · Expert from 20 · Artisan from 35.",
  "0• Reward: Merchant’s Favor (5–20 per crate ). The {first} turn-in gives +50 Favor ; the recipes cost 30 and are often BoP.",
  "0• Turn in: {Marcy Baker, Three Corners (Redridge) /way 9.5 71.1}",
  "1Camping",
  "0Official Blizzard image from the Camping announcement.",
  "0• Lvl ~5: quest {The Great Outdoors} in the starting zone -> learn Cooking -> {Basic Campfire} (Flint and Tinder + Simple Wood).",
  "0• Basic Campfire has 3 slots (Journeyman 5, Expert 10); each player places {one} camp object. Campfire ~10 min, camp object cooldown 1 hour.",
  "0• Sit (/sit) for {1 minute}: 1-hour buff from all camp objects. No professions are needed. They don’t stack with equivalent class buffs.",
  "2Priorities for the Warrior",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP: according to Maxroll, the best for XP/hour; the Warrior has no mana buff to chase, so XP comes first.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing priority 2\n+8% stats (doesn't stack with Blessing of Kings): Strength and Stamina useful in leveling (Maxroll).",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning priority 3\n+2% crit (doesn't stack with Moonkin Aura), confirmed by Method and Maxroll; Skinning is also a gold profession.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\n+Stamina (doesn't stack with Power Word: Fortitude): more safety for a Warrior without a heal.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nExtra armor (doesn't stack with Mark of the Wild): useful for tanks but Enchanting is expensive while leveling.",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy\nMana/5: useless to the Warrior, only take it if the party has casters.",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring\nSpirit: useless for Rage.",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism\nIntellect: useless for Rage.",
