  "0Mobalytics – Feor, Hunter Leveling Guide 1-60 (Verified) · 222 (most voted Hunter guide), updated Nov 7, 31/20/0 at 60 · Deadly Aspects 5 (10–14), Focused Fire 2 (15–16), Improved Revive Pet 2 (17–18), Endurance Training (19) · Pathfinding 2 (20–21) · Bestial Swiftness 22, Unleashed Fury 23–24 and 26–27, Summon Hawk 25, Ferocity 28–29, Intimidation 30. Then Bestial Discipline 31–32, Ferocity 33–35, Frenzy 36–39, Bestial Wrath 40, Lethal Attacks 41–45, Careful Aim 46–50, Rapid Killing 51–52, Hawk Eye 53–55, Trueshot Aura 56, Mortal Shots 57–60.",
  "0wowforever.be – leveling build (client) · client data 1.60.1.70707, read Nov 1; up to 35 only · Deadly Aspects 5 (10–14) -> Focused Fire 2 (15–16) -> Improved Revive Pet (17) -> Endurance Training 2 (18–19) · Pathfinding 2 (20–21) · Unleashed Fury 5 (22–26) -> Summon Hawk (27) -> Improved Revive Pet (28) -> Ferocity (29–30); 31 Bestial Swiftness, 32 Intimidation, 33–35 Ferocity. Beyond 35: \"only covered up to 35\".",
  "0Method – Celz (Hunter guide) · upd. Oct 21 · Method; order decoded by me from the talent link ; includes 5 Talented points · Deadly Aspects 5, Focused Fire 2, Improved Revive Pet 1, Endurance Training 2 · Unleashed Fury (20–24) · Summon Hawk 25, Improved Revive Pet 26, Ferocity 27–28, Bestial Swiftness 29, Intimidation 30. With Talented: Ferocity at 5/5 and Bestial Discipline 2.",
  "0Mobalytics – Crix (BM Hunter Leveling 1-30, Verified) · 62 · Oct 28 · 26/0/0 (Talented included) · Deadly Aspects 5, Focused Fire 2, Improved Revive Pet (17), Pathfinding 2 (18–19) · Bestial Swiftness · Unleashed Fury 4 (21–24), Summon Hawk 25, Unleashed Fury 26, Ferocity 27–29, Intimidation 30. Talented: Ferocity 2, Bestial Discipline 2, Frenzy 1. Pathfinding (row 3) requires 10 points: at 18–19 you only have 8 (see open questions).",
  "0Zockify – Hunter Leveling (build 31/20/0 up to 60) · upd. Oct 25 · calculator link on client 70707 · Deadly Aspects, Focused Fire, Improved Revive Pet (17), Pathfinding (18–19) · Bestial Swiftness · Unleashed Fury 21–24 and 26, Summon Hawk 25, Improved Revive Pet 27, Ferocity 28–29, Intimidation 30. Then 31–33 Ferocity, 34 Improved Mend Pet, 35–39 Frenzy, 40 Bestial Wrath, 41–45 Lethal Attacks, 46–50 Careful Aim, 51–53 Hawk Eye, 54–55 Rapid Killing, 56 Trueshot Aura, 57–60 Mortal Shots.",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Sponge (Hunter Leveling) · Warcraft Tavern · Oct 2026 · solo build in images (not readable): using text and milestones · Beast Mastery \"the smoothest\"; Deadly Aspects, Focused Fire … · order not readable · Milestones: Summon Hawk 25, Intimidation 30, Bestial Discipline 30 (with Legacy), Bestial Wrath 40. With Talented: Intimidation and 1 Frenzy point.",
  "0wowforeverguides.com – Harenil and ForeverWisp · upd. Oct 19 and 20 · theory stated as \"untested\" · Endurance Training 5 first, Focused Fire 2, Pathfinding 2 · Bestial Swiftness / Unleashed Fury · Unleashed Fury 5, Ferocity 5, Summon Hawk (26 according to ForeverWisp), Intimidation 30. Without Deadly Aspects: weak source, discarded.",
  "3Recommended pets to tame, by level and zone",
  "0{Level} · {Pet (level · zone)} · {Why}",
  "010 (first Pet) · {Cat}: The Rake (10 · Mulgore, rare), Ghostfang (10 · Dun Morogh, rare), Feral Nightsaber (10–11 · Teldrassil) {Boar}: Scarred Crag Boar (9–10 · Dun Morogh), Longsnout (10–11 · Elwynn Forest), Corrupted Mottled Boar (10–11 · Durotar), Mountain Boar (10–11 · Loch Modan) {Fox} : Vuldren Alpha (10 · Zephras Isle) · Cat: damage and Bite/Claw (Warcraft Tavern, Mobalytics). Boar: sturdier, has {Charge} (Warcraft Tavern, Zockify). Fox: Trickster’s Dance (+50% Dodge), new family not yet evaluated.",
  "012–19 · {Cat}: Savannah Prowler (14–15 · The Barrens), Savannah Patriarch (15–16 · The Barrens), Moonstalker (14–15 · Darkshore), Moonstalker Sire (17–18 · Darkshore), Ghost Saber and Moonstalker Matriarch (19–20 · Darkshore) {Boar}: Goretusk (14–15 · Westfall), Elder Mountain Boar (16–17 · Loch Modan), Great Goretusk (16–17 · Redridge Mountains) {Bear} (Swipe on 3 targets): Grizzled Black Bear (13–14 · Loch Modan), Black Bear Patriarch (16–17 · Loch Modan), Grizzled Thistle Bear (16–17 · Darkshore) {Carrion Bird}: Greater Fleshripper (16–17 · Westfall) – Demoralizing Screech · Cat stays the damage choice. Bear (wow4evernews, topbuilds): better on multiple pulls. Bite 3 / Claw 3 require a level 16 Pet.",
  "020–30 · {Cat}: Starving Mountain Lion (23–24 · Hillsbrad Foothills) , Twilight Runner (23–24 · Stonetalon Mountains), Humar the Pridelord (23 · The Barrens, rare elite), Crag Stalker (25–26 · Thousand Needles), Feral Mountain Lion (27–28 · Hillsbrad Foothills), Needles Cougar (27–28 · Thousand Needles) {Boar}: Bellygrub (24 · Redridge Mountains) – Charge rank 3 {Bear}: Gray Bear (21–22 · Hillsbrad Foothills), Elder Ashenvale Bear (25–26 · Ashenvale) – Claw rank 4, Big Samras (27 · Hillsbrad Foothills, rare) {Wolf}: Black Ravager Mastiff (25–26 · Duskwood) – Bite 4 and Furious Howl 2, Ghostpaw Alpha (27–28 · Ashenvale) · From a level 24 Pet you learn Bite 4 / Claw 4 / Charge 3 / Furious Howl 2: tame them as temporary \"carriers\" and teach them to the main Pet. Wolf for groups and dungeons (Furious Howl).",
  "032–40 · Stranglethorn Tiger and Kurzen War Tiger (32–33 · Stranglethorn Vale) -> {Dash 1}; Mistvale Gorilla (32–33 · Stranglethorn Vale); Broken Tooth (37 · Badlands, rare Cat, attack speed 1 s); Longtooth Runner (40–41 · Feralas) -> Bite 6, Furious Howl 3, Dash 2 · Candidates from Petopia/LePrestore, not verified in client 60.",
  "0Data: Zockify Pet Finder (upd. Oct 20) for names, levels and zones; the Pets also exist on the Wowhead Forever map . Families: Cat and Boar (Warcraft Tavern), Cat (Mobalytics), Boar (Zockify). A range like \"14–15\" means the mob can be one of two levels: you need at least its level to tame it.",
  "3First Pet by race (class quest at level 10)",
  "0Class quest {Taming the Beast} (level 10): three tames with the Taming Rod, then {Training the Beast} for Beast Training, Feed Pet and Revive Pet. Before taming your real Pet, put the quest one in Stable. Trainer and last tame (wowforeverguides.com, Harenil , and ForeverWisp from Wowhead):",
  "0• Orc / Troll: Thotar (Razor Hill · Durotar) -> Armored Scorpid (first tame: Dire Mottled Boar)",
  "0• Tauren: Yaw Sharpmane (Bloodhoof Village · Mulgore) -> Swoop",
  "0• Dwarf: Grif Wildheart (Kharanos · Dun Morogh) -> Ice Claw Bear (first tame: Large Crag Boar)",
  "0• Night Elf: Dazalar (Dolanaar · Teldrassil) -> Strigid Screecher",
  "0• Human : Josephine Carson (Elwynn Forest) -> Young Forest Bear (first tame: Rockhide Boar)",
  "0• Skyborne : Quel’ana Quickgale (Valanaar · Zephras Isle) -> Vuldren Alpha (Fox)",
  "0Tame Beast fails on beasts above your level (Sep 24). While taming, your armor is 100%: use Aspect of the Monkey, Concussive Shot or a Freezing Trap (Warcraft Tavern). You can't tame with an active Pet, even if dismissed. Stable: 1 active Pet + 2 in Stable (Stable Master).",
  "3How to learn Pet abilities (Bite, Claw, Charge, Howl, Dash, Dive)",
  "0Pets learn {Bite}/{Claw}, {Charge}, {Furious Howl}, {Dash}/{Dive} only from wild beasts (LePrestore from Petopia, Oct 26–27). Procedure (Zockify, LePrestore): put your Pet in Stable, tame a beast that knows the rank (Beast Lore, from 24, shows the abilities), fight with it until \"You have learned a new spell\" appears, then summon your Pet back and teach the ability with Beast Training. You can skip intermediate ranks. Growl, Great Stamina and Natural Armor are instead bought from the Pet Trainer.",
  "0• {Bite 3 / Claw 3}: level 16 Pet. {Bite 4 / Claw 4 / Charge 3 / Furious Howl 2}: level 24 Pet.",
  "0• Bite 4: Giant Moss Creeper (24–25 · Hillsbrad Foothills), Black Ravager (24–25 · Duskwood), Leech Widow (24 · Wetlands).",
  "0• Claw 4: Elder Ashenvale Bear (25–26 · Ashenvale), Barbed Crustacean (25–26 · Blackfathom Deeps).",
  "0• Charge 3: Bellygrub (24 · Redridge Mountains), Agam'ar (24–25 · Razorfen Kraul).",
  "0• Furious Howl 2: Black Ravager Mastiff (25–26 · Duskwood), Ghostpaw Alpha (27–28 · Ashenvale).",
  "0• {Dive 1}: Kraul Bat (30–31 · Razorfen Kraul). {Dash 1}: Kurzen War Tiger or Stranglethorn Tiger (32–33 · Stranglethorn Vale), so not at 30. Dash 2: Longtooth Runner (Feralas) or Ridge Stalker Patriarch (Badlands), 40–41. Dash 3: Vilebranch Raiding Wolf (The Hinterlands), 50–51 (Zockify, LePrestore).",
  "0• Higher ranks: Bite/Claw 5 from Pet 32, 6 from 40, 7 from 48, 8 from 56 (carriers from Petopia: Plains Creeper, Scorpashi Lasher, Silt Crawler, Elder Shardtooth…).",
  "3Talent variants and other specs",
  "0{Marksmanship / Survival}: Warcraft Tavern says the Hunter can level with any spec but {Beast Mastery is the smoothest}. Marksmanship does more damage but makes you pull threat away from the Pet (constant kiting); Survival is melee and traps and is played \"harder\". Lone Wolf (MM, +20% damage without a Pet) is not recommended for leveling. On Mobalytics the only MM guide found is Robcat (6 , Oct 30).",
  "0{Detail variants}: (1) {Pathfinding 2 + Bestial Swiftness at 20} (Crix, Zockify) instead of the 2 Endurance Training: +6% Cheetah speed and faster Pet earlier, but the 10-point prerequisite isn't met until 20. (2) Spirit Bond 2 (1% Health every 10 s at rank 1, every 5 s at rank 2, for you and the Pet) instead of one Frenzy point reduces downtime. (3) With Legacy {Talented} (5 points) follow Method/Crix: Ferocity 5/5, Bestial Discipline 2/2, Frenzy 1.",
  "31–9 · Kiting without a Pet",
  "0^ability_hunter_aspectofthemonkey,ability_hunter_snipershot,ability_whirlwind,ability_hunter_quickshot,ability_impalingbolt,spell_frost_stun,ability_meleedamage^Aspect of the Monkey -> Hunter's Mark -> Auto Shot -> Serpent Sting -> Arcane Shot -> Concussive Shot -> Raptor Strike",
  "0Open from max distance: Auto Shot (standing still 0.5 s), Serpent Sting only if the mob lives long enough, Arcane Shot on cooldown. After each shot take a step back and resume; Concussive Shot from 8 to slow. If it reaches melee: Raptor Strike. One mob at a time (Warcraft Tavern, Zockify).",
  "310–19 · The Pet holds the mob",
  "0^ability_hunter_beastcall,ability_physical_taunt,spell_nature_ravenform,ability_hunter_snipershot,ability_whirlwind,ability_impalingbolt,ability_hunter_mendpet^Call Pet -> Pet: Growl -> Aspect of the Hawk -> Hunter's Mark -> Auto Shot -> Arcane Shot -> Mend Pet",
  "0Send the Pet in first and let it use Growl; then Hunter’s Mark, Auto Shot and Arcane Shot. Aspect of the Hawk always active in combat. From 18, Multi-Shot on 2+ mobs. Mend Pet when it drops. If the mob reaches you: Wing Clip (12) or Concussive Shot and resume at range (Method).",
  "320–24 · Aimed Shot and Freezing Trap",
  "0^ability_hunter_beastcall,ability_hunter_quickshot,inv_spear_07,ability_impalingbolt,spell_frost_chainsofice^Pet in front -> Serpent Sting -> Aimed Shot -> Arcane Shot -> Freezing Trap",
  "0Aimed Shot (2 s cast) on the single target; Multi-Shot if there are 2–3 mobs. Aimed Shot and Multi-Shot share 6 s: one per cycle; Arcane Shot has its own timer. Freezing Trap on the extra mob (10 s). Aspect of the Cheetah (20) to move, but switch back to Hawk before the pull.",
  "325–30 · Summon Hawk, 2 hawks always up",
  "0^ability_hunter_animalhandler,inv_spear_07,ability_impalingbolt,ability_hunter_runningshot^Summon Hawk -> Summon Hawk -> Aimed Shot -> Arcane Shot -> Rapid Fire",
  "0From 25, keep 2 hawks and the Pet on every mob that lives more than a few seconds (they last 18 s: don't recast before the last second). Summon Hawk shares 6 s with Arcane Shot: use Arcane Shot every third cast or on a nearly dead mob (Method). Rapid Fire (26) on difficult pulls, Intimidation (30) if the mob turns toward you, Feign Death (30) to reset.",
  "3AoE · multiple pulls",
  "0^spell_frost_freezingbreath,spell_frost_chainsofice,ability_upgrademoonglaive,ability_devour,ability_rogue_feigndeath^Frost Trap -> Freezing Trap -> Multi-Shot -> Intimidation -> Feign Death",
  "0Frost Trap (28) slows the group by 60%; Freezing Trap on one mob. Multi-Shot on 3 targets (costs a lot of Mana). If the Pet loses threat: Intimidation (30) or Distracting Shot; if the mob reaches you, Wing Clip and back off. Traps can be placed in combat (30 s cooldown, a Fire and an Ice together from Oct 15) but always at your feet: back up toward the trap.",
  "3Pet management and threat",
  "0• The Pet does most of the damage and holds threat: send it first, {Growl} on autocast (turn it off in dungeons if there's a tank).",
  "0• {Aspect of the Hawk} always in combat; {Cheetah} only while traveling (if they hit you, you're Dazed for 4 s).",
  "0• Happiness: Happy 125% damage, Content 100%, Unhappy 75%. Use Feed Pet out of combat with food from its diet (beta bug: only drops when the Pet dies).",
  "0• The Pet takes 25% of mob XP (green or higher mobs only) and stops at your level.",
  "0• Ranged abilities don't work within 8 yd of the enemy: keep the Pet in front.",
  "3Mana and downtime",
  "0• Mana is your resource (Pets use Focus). Aimed Shot, Multi-Shot and Summon Hawk cost a lot: don't spend it all, keep a reserve for Feign Death and traps (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• If it runs low: let the Pet and Auto Shot work, no mana-costing abilities until it regenerates; drink between pulls.",
  "0• Mana in combat depends on Spirit: {Bestial Discipline} (BM), Rapid Recuperation (MM) and Resourcefulness (Survival) help.",
  "0• Legacy: {Thrill of Adventure} gives some Health and Mana for each non-trivial kill (wowforeverguides).",
  "3Chain pull and Feign Death",
  "0The Hunter excels at chain pulling: you move to the next mob while the previous one dies to DoTs or traps, but watch out for live mobs wandering toward other packs (Warcraft Tavern). {Feign Death} (30) resets a bad pull: put the Pet on passive and call it back first, then stay down until the mobs wander off (Zockify). Before 30, use Scare Beast, Freezing Trap or Distracting Shot.",
  "0Priority (Warcraft Tavern): Agility > Attack Power > Critical Strike > Intellect > Stamina/Spirit > Strength > Armor. Before 10: Agility, AP, Intellect, Stamina/Spirit, Armor. Spirit matters for Mana in combat (Bestial Discipline). The ranged weapon is your first upgrade; then melee for stats. Ranged (Warcraft Tavern): Barbaric Crossbow (13–16, Ragefire Chasm), Calibrated Blunderbuss (13–16, quest Hall of Thanes, Alliance only), Venomstrike (19–22, Wailing Caverns), Naga Heartpiercer (22–29, Blackfathom Deeps), Fallenroot Longbow (23–29, Blackfathom Deeps), Quilboar Blaster (29–30, quest Razorfen Kraul), Master Hunter’s Bow (30, quest Big Game Hunter). Crafted and dungeon: Brawler’s Leather Hood, Dark Leather Boots, Stalker’s Leather Belt, Bloodied Chestwraps, Triprunner Dungarees. Mail from 40, Dual Wield from 20 ( client, wowforeverguides).",
  "0• Aimed Shot is base at level 20 (2 s cast, 6 s cooldown shared with Multi-Shot): Blizzard deep dive Sep 30, client.",
  "0• Summon Hawk, new BM talent (level 25 with all points in BM): max 2 hawks, 6 s cooldown shared with Arcane Shot; from Oct 15 the hawk appears on the target and stays there.",
  "0• New talents: Focused Fire, Careful Aim (20–100% Int -> AP), Lone Wolf, Rapid Killing; changed Deadly Aspects, Ferocity and Unleashed Fury (now also apply to Hawks). Intimidation requires Bestial Swiftness.",
  "0• Traps usable in combat (30 s cooldown), a Fire and an Ice together, and Fire trap scaling with AP (Oct 15).",
  "0• Pets: gain stats from the Hunter's equip (10% AP, 100% crit), each family has a unique ability, Bite or Claw and Dash or Dive, Fox is new; they inherit the highest crit and benefit from Expertise (Oct 15).",
  "0• Sep 24: Tame Beast doesn't work on beasts above your level; Furious Howl 40%. Oct 15: Dismember 25%/6 s, Sonic Blast +30% cast time/1 min cooldown, Mine! 3 s/90 s; Improved Mend Pet reduces Mana cost.",
  "0• Oct 15: Auto Shot requires 0.5 s standing still; new Auto Attack/Auto Shot option. Scorpid Sting now 2% hit; Aspect of the Beast gives melee AP; Disengage reduces threat twice as much.",
  "0• Humans and Skyborne (Alliance and Horde) can be Hunters. Oct 26–27: Orc Command +5% damage to Pets, Human Ruthless 1%, Skyborne Wind Blessed 2%.",
  "0• Dungeons: quest XP reduced by 50% from Oct 1; Excavation Site: Wetlands is new.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes and hotfix of 3 Nov): Arcane Shot and Serpent Sting get more Attack Power and deal more, Aspect of the Hawk is back to Classic values, Trueshot Aura gives up to 100 ranged attack power, Barrage and Lightning Reflexes as in Classic; all traps share one 30 sec cooldown.",
  "0{Raptor Strike} Lvl 1\nMelee strike: only needed when the mob reaches you. After 10 it loses almost all its value (Method).",
  "0{Auto Shot} Lvl 1\nYour main damage. From Oct 15 you have to stand still 0.5 s before shooting; it keeps going while you cast Aimed Shot.",
  "0{Track Beasts} Lvl 1\nShows beasts on the minimap: needed to find Pets to tame.",
  "0{Serpent Sting} Lvl 4\nNature DoT, no immediate damage: don't use it on mobs that die right away.",
  "0{Aspect of the Monkey} Lvl 4\n+8% Dodge: keeps you alive before 10, when you don't have a Pet yet.",
  "0{Arcane Shot} Lvl 6\nInstant Arcane shot, 6 s cooldown. From 25 it shares the cooldown with Summon Hawk.",
  "0{Hunter's Mark} Lvl 6\nIncreases Ranged Attack Power of whoever attacks the target: including the Pet (scales with your AP).",
  "0{Concussive Shot} Lvl 8\nRanged slow (12 s cooldown): your kiting tool before the Pet.",
  "0{Aspect of the Hawk} Lvl 10\n+Ranged Attack Power and the base of Deadly Aspects: always active in combat.",
  "0{Track Humanoids} Lvl 10\nHumanoid tracking.",
  "0{Tame Beast / Beast Training / Feed Pet / Revive Pet / Call Pet / Dismiss Pet} Lvl 10\nFrom the level 10 class quest (Taming the Beast + Training the Beast). You can't tame beasts above your level, or with an active Pet.",
  "0{Mend Pet} Lvl 12\nHeals the Pet in a channel (5 s): essential vs elites or groups.",
  "0{Wing Clip} Lvl 12\nMelee slow (40 Mana): if the mob gets on you.",
  "0{Distracting Shot} Lvl 12\nInstant ranged threat.",
  "0{Scare Beast} Lvl 14\nFear on a Beast (10 s): careful, the mob can run into other groups.",
  "0{Eyes of the Beast / Eagle Eye} Lvl 14\nExploration: control your Pet or zoom out from a distance; Eyes of the Beast lets you pull from far away.",
  "0{Immolation Trap} Lvl 16\nFire trap (DoT): usable in combat and scales with AP (Oct 15).",
  "0{Mongoose Bite} Lvl 16\nMelee strike: mainly useful for Survival.",
  "0{Multi-Shot} Lvl 18\nAoE on 3 targets; shares the cooldown (6 s) with Aimed Shot.",
  "0{Aimed Shot} Lvl 20\nBase for all Hunters (a talent in Classic Era): 2 s cast, 6 s cooldown shared with Multi-Shot. Your single-target shot.",
  "0{Freezing Trap} Lvl 20\n10 s CC on the first mob that passes (broken by damage); usable in combat. 30 s cooldown shared with Frost Trap.",
  "0{Aspect of the Cheetah} Lvl 20\n+30% speed out of combat: if you get hit you stay Dazed.",
  "0{Disengage} Lvl 20\nReduces threat on the target ( double from Oct 8).",
  "0{Scorpid Sting} Lvl 22\nChanged: 2% chance for it to hit you for 20 s (no longer reduces Strength and Agility).",
  "0{Track Hidden} Lvl 24\nDetects stealthed units on the minimap (Method: \"incredible\" for quests).",
  "0{Beast Lore} Lvl 24\nBeast information: useful to know what a Pet to tame will teach.",
  "0{Rapid Fire} Lvl 26\n5 min cooldown: +40% ranged and melee attack speed for 15 s. Use it on difficult pulls.",
  "0{Track Elementals} Lvl 26\nElemental tracking.",
  "0{Frost Trap} Lvl 28\nArea that slows by 60% for 30 s: essential for multiple pulls.",
  "0{Feign Death} Lvl 30\nLeaves combat (can miss): put the Pet on passive first.",
  "0{Aspect of the Beast} Lvl 30\nGives Melee Attack Power and makes you untrackable: for when the mob reaches you.",
  "0{Flare} Lvl 32\nReveals stealth and invisible within 10 yd. Track Demons at the same level (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0{Explosive Trap} Lvl 34\nFire AoE trap. Serpent Sting 5 and Disengage 2 at the same level.",
  "0{Viper Sting} Lvl 36\nDrains mana from the target. At the same level: Summon Hawk 2, Aimed Shot 3, Arcane Shot 5, Mend Pet 4.",
  "0{Aspect of the Pack} Lvl 40\n+30% speed to the whole group. Volley, Track Giants, Freezing Trap 2, Apprentice Riding and Dual Specialization at the same level.",
  "0{Aspect of the Wild} Lvl 46\nNature resistance to the group.",
  "0{Track Dragonkin} Lvl 50\nDragonkin tracking.",
  "0{Tranquilizing Shot} Lvl 60\nRemoves a Frenzy/Enrage effect from the enemy.",
  "0{Summon Hawk} Lvl 25\nBM talent (16th point): hawk that attacks for 18 s, max 2; 80 Mana, 6 s cooldown shared with Arcane Shot.",
  "0{Intimidation} Lvl 30\nBM talent: requires Bestial Swiftness; 3 s stun on the Pet's next attack, +100% crit on that hit.",
  "0{Bestial Wrath} Lvl 40\nBM talent (31st point): Pet +50% damage for 18 s, 2 min cooldown.",
  "0{Trueshot Aura} Lvl 56\nMM talent of the level 60 build: +RAP to party and raid within 45 yd.",
  "0{Human Hunter:} New combination. Ruthless +1% crit (was 2%, halved on Oct 26), The Human Spirit +10% Spirit (doubled), Will to Survive (removes stuns), Perception. Method recommends it, but its numbers predate the patch.",
  "3Other races for the Hunter",
  "0• {Dwarf} (Alliance): Big Game Hunter: +5% damage vs Beasts (many leveling mobs) ; Artisan’s Precision +1% Hit; Stoneform. Great, but no racial for the Pet.",
  "0• {Night Elf} (Alliance): Shadowmeld (stealth while standing still, useful for drinking), Elune’s Light (+10% crit for 15 s, Method), Quickness (+1% Dodge, +2% speed), Wisp Spirit. Method: among the best Alliance races.",
  "0• {Skyborne (High Order)} (Alliance): High Order (Alliance): Wind Blessed +2% Haste (was 3% before Oct 26), Walk on Air, Elemental Insight +5% vs Elementals, Read Ley Line (regenerates Health and Mana +50% for 15 s, 100% if Attuned to a Ley Line). They start at Zephras Isle (3–12) with the new Hunter quest and the Fox Vuldren Alpha.",
  "0• {Orc} (Horde): Command: Pets deal +5% damage (back on Oct 26, for BM); Blood Fury +10% AP for 15 s with 2 min cooldown; Hardiness (stun 20%); Shatter Curse. According to Method the best Horde race, but Savage has been removed.",
  "0• {Tauren} (Horde): War Stomp (2 s stun to escape), Endurance (5% Health), Plainsrunning (+2% speed every 5 s, max 60%), Cultivation (duplicates herbs). No offensive bonus.",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Beast Slaying +5% damage to Beasts (great for leveling) ; Berserking +10% haste for 10 s; Regeneration; Rapid Regeneration (channel, 50% Health). With the Orc, it's the most sensible choice for a Horde Hunter.",
  "0• {Skyborne Windshaper} (Horde): Windshaper (Horde): same Wind Blessed, Walk on Air and Elemental Insight; instead of Read Ley Line they have Skysight (+15% speed for 15 s, 30% with Charged to an elemental convergence). They start at Zephras Isle with the same Hunter quest.",
  "0Skinning (hides sell) plus Herbalism or Mining for materials; Fishing and Cooking for food and XP buff; Engineering if you want to make Scopes for your weapon (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0Leatherworking + Skinning (Method, Warcraft Tavern): from 10 you can make BoP equip with lots of Agility (Brawler’s Leather Helm (\"BiS in beta\" according to Method), Dark Leather Boots, Stalker’s Leather Belt). Cooking for the food XP bonus, First Aid to heal yourself and for Poison, Disease and Bleed, which the Hunter doesn't remove.",
  "2Advice for the Hunter",
  "0Take Leatherworking + Skinning and keep Cooking, First Aid and Fishing. The Pet keeps the mob busy while you skin: no extra downtime. Aspect of the Cheetah speeds up gathering.\nSkinning + Leatherworking in leveling (leather always ready). Endgame Engineering + Mining (Gfinity: 'peak synergy with Hunters'). Sources .",
  "2Priorities for the Hunter",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP (5% of a level, once an hour, only if you don't already have Rested). The most useful for leveling; with Skinning, it's the pairing recommended by Method and Warcraft Tavern.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing priority 2\n+8% to all primary stats (like Blessing of Kings): \"universal\" according to Warcraft Tavern; Fishing pairs with Cooking.",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning priority 3\n+2% crit (like Leader of the Pack). Warcraft Tavern: \"great for Hunters\"; Skinning goes with Leatherworking.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nLike Mark of the Wild (doesn't stack with a Druid): primary stats, armor and resist. The buffs also apply to the Pet if you summon it while sitting at camp (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy\nMana/5 (like Blessing of Wisdom): Aimed Shot, Multi-Shot and Summon Hawk use a lot of Mana.",
  "0{Reagent Bot} · Engineering\nSells food, water and materials in the field: fewer trips to the vendor (Warcraft Tavern). Gives no buff.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nStamina (like Power Word: Fortitude), for you and your Pet; you learn First Aid anyway.",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism\nIntellect (like Arcane Intellect): more Mana and, from 46 with Careful Aim, AP too.",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring\nSpirit (like Divine Spirit): helps Mana in combat with Bestial Discipline.",
  "0{Lodestone} · Mining\nMelee Attack Power (like Blessing of Might): for Survival; for a ranged BM it's worth little.",
  "0{Sharpening Wheel} · Blacksmithing\nStrength: minimal priority for a Hunter.",
