  "0wowforever.be (client) · client data 70707 (up to 35) · IFB 5 · Precision 2 · Frostbite 3 · Ice Lance · Ice Shards 4 · Shatter 3 · Ice Block · Ice Shards 5 · FoF",
  "0{This guide} (= Mobalytics – Asuna_qt) · 112 , “Verified”, upd. Nov 4 · IFB 5 · Precision 3 · Frostbite 2 · Ice Lance · Ice Shards 4 · Ice Block · Shatter 3 · Ice Shards 5 · FoF",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Nevermore · “the strongest Frost build at 30” · Pure Frost with Ice Lance + Fingers of Frost · (exact talent points only in image)",
  "0Icy Veins – Teloril · updated Oct 30 · Arcane: Wand Spec 2 · Imp. Channeling 3 · Missile Barrage 2 · Precision 3 · IFB · Ice Lance only at {27}, Fingers of Frost at {37}",
  "3Icy Veins' “mana-efficient” alternative: when it makes sense",
  "0Icy Veins starts in the Arcane talent tree with {Wand Specialization} (+25% Wand damage) and {Missile Barrage} (20% chance for Frostbolt to make the next Arcane Missiles free). You drink less, but Ice Lance arrives at 27 instead of 20 and Fingers of Frost at 37 instead of 30.",
  "0For a 1–30 run, the pure Frost build is stronger early on and the most voted. Consider the alternative only if you often run out of mana and use the Wand a lot.",
  "31–9 · Before talents",
  "0^spell_frost_frostbolt02,inv_wand_01^Frostbolt -> Wand (Shoot)",
  "0Open from max distance with Frostbolt (Fireball before 4), finish with the Wand (Shoot). Fire Blast if you're moving.",
  "310–19 · Kiting",
  "0^spell_frost_frostbolt02,spell_frost_frostnova^Frostbolt -> Frost Nova -> Frostbolt",
  "0If the mob reaches you: Frost Nova, take a few steps back, resume with Frostbolt. Each Frostbite is free time for Wand or Frostbolt.",
  "320+ · Frostbite triggers at range",
  "0^spell_frost_frostbolt02,spell_frost_frostblast^Frostbolt -> + Ice Lance",
  "0Cast Frostbolt and queue Ice Lance right after: they arrive together on the Frozen target. If Ice Lance is on cooldown, use Cone of Cold (from 26).",
  "320+ · The mob is in melee",
  "0^spell_frost_frostnova,spell_arcane_blink,spell_frost_frostbolt02,spell_frost_frostblast^Frost Nova -> Step back -> Frostbolt -> + Ice Lance",
  "0Only one Ice Lance per Nova (8 s cooldown). Then Frostbolt while it's Frozen, and start over.",
  "330 · Fingers of Frost",
  "0^ability_mage_wintersgrasp,spell_frost_frostblast^Proc -> Ice Lance",
  "0With 1 talent point you have 1 charge: spend it on Ice Lance. If Ice Lance is on cooldown, Frostbolt + Ice Lance as soon as it's back. With 2 talent points (31): Frostbolt on the first charge, Frostbolt + Ice Lance on the second (Icy Veins).",
  "3AoE · 3+ mob",
  "0^spell_frost_frostnova,spell_fire_selfdestruct,spell_nature_wispsplode,spell_frost_glacier^Frost Nova -> Flamestrike -> Arcane Expl. -> Cone of Cold",
  "0Solo: Nova, then close-range AoE. Blizzard only if you're safe (in a group). Costs a lot of mana: drink afterwards.",
  "3Pre-launch news : Ice Lance with cooldown",
  "0Ice Lance now has an {8 second cooldown} (client 70707, Wowhead, change noted by Icy Veins on Oct 30). You can no longer spam it during Frost Nova: {one} Ice Lance per Freeze, well placed. Damage on Frozen targets: +300% according to the client (Icy Veins says +200%: the tooltip is the authority).",
  "3What is “spell batching” and why it matters",
  "0As in Classic, the server processes actions in small intervals. If you press Ice Lance right after a Frostbolt starts, the two hits arrive together: both find the target still Frozen and benefit from Shatter. Freeze breaks on damage, even your own. Ice Lance “snapshots” the Frozen state at the moment of the cast (Icy Veins).",
  "3Mana: the rules that save the most time",
  "0• {5-second rule:} mana only regenerates after 5 s without spending any. Finish mobs with the Wand.",
  "0• Don't waste a high-Rank Frostbolt on a nearly dead mob: use Fire Blast or Wand.",
  "0• On login, spend mana on Conjure Food, Conjure Water and Mana Gem (from 28).",
  "0• Get a Wand as soon as possible: Lesser Magic Wand (lvl 5) and Greater Magic Wand (lvl 13), from Enchanting or the Auction House. Enchanters make them to level up their skill: they cost little.",
  "0Intellect and Spirit for mana, Stamina to survive; Frost spell damage when it arrives. The weapon matters: Wand (Shoot) and Staff.",
  "0• Ice Lance talent at 20: 8 s cooldown, +300% on Frozen targets (client 70707, Oct 30).",
  "0• Fingers of Frost at 30 (talent).",
  "0• Elemental Precision -> Precision, 3 ranks of 2% (Oct 16 hotfix, KamiLabs/Venruki); Piercing Ice removed.",
  "0• Frost Blast at 24: fast Chill.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): Ignite also triggers from Flamestrike's ticks, Missile Barrage is spent when Arcane Missiles starts and Arcane Missiles can give Clearcasting again; a rank learned more than 12 levels below yours has a lower chance to trigger Arcane Concentration, Frostbite and Fingers of Frost.",
  "0{Frost Armor} Lvl 1\nAlways active: applies Chill to whoever hits you in melee and can trigger Frostbite.",
  "0{Arcane Intellect} Lvl 1\nAlways active.",
  "0{Fireball} Lvl 1\nYour attack until 4.",
  "0{Frostbolt} Lvl 4\nThe filler: damage + Chill (slow).",
  "0{Conjure Water} Lvl 4\nFree water.",
  "0{Fire Blast} Lvl 6\nInstant: to finish or while moving.",
  "0{Conjure Food} Lvl 6\nFree food.",
  "0{Polymorph} Lvl 8\nTakes the second mob out of combat.",
  "0{Arcane Missiles} Lvl 8\nUseful only with Missile Barrage (Icy Veins build).",
  "0{Frost Nova} Lvl 10\nFreeze (root) on whoever is near you. Rank 1 lasts the same and costs less.",
  "0{Arcane Explosion} Lvl 14\nAoE around you.",
  "0{Flamestrike} Lvl 16\nGround AoE; open group pulls.",
  "0{Blizzard} Lvl 20\nChanneled AoE when you're safe.",
  "0{Blink} Lvl 20\nEscape, breaks roots and stuns; +20% speed if used while running.",
  "0{Evocation} Lvl 20\nRestores most of your mana in 8 s.",
  "0{Teleport (faction capitals)} Lvl 20\nBack to the Trainer in an instant.",
  "0{Counterspell} Lvl 24\nInterrupts casters (especially healers).",
  "0{Frost Blast} Lvl 24\nFast Chill (1.5 s cast, 40% slow for 9 s): replaces Frostbolt Rank 1.",
  "0{Cone of Cold} Lvl 26\nInstant AoE with Chill: your “backup Nova”.",
  "0{Conjure Mana Agate} Lvl 28\nMana Gem for long pulls.",
  "0{Ice Armor} Lvl 30\nReplaces Frost Armor.",
  "0{Teleport (third capital)} Lvl 30\nAn extra Teleport.",
  "0{Ice Lance (talent)} Lvl 20\n8 s cooldown, +300% on Frozen targets.",
  "0{Ice Block (talent)} Lvl 25\nImmune 10 s, cooldown 5 min.",
  "0{Human Mage:} Extra Spirit (The Human Spirit) to regenerate mana.",
  "3Other races for the Mage",
  "0• {Gnome} (Alliance): Expansive Mind (+Intellect) and Escape Artist to free yourself from roots.",
  "0• {Skyborne (High Order)} (Alliance): Skyborne racial: Haste and mana regen (High Order) .",
  "0• {Orc} (Horde): Blood Fury for burst; stun resistance.",
  "0• {Undead} (Horde): Will of the Forsaken against Fear/Charm; Cannibalize reduces downtime.",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Berserking for burst; faster Health regeneration.",
  "0Mining + Herbalism (or Skinning).",
  "0{Tailoring + Enchanting} (Icy Veins, Method, Mobalytics): rare BoP equip you sew yourself from 10 (Novice Arcanist’s Sash), Wands you make yourself, bags to sell. It costs gold rather than earning it.",
  "2Advice for the Mage",
  "0Main on gathering professions; {bank alt Tailoring + Enchanting} that receives cloth and green BoE. On everyone: Cooking, First Aid (the mage doesn't heal), Fishing.\nTailoring + Enchanting in leveling. Dungeons and speedrunning: Engineering + Mining with grenades (Gfinity). Sources .",
  "2Mage perks",
  "0• {Lvl 20:} Teleport to two capitals of your faction (Icy Veins, Method).",
  "0• {Lvl 30:} Teleport to the third capital.",
  "0• {Lvl 40:} Teleport Dalaran and Portal.",
  "0• Icy Veins tip: {don't} set your Hearthstone in a capital where you can teleport; set it in the zone where you do quests.",
  "0• Blink used as soon as it's ready while running +20% travel speed.",
  "2Priorities for the Mage",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP up to 5% of a level, once an hour. {The most useful for leveling.}",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy priority 2\nUp to 29 mana/5 s: fewer breaks to drink.",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism priority 3\nUp to +25 Intellect (does not stack with Arcane Intellect).",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring\nUp to +32 Spirit.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing\n+8% to all stats.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nUp to +56 Stamina.",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning\n+2% crit.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nArmor, stats, resistance.",
