  "Summon Charger (Alliance: Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, Grimand Elmore; Horde: Summon Forsaken Charger).",
  "Deflection:Retribution;Deflection:Retribution;Deflection:Retribution;Deflection:Retribution;Deflection:Retribution;Conviction:Retribution;Conviction:Retribution;Conviction:Retribution;Improved Judgement:Retribution;Improved Judgement:Retribution;Pursuit of Justice:Retribution;Pursuit of Justice:Retribution;Seal of Command:Retribution;Sanctified Judgement:Retribution;Sanctified Judgement:Retribution;Two-Handed Weapon Specialization:Retribution;Two-Handed Weapon Specialization:Retribution;Two-Handed Weapon Specialization:Retribution;Sacred Arbiter:Retribution;Sanctified Judgement:Retribution;Vengeance:Retribution;Vengeance:Retribution;Vengeance:Retribution;Repentance:Retribution;Benediction:Retribution;Champion of the Light:Retribution;Champion of the Light:Retribution;Champion of the Light:Retribution;Champion of the Light:Retribution;Champion of the Light:Retribution;Unsealed Wrath:Retribution;Divine Strength:Holy;Divine Strength:Holy;Divine Strength:Holy;Divine Strength:Holy;Divine Strength:Holy;Reverence:Holy;Reverence:Holy;Improved Seals:Holy;Improved Seals:Holy;Improved Seals:Holy;Improved Seals:Holy;Improved Seals:Holy;Divine Intellect:Protection;Divine Intellect:Protection;Divine Intellect:Protection;Divine Intellect:Protection;Divine Intellect:Protection;Precision:Protection;Precision:Protection;Precision:Protection",
  "1Talents: Retribution 1–60",
  "0{Choice:} Retribution with a slow Two-Handed: it's the consensus for solo leveling. The talent order is that of the most voted Paladin guide, {Mobalytics yumytv (102 , upd. Nov 1)}: Deflection 10–14, Conviction, Improved Judgement, Pursuit of Justice and Seal of Command at 22, then Sanctified Judgement and Two-Handed Weapon Specialization; final split 12 Holy / 8 Protection / 31 Retribution, same as Zockify. Maxroll, Conquest Capped and Icy Veins also agree on the spec. wowforever.be (client data) instead opens in Holy: you'll find it as build B.",
  "0{Deflection} 5/5 · lvl 10–14",
  "0{Conviction} 3/3 · lvl 15–17",
  "0{Improved Judgement} 2/2 · lvl 18–19",
  "0{Pursuit of Justice} 2/2 · lvl 20–21",
  "0{Seal of Command} 1/1 · lvl 22",
  "0{Sanctified Judgement} 2/3 · lvl 23–24",
  "0{Two-Handed Weapon Specialization} 3/3 · lvl 25–27",
  "0{Sacred Arbiter} 1/1 · lvl 28",
  "0{Sanctified Judgement} 3/3 · lvl 29",
  "0{Vengeance} 3/3 · lvl 30–32",
  "0{Repentance} 1/1 · lvl 33",
  "0{Benediction} 1/5 · lvl 34",
  "0{Champion of the Light} 5/5 · lvl 35–39",
  "0{Unsealed Wrath} 1/1 · lvl 40",
  "0{Divine Strength} 5/5 · lvl 41–45",
  "0{Reverence} 2/2 · lvl 46–47",
  "0{Improved Seals} 5/5 · lvl 48–52",
  "0{Divine Intellect} 5/5 · lvl 53–57",
  "0{Precision} 3/3 · lvl 58–60",
  "0{This guide} = Mobalytics – yumytv · 102 · upd. Nov 1 · Deflection 5 · Conviction 3 · Improved Judgement 2 · Pursuit of Justice 2 · Seal of Command (22) · Sanctified Judgement 3 · Two-Handed Weapon Spec 3 · Sacred Arbiter · Vengeance",
  "0Mobalytics – yumytv (Paladin Leveling Guide 1-60) · 102 (the most saved Paladin guide) / upd. Nov 1 / 12/8/31 · Order not readable (split 12 Holy / 8 Prot / 31 Ret only). Rotation: Retribution Aura + Blessing of Might, Seal of Righteousness, Judgement + Holy Strike on cooldown · not found · not found",
  "0wowforeverbuilds – Ret 10–60 (Sep 15) · upd. Oct 24, beta 70532, 'theorycraft' · Benediction 5 (10–14) -> Improved Judgement 2 -> Conviction 3 (17–19) · Seal of Command · Conviction 4–5 (now impossible), Sanctified Judgement 3, Eye for an Eye 2, Pursuit of Justice 2, Vengeance at 30; Two-Handed Spec 33–35, Repentance 36, Twist of Light 40",
  "0wowforeverbuilds – Ret 10–60 (Sep 19, 'played in beta') · upd. Oct 24, 70532 · Benediction 5 (10–14) -> Conviction 5 (15–19) · Seal of Command · Sanctified Judgement 3, Vindication 3, Pursuit of Justice 1, Sacred Arbiter (28 in table, 30 in text), Pursuit 2, Two-Handed Spec from 30",
  "0wowforeverguides – Harenil · upd. Oct 21 · Benediction 5 (10–14) -> Conviction 5 (15–19) · Sanctified Judgement 3 + Seal of Command + Pursuit of Justice 1 · Sacred Arbiter, Holy Conduit 2, Improved Judgement 2, Two-Handed Spec 3 (30–32), Vengeance",
  "0Leprestore – Graham Smith · upd. Oct 21, 16/0/35 · Benediction 5 (10–14) -> Conviction 5 (15–19) · Seal of Command · Sanctified Judgement 3, Pursuit of Justice 2 (24–25), Sacred Arbiter (26), Vindication 3 (27–29), Vengeance 3 (30–32), Two-Handed Spec 3 (33–35)",
  "0Zockify · upd. Oct 30, 12/8/31 · Ret first: Benediction (full), Pursuit of Justice, Seal of Command, Sanctified Judgement, Sacred Arbiter, Champion of the Light, Unsealed Wrath; then Divine Strength, Improved Seals, Divine Intellect, Toughness, Precision (order by level not given) · Seal of Command · not found",
  "0Method – Jurdi · upd. Oct 10 · Holy: Divine Strength -> Improved Seals · Retribution: Holy Conduit, Pursuit of Justice (no Seal of Command) · Build for 10–30 (35 with Talented); then respec for role",
  "0wowforever.be (client data 70707) · client, Nov 1, known up to 35 · Divine Strength 5 (10–14) -> Improved Seals 3 (15–17) -> Benediction (18–) · Benediction 3/5 (no Seal of Command) · Benediction 5, Improved Judgement 2, Conviction 3, Pursuit of Justice 2 (28–29), Sanctified Judgement 3 (30–32), then Unyielding Faith 2 and Sacred Arbiter 35",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Passion · no date; beta build of 26 points · Retribution for the first 20–30 levels, also for 1H+shield · Seal of Command before the pull (Righteousness if 1H or high spell power) · Mana efficiency + Consecration; you can skip a point for Repentance",
  "0Icy Veins – Ret leveling (snippet only) · Oct 30 · Benediction (Deflection if you want less damage taken); Conviction instead of Holy Conduit at 18–19 · Benediction + Holy Conduit for cheaper Consecration · Pursuit of Justice early (travel talent up to 60)",
  "3wowforever.be alternative (Holy first, client 70707)",
  "0The wowforever.be order, the only one verified on the post-hotfix client, but {without Seal of Command} until 35:",
  "0• 10–14 {Divine Strength} 5/5 · 15–17 {Improved Seals} 3/5",
  "0• 18–22 {Benediction} 5/5 · 23–24 Improved Judgement · 25–27 Conviction 3/3",
  "0• 28–29 Pursuit of Justice · 30–32 Sanctified Judgement · 33–34 Unyielding Faith · 35 Sacred Arbiter",
  "0It works fine with Seal of Righteousness (scales with spell power) and with a 1H. With a slow Two-Handed, the consensus prefers Seal of Command at 20.",
  "3Protection / Shockadin alternative",
  "0{Protection} (dungeons and multi-mob pulls, 0/33/18 Zockify): Shield Specialization, Templar's Bulwark, Holy Shield, Reckoning. Maxroll advises against it for solo leveling. {Shockadin} (21 Holy with Holy Shock and Champion of the Light): Warcraft Tavern talks about surprising damage, but as a healer it's not recommended. Retribution remains the fastest spec solo (Maxroll, Mobalytics, Conquest Capped).",
  "3Legacy: Talented",
  "0The Legacy {Talented} brings points forward by 5 levels (from 5): at 30 you already have the 35 build. First recommended Legacy: Thrill of Adventure (Zockify, Conquest Capped); Talented for alts. The total stays at 51 points.",
  "31–9 · Seal, Judgement and Holy Strike",
  "0^spell_holy_fistofjustice,ability_thunderbolt,spell_holy_righteousfury,classicon_paladin,spell_holy_holybolt^Blessing of Might -> Seal of Righteousness -> Judgement -> Holy Strike (from 6) -> Holy Light after the kill",
  "0Before the pull: Blessing of Might (4) and Seal of Righteousness. While running toward the mob, cast Judgement (from 4), then hit; Holy Strike on cooldown from 6. Hammer of Justice from 8 on casters. After the kill, Holy Light if health is below 60%.",
  "310–19 · Mana first",
  "0^spell_holy_auraoflight,ability_thunderbolt,spell_holy_righteousfury,classicon_paladin,spell_holy_sealofmight^Retribution Aura (16) -> Seal of Righteousness -> Judgement -> Holy Strike -> Hammer of Justice",
  "0With Benediction, mana lasts longer. Order: Seal -> Judgement -> Holy Strike on cooldown, auto-attack in between. Retribution Aura from 16. Lay on Hands (10) and Divine Protection (6) are the emergencies; Redemption (12) for companions. Solo, leave Righteous Fury off: it's only threat.",
  "322–30 · Seal of Command and Consecration",
  "0^spell_holy_holysmite,spell_holy_righteousfury,ability_warrior_innerrage,classicon_paladin,spell_holy_innerfire^Seal of the Crusader (tough mobs) -> Judgement -> Seal of Command -> Holy Strike -> Consecration (2+ mobs)",
  "0With a slow Two-Handed (3.3 s or more per Mobalytics and Maxroll): on tough mobs open with Seal of the Crusader -> Judgement -> Seal of Command; on easy mobs only Seal of Command. Judgement and Holy Strike on cooldown, even in a macro. With Sacred Arbiter (26), Holy Strike also refreshes Judgements. Exorcism only on Undead and Demons. With a fast Two-Handed, a 1H or lots of spell power, stay on Seal of Righteousness (Warcraft Tavern, Maxroll).",
  "0^spell_holy_prayerofhealing,spell_holy_innerfire,classicon_paladin,spell_holy_sealofmight^Repentance (1 Humanoid) -> Consecration -> Holy Strike -> Hammer of Justice",
  "0Two mobs: Repentance on a Humanoid (talent, 36) or Hammer of Justice and kill one mob at a time. Three or more: Consecration in the center (the first 4 enemies take more damage), then Holy Strike and Judgement. Consecration costs a lot of mana (coefficient lowered from 0.095 to 0.042 on Oct 15): use it only when needed; Holy Conduit removes 40% of the cost. From 40, Hammer of the Righteous hits up to 4 targets.",
  "0^spell_holy_sealofwisdom,spell_holy_righteousnessaura,spell_holy_healingaura^Blessing of Wisdom -> Seal of Wisdom (38) -> Seal of Light (30)",
  "0Sanctified Judgement returns 60% of the Seal's cost on each Judgement; Benediction 10% on instants. Solo, use Blessing of Kings (base at 20) and leave the rest to Camp (Mana Well, Lodestone). Only heal if mana is above 50% (wowforeverbuilds). From 38, judge a mob with Seal of Wisdom to recover mana.",
  "3Combat tips",
  "0• Judgement {no longer consumes the Seal} : the Seal stays active for 30 s; renew it only when it expires.",
  "0• Holy Strike and Judgement in a macro: fewer clicks, less dead time (Mobalytics, wowforeverbuilds).",
  "0• Hammer of Justice is the only control: the Paladin {has no interrupt or slow} (Blizzard).",
  "0• Emergency: Divine Protection (6) or Divine Shield (34) + two Holy Lights can turn a bad pull around (Conquest Capped); Lay on Hands as a last resort.",
  "0• From 40 with Unsealed Wrath: switch Seal right after a Judgement, the old Seal also applies to the next hit. Costs mana: only if you have some.",
  "0• Best zones: Undead and Demons (Exorcism, Holy Wrath, Turn Undead).",
  "3Blessing and Aura solo",
  "0Blessing of Might and Retribution Aura for damage (yumytv on Mobalytics). Blessing of Kings is base from 20. Camp Lodestone replaces Might and Mana Well replaces Wisdom (Maxroll): in that case cast Kings on yourself.",
  "0Weapon damage first (Mobalytics and Maxroll: wide damage range and slow weapon, 3.3 speed or more); then Strength and Hit (Precision gives +3%); Stamina and Intellect to survive and for mana (Intellect matters more from 43 with Champion of the Light). Mail up to 40, Plate after. Weapon (slow 2H with the most DPS): Northshire Hammer (Q7), Ironforge Greathammer (Hall of Thanes, 13), Rhahk'Zor's Hammer (Deadmines, 16–22), Smite's Mighty Hammer (Deadmines, 18), Verigan's Fist / Wolfsbane (class quest 20), Scepter of the Abandoned (Ruins of Lordaeron, 17–25), The Stitcher (Horde, 20–25), Corpsemaker (Razorfen Kraul, 29), Ravager (Scarlet Monastery, 37; classicwowforever lists Bonebiter), Abandoned Ferocity / Scavenged Magram Armament (Desolace, Q42), Diabolic Skiver (Zul'Farrak, 44), Princess Theradras' Scepter (Maraudon, 49), Thorium Poleaxe (BS 260, 52), Legionite Glaive (BS 300, 58). Sources: Zockify, Maxroll, classicwowforever, Conquest Capped.",
  "0• Holy Strike (6, 10 s cooldown), Seal of Fury (10), Hammer of the Righteous (40) and Revoke (26) are new; Righteous Fury drops from 16 to 10 (client, Bind on Forever).",
  "0• Judgement no longer consumes the Seal (Blizzard deep dive, Sep 30; Method, Oct 10).",
  "0• Blessing of Kings and Consecration are base at 20; Consecration hits the first 4 enemies harder (coefficient 0.095 -> 0.042, Oct 15).",
  "0• Oct 31 hotfix (216 changes, Playfulls datamining): Twist of Light renamed Unsealed Wrath (requires Repentance); Conviction 3 ranks, 6% crit on everything; Champion of the Light 5 ranks; Holy Conduit in the Holy tree; Divine Intellect in the Protection tree; Improved Seals 5 ranks; Instrument of Law removed; Turn Evil new.",
  "0• Benediction now 10% on all instants (was 15% on Seal and Judgement only); Sacred Arbiter +20% (beta, Sep 24).",
  "0• Salvation is no longer a Blessing (Oct 15); Blessing of Light, Salvation and Revoke haven't responded on Wowhead since Oct 31 .",
  "0• Lay on Hands 20 min (was 1 hour); Resistance Aura on the whole raid; no baseline seal twisting.",
  "0• Vindication no longer raises your AP (Oct 31). Retribution Aura bug fix Oct 8. Human Ruthless and Dwarf Earth Fury Oct 15. Two-Handed Weapon Specialization: Sep 24 at 2/4/6%, now 6% physical and 20% threat.",
  "0• Blizzard Oct 8: dungeon XP will be close to quest XP but won't return to Classic levels; Legacy Talented gives talents from 5.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): Vengeance stacks up to 5 times (15% at rank 3 instead of 9%), Two-Handed Weapon Specialization raises Holy damage too (up to 6%), Templar's Bulwark's shield is now a Magic effect that can be dispelled.",
  "0{Seal of Righteousness} Lvl 1\nBase Seal: extra Holy damage on every hit, stronger with slow weapons and spell power.",
  "0{Holy Light} Lvl 1\nYour main heal between pulls.",
  "0{Devotion Aura} Lvl 1\n+Armor for you and the group.",
  "0{Blessing of Might} Lvl 4\n+Attack Power for 1 hour: always active.",
  "0{Judgement} Lvl 4\nReleases the Seal's effect without consuming it (10 s cooldown, 6% mana). Use it on cooldown.",
  "0{Holy Strike} Lvl 6\nNew: instant hit with weapon damage + Holy, 10 s cooldown, 5 Mana. Your second on-cooldown button.",
  "0{Divine Protection} Lvl 6\nImmune to physical damage and spells for 6 s (you can't attack). Applies Forbearance.",
  "0{Seal of the Crusader} Lvl 6\nOpening Seal: +AP and faster attacks; its Judgement increases Holy damage on the mob.",
  "0{Hammer of Justice} Lvl 8\n3 s stun: stops casters and fleeing mobs.",
  "0{Purify} Lvl 8\nRemoves diseases and Poison.",
  "0{Lay on Hands} Lvl 10\nHeals for your max health, drains your mana to zero. 20 min cooldown (was 1 hour).",
  "0{Blessing of Protection} Lvl 10\nImmune to physical damage for 6 s (Forbearance).",
  "0{Righteous Fury} Lvl 10\nNow at 10 (was 16): only needed for tanking; solo, keep it off.",
  "0{Seal of Fury} Lvl 10\nNew tank Seal: fixed Holy per hit and shield absorb; Judgement taunts. Not needed for Retribution.",
  "0{Redemption} Lvl 12\nResurrection. Unlocked via the class quest (Tome of Divinity / A Lesson in Divinity).",
  "0{Blessing of Wisdom} Lvl 14\nMana every 5 s.",
  "0{Retribution Aura} Lvl 16\nHoly damage to whoever hits you, scales with spell power: the leveling aura.",
  "0{Blessing of Freedom} Lvl 18\nImmune to root and slow for 10 s.",
  "0{Blessing of Kings} Lvl 20\nNow base (was a Protection talent): +10% to all stats for 1 hour.",
  "0{Consecration} Lvl 20\nNow base (was a Holy talent): deals more damage to the first 4 enemies that enter. Costs a lot of mana.",
  "0{Exorcism} Lvl 20\nInstant Holy damage vs Undead and Demons.",
  "0{Flash of Light} Lvl 20\nFast heal (1.5 s).",
  "0{Concentration Aura} Lvl 22\nLess pushback when healing.",
  "0{Seal of Justice} Lvl 22\nChance-based stun; Judgement prevents escape.",
  "0{Turn Undead} Lvl 24\nFear on Undead (with Turn Evil also on Demons).",
  "0{Salvation} Lvl 26\nNo longer a Blessing (Oct 15, Blizzard); the Wowhead tooltip hasn't responded since Oct 31.",
  "0{Revoke} Lvl 26\nRemoves Salvation from allies; Wowhead tooltip not responding.",
  "0{Shadow Resistance Aura} Lvl 28\nShadow resistance for the group.",
  "0{Divine Intervention} Lvl 30\nYou sacrifice yourself to save an ally; requires Symbol of Divinity.",
  "0{Seal of Light} Lvl 30\nSeal with a chance-based heal.",
  "0{Frost Resistance Aura} Lvl 32\nResist Frost.",
  "0{Divine Shield} Lvl 34\nImmune to everything for 10 s, damage 50%, Forbearance. Life saver.",
  "0{Fire Resistance Aura} Lvl 36\nResist Fire.",
  "0{Seal of Wisdom} Lvl 38\nMana Seal: judge a mob to recover mana.",
  "0{Hammer of the Righteous} Lvl 40\nNew: hits the target and up to 3 nearby enemies.",
  "0{Blessing of Light} Lvl 40\nLevel from Bind on Forever and Tavern; Wowhead tooltip not responding.",
  "0{Cleanse} Lvl 42\nRemoves Poison, diseases and Magic.",
  "0{Hammer of Wrath} Lvl 44\nFinisher below 20% health.",
  "0{Blessing of Sacrifice} Lvl 46\nTransfers damage from an ally to you.",
  "0{Holy Wrath} Lvl 50\nAoE on Undead and Demons with stun.",
  "0{Greater Blessing of Might} Lvl 52\nGroup version; requires the Symbol of Kings reagent.",
  "0{Greater Blessing of Wisdom} Lvl 54\nSame.",
  "0{Greater Blessing of Kings} Lvl 60\nSame.",
  "0{Mass Salvation} Lvl 60\nRaid version of Salvation.",
  "0{Greater Blessing of Light} Lvl 60\nGroup version of Blessing of Light.",
  "0{Seal of Command} Lvl 22\nSeal talent: 65 Mana, 70% extra weapon damage as Holy. Its Judgement deals 69–73 Holy (138–146 if the target is stunned).",
  "0{Sacred Arbiter} Lvl 28\nPassive: Holy Strike +20% damage and refreshes all Judgements on the target.",
  "0{Repentance} Lvl 33\nIncapacitates a Humanoid for 6 s, 60 Mana, 1 min cooldown.",
  "0{Unsealed Wrath} Lvl 40\nMelee hits keep a copy of the active Seal for 15 s (up to 3 stacks): Forever's seal twisting. Until Oct 31 it was called Twist of Light.",
  "0{Human Paladin:} Ruthless +2% crit on all spells and attacks ( replaces Sword Specialization, Oct 15), Will to Survive (removes stuns), Perception, The Human Spirit (+Spirit). Maxroll recommends it.",
  "3Other races for the Paladin",
  "0• {Dwarf} (Alliance): Stoneform; Earth Fury +2% crit damage and healing ( replaces Mace Specialization, Leprestore). Conquest Capped also cites Artisan's Precision and Big Game Hunter . Starts from Coldridge Valley.",
  "0• {Undead} (Horde): First time Horde Paladins. Will of the Forsaken (removes Charm/Fear/Sleep, with no immunity afterwards), Cannibalize (restores health and mana), Touch of the Grave (20% drain, 25 s cooldown from Oct 15). Conquest Capped and Maxroll list it as the best for leveling. Starts from Deathknell/Brill; trainers Aramis Hammerhand, Shari Stilwell, Hilda the Breaker (Bandarion Keep).",
  "0Not found for the Paladin in sources. Mining is the most cited (Maxroll, Zockify, Conquest Capped, Method): sell the ore you don't use.",
  "0Mining + Blacksmithing: crafted 2H weapons and armor (Heavy Copper Maul at level 11, Thorium Poleaxe 52, Legionite Glaive 58 BoP) and the Camp Lodestone/Sharpening Wheel. Enchanting (Maxroll) for disenchant and Enchanted Lute. Engineering as an alternative (Method; Zockify for tank dungeons).",
  "2Advice for the Paladin",
  "0Cooking (food with XP) and First Aid (bandages between pulls) for everyone; Fishing for cheap food (Conquest Capped). Camp makes professions more useful: Mining (Lodestone), Alchemy (Mana Well), Leatherworking (Camp Tent).\nMining + Blacksmithing for Prot and Ret. Holy: Herbalism + Alchemy (Gfinity), for mana consumption. Sources .",
  "0• {The Test of Righteousness} · inside the dungeon",
  "2Priorities for the Paladin",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nExtra Rested XP (up to 5% of a level, once an hour): the bonus that's worth the most for anyone.",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy priority 2\nUp to 29 mana/5 s: mana is the Ret's limit. Doesn't stack with Blessing of Wisdom: cast Kings on yourself (Maxroll).",
  "0{Lodestone} · Mining priority 3\nAttack Power; doesn't stack with Blessing of Might. Pairs with Blacksmithing (Maxroll; it wasn't in the task's list).",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning\n+2% crit; the only conflict is Moonkin Aura.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nUp to +56 Stamina; no conflict with your spells.",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism\nUp to +25 Intellect: more mana and, from 43, more damage with Champion of the Light.",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring\nUp to +32 Spirit: not very useful for a Ret.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nArmor, stats and resistance.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing\n+8% to all stats, but doesn't stack with Blessing of Kings.",
