  "Wand Specialization:Discipline;Wand Specialization:Discipline;Spirit Tap:Shadow;Spirit Tap:Shadow;Spirit Tap:Shadow;Spirit Tap:Shadow;Spirit Tap:Shadow;Improved Shadow Word: Pain:Shadow;Improved Shadow Word: Pain:Shadow;Shadow Focus:Shadow;Shadow Focus:Shadow;Shadow Focus:Shadow;Mind Flay:Shadow;Improved Mind Flay:Shadow;Improved Mind Flay:Shadow;Shadow Focus:Shadow;Shadow Focus:Shadow;Vampiric Embrace:Shadow;Shadow Weaving:Shadow;Shadow Weaving:Shadow;Shadow Weaving:Shadow;Dark Inspiration:Shadow;Silence:Shadow;Devouring Contagion:Shadow;Devouring Contagion:Shadow;Dark Inspiration:Shadow;Dark Inspiration:Shadow;Darkness:Shadow;Darkness:Shadow;Darkness:Shadow;Darkness:Shadow;Darkness:Shadow;Shadowform:Shadow;Twin Disciplines:Discipline;Twin Disciplines:Discipline;Twin Disciplines:Discipline;Martyrdom:Discipline;Martyrdom:Discipline;Twin Disciplines:Discipline;Twin Disciplines:Discipline;Mental Strength:Discipline;Meditation:Discipline;Meditation:Discipline;Meditation:Discipline;Mental Agility:Discipline;Mental Agility:Discipline;Mental Agility:Discipline;Improved Power Word: Shield:Discipline;Improved Power Word: Shield:Discipline;Improved Power Word: Shield:Discipline;Inner Focus:Discipline",
  "1Talents: Shadow 1–60",
  "0{Choice:} Deep Shadow build: the most preferred by Forever guides for the Priest. Mobalytics DoubleZug ({128 }, Verified, upd. Nov 4), Twicks 27 and Kargoz 8 are Shadow; Warcraft Tavern, Icy Veins (“Deep Shadow”), wowforever.gg and wow4evernews go Shadow up to 30. All sources agree on 10–18: Wand Specialization 2/2, Spirit Tap 5/5, Improved Shadow Word: Pain 2/2; then Shadow Focus, Mind Flay at 22, Vampiric Embrace at 27, Shadow Weaving (28–30) and Shadowform at 42, without respec. The Disc hybrid with Meditation (wowforever.be = Method, Amaxagon, upd. Oct 29; ConquestCapped) remains the alternative: Disc up to 39 (only 7 Shadow points, NOT “Disc up to ~23”) and Shadow respec at 40. DoubleZug himself says the two paths perform “very similarly”; Shadow avoids the respec.",
  "0{Spirit Tap} 5/5 · lvl 12–16",
  "0{Improved Shadow Word: Pain} 2/2 · lvl 17–18",
  "0{Shadow Focus} 3/5 · lvl 19–21",
  "0{Mind Flay} 1/1 · lvl 22",
  "0{Improved Mind Flay} 2/2 · lvl 23–24",
  "0{Shadow Focus} 5/5 · lvl 25–26",
  "0{Vampiric Embrace} 1/1 · lvl 27",
  "0{Shadow Weaving} 3/3 · lvl 28–30",
  "0{Dark Inspiration} 1/5 · lvl 31",
  "0{Silence} 1/1 · lvl 32",
  "0{Devouring Contagion} 2/2 · lvl 33–34",
  "0{Dark Inspiration} 3/5 · lvl 35–36",
  "0{Darkness} 5/5 · lvl 37–41",
  "0{Shadowform} 1/1 · lvl 42",
  "0{Twin Disciplines} 3/5 · lvl 43–45",
  "0{Martyrdom} 2/2 · lvl 46–47",
  "0{Twin Disciplines} 5/5 · lvl 48–49",
  "0{Mental Strength} 1/5 · lvl 50",
  "0{Meditation} 3/3 · lvl 51–53",
  "0{Mental Agility} 3/3 · lvl 54–56",
  "0{Improved Power Word: Shield} 3/3 · lvl 57–59",
  "0{Inner Focus} 1/1 · lvl 60",
  "0wowforever.be – leveling build (client data, 10->60) – hybrid (alternative) · client data; order = Method string · Wand Spec 2/2 -> Spirit Tap 5/5 -> Imp. SW:P 2/2; Twin Disciplines starts at 19 · Twin Disciplines 2/5 (11 points: Wand 2, Spirit Tap 5, ISWP 2, Twin 2) · Twin 5/5, Martyrdom 2/2, Mental Strength 1, Inner Focus 1, Meditation 3/3 (28–30). 31–39: Mental Agility 2, Imp. Inner Fire 3, Imp. PW:S 3, Penance (37). Shadow respec at 40.",
  "0Method – Amaxagon – hybrid (alternative) · upd. Oct 29; talent string identical to wowforever.be · same (Wand -> Spirit Tap -> ISWP) · Twin Disciplines in progress · Disc: Twin, Martyrdom, Meditation. “Mana efficient and tanky”, damage drops late in 30; respec at 40 for Shadowform.",
  "0ConquestCapped – Kir – hybrid (alternative) · upd. Oct 28; text only, no ranks · Wand 2, Spirit Tap 5, ISWP 2 · Disc/Shadow hybrid · Mental Strength, Martyrdom, Meditation (Mental Strength in place of Imp. PW:S after Oct 15). Penance option: 21 Disc points if you heal dungeons.",
  "0Mobalytics – DoubleZug (Priest 1–60) – MAIN BUILD · 128 · upd. Nov 4 · Verified; 20/0/31 at 60 · Wand 2/2 (10–11), Spirit Tap 5/5 (12–16), ISWP 2/2 (17–18) · Shadow Focus 3/5 (19–21) · Mind Flay (22), Imp. Mind Flay 2/2 (23–24), Shadow Focus 5/5 (25–26), Vampiric Embrace (27), Shadow Weaving 3/3 (28–30). 31–41: Dark Inspiration, Silence, Devouring Contagion, Darkness; Shadowform at 42.",
  "0wowforever.gg – Priest Shadow leveling · upd. Oct 30; data from talentsforever.com · Wand 1->2, Spirit Tap 5, ISWP 2, Shadow Focus 2 · 11 pt: Wand 2, Shadow Focus 2, Spirit Tap 5, ISWP 2 · +Shadow Focus 1, Shadow Reach 2, Mind Flay, Imp. Mind Flay 2, Vampiric Embrace, Shadow Weaving 3 (21 pt)",
  "0wow4evernews – Max Calder · published Sep 21, upd. Oct 7 (client 70170) · Wand 2, Spirit Tap 5, ISWP 2 (10–18), Shadow Reach 2 (19–20) · Blackout 1 at 21 · Mind Flay 22, Blackout 5/5, Vampiric Embrace 27, Shadow Weaving 3 (28–30). “No Meditation before 30.”",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Cyradys · beta images (21 pts at 30); Oct · Wand Spec then Spirit Tap/ISWP · Mind Flay and Devouring Plague from 20 (rotation) · Three variants: Disc (Wand 2, Twin, Meditation, Penance), Holy (dungeons), Shadow (doesn't shine before 28). Pre-Oct 15 image layout: per-point detail not reliable",
  "0Maxroll – Cere · upd. Oct 30 (release Oct 27); text only · Wand Spec, Spirit Tap (can be delayed for Penance earlier) · — · Disc (Meditation, Mental Agility, Penance; for party) or Shadow Magic for solo questing (Spirit Tap, Shadow Focus 3/5, Devouring Contagion, Silence, Shadow Weaving, Darkness, Shadowform). Disc “very slow” solo.",
  "0KamiLabs – from Scriblet video · Sep 23; build at 20 = Wand 2, Spirit Tap, ISWP · Wand Spec, Spirit Tap, ISWP · same; from 20 Imp. Psychic Scream, Vampiric Embrace, Shadowform · For groups: Meditation build. Mind Flay not used (less than one wand shot).",
  "0Icy Veins – Shadow Priest leveling (snippet only) · upd. by level 30; not read on page · — · — · “Deep Shadow”: Shadow Reach, Shadow Weaving, ISWP, Imp. Mind Blast; they prefer Blackout over Shadow Focus.",
  "3Discipline hybrid alternative + Shadow respec at 40 (wowforever.be = Method, Amaxagon upd. Oct 29; ConquestCapped Oct 28)",
  "0{Order wowforever.be/Method (client data):} Wand Specialization ×2 (10–11) -> Spirit Tap ×5 (12–16) -> Improved Shadow Word: Pain ×2 (17–18) -> Twin Disciplines ×5 (19–23) -> Martyrdom ×2 (24–25) -> Mental Strength (26) -> Inner Focus (27) -> Meditation ×3 (28–30) -> Mental Agility ×2 (31–32) -> Improved Inner Fire ×3 (33–35) -> Improved Power Word: Shield (36) -> {Penance} (37) -> Improved Power Word: Shield ×2 (38–39).",
  "0{Respec at 40 (31 Shadow points):} Shadow Focus ×5, Improved Shadow Word: Pain ×2, Improved Mind Blast ×4, Mind Flay, Improved Mind Flay ×2, Spirit Tap ×5, Shadow Weaving ×3, Vampiric Embrace, Devouring Contagion ×2, Darkness ×5, Shadowform. {41–60:} Twin Disciplines ×5, Early Demise ×2, Martyrdom ×2, Mental Strength ×3, Inner Focus, Meditation ×3, Mental Strength ×2, Shadow Reach ×2.",
  "0{Pros:} “mana efficient and tanky”, Meditation at 30, Penance at 37 (Method). {Cons:} damage drops late in 30 (Method) and the respec costs gold. Note: wowforever.be does NOT switch to Shadow at ~23, it stays Disc until 39.",
  "3Penance / pure Discipline variant (WT, Maxroll, Mobalytics)",
  "0From 30 you can respec 21 points into Discipline for {Penance} (at the cost of Spirit Tap, Mobalytics Disc 16/0/5). ConquestCapped: Penance scaled back after beta. Useful for dungeons/party; {solo questing is “very slow”} (Maxroll).",
  "3Holy/Smite variant (DoubleZug, WT)",
  "0Holy gives Twilight Focus (anti-pushback), Improved Renew, Divine Fury (faster Smite/Holy Fire). DoubleZug: “third choice” for mid-game; WT: healer leveling not recommended (slow kills). Prayer of Mending () arrives at 40.",
  "3Shadowform: 40 or 42?",
  "0DoubleZug waits for 42 and saves for the mount; anyone who wants the form right away redoes the build at 40 with Darkness 5/5 in place of Wand Specialization (same author). The main build here doesn't require a respec.",
  "3Other Shadow variants ()",
  "0wowforever.gg: Shadow Focus 2 at 20, Mind Flay/Improved Mind Flay/VE/Shadow Weaving 3 at 30 (21 points). wow4evernews (Max Calder, upd. Oct 7): Shadow Reach 19–20, Blackout 21–26, Mind Flay 22, VE 27, Shadow Weaving 28–30. Icy Veins (snippet only): Shadow Reach, Shadow Weaving, ISWP, Improved Mind Blast, prefers Blackout over Shadow Focus.",
  "31–9 · Smite + DoT + melee",
  "0^spell_holy_holysmite,spell_shadow_shadowwordpain,spell_holy_powerwordshield,inv_wand_01^Smite ×1–2 -> SW:P (from 4) -> PW:S (from 6) -> Wand (from 5, craft)",
  "01–3: Smite until the mob is low or out of mana, then melee. From 4: Smite -> Shadow Word: Pain -> Smite -> melee. If someone contests your tag, open with SW:P (DoTs tag immediately). From 6, put PW:S up before the pull. As soon as you have a Lesser Magic Wand (level 5, Enchanting, see professions), Smite almost disappears: the wand costs 0 mana and doesn't break regen.",
  "310–19 · Pre-shield, Mind Blast, DoT, wand",
  "0^spell_holy_powerwordshield,spell_shadow_unholyfrenzy,spell_shadow_shadowwordpain,inv_wand_01,spell_holy_renew^PW:S -> Mind Blast -> SW:P -> Wand -> Renew (between pulls)",
  "0Pre-cast PW:S and Mind Blast (if big mob), SW:P on 2–3 mobs (not too many: DoTs need to reach ~24 s), then wand; tab-target with the wand to avoid wasting ticks. Between pulls use excess mana for Renew, Inner Fire and Power Word: Fortitude. Psychic Scream if you're in trouble and the mobs don't flee toward others (open spaces, beasts). Stop after each kill to trigger Spirit Tap.",
  "320–41 · Multi-DoT + Devouring Plague + Vampiric Embrace",
  "0^spell_holy_powerwordshield,spell_holy_searinglight,spell_shadow_shadowwordpain,spell_shadow_devouringplague,spell_shadow_unsummonbuilding,inv_wand_01^PW:S -> Holy Fire / Mind Blast -> SW:P -> Devouring Plague -> Vampiric Embrace (27+) -> Wand",
  "0Prepull: PW:S, Renew, Inner Fire (and Shadowguard if Troll). Open with Holy Fire (3.5 s, efficient) or Mind Blast on tough mobs, SW:P on 2–3 mobs, Devouring Plague + Vampiric Embrace on the toughest mob and let it live until the DoT ends (strong heal). Wand as filler, tab-target to avoid overkill. Mind Flay (from 24) only to snare a fleeing mob: before 28 + Improved Mind Flay it doesn't beat DoT+wand (DoubleZug). With Devouring Contagion (33–34) put DP on the target to kill first and let the DoT jump.",
  "0^spell_shadow_shadowwordpain,spell_shadow_psychicscream,spell_shadow_devouringplague,inv_wand_01^SW:P ×3 -> Psychic Scream -> DP on the tough mob -> Wand in rotation",
  "0No real AoE (Method: “No AoE”). Multi-DoT: SW:P on 3–4 mobs (2–3 safe, unprotected), one DP on the toughest mob, wand in rotation to avoid overkill. From 33 Devouring Contagion: DP on the target to kill first and the DoT jumps. Psychic Scream if mobs reach melee; one kill to trigger Spirit Tap, then heal with PW:S/Renew.",
  "342+ · Shadowform: Mind Blast + Flay",
  "0^spell_shadow_shadowform,spell_holy_powerwordshield,spell_shadow_unholyfrenzy,spell_shadow_shadowwordpain,spell_shadow_devouringplague,spell_shadow_siphonmana^Shadowform -> PW:S -> Mind Blast -> SW:P -> Devouring Plague -> Mind Flay ×2 -> Blast",
  "0Shadowform before the pull, PW:S, open with Mind Blast, SW:P, Devouring Plague on the key mob, VE if health is low; filler Mind Flay ×2 -> Mind Blast (DoubleZug), with Shadow Word: Death (trainer 32) and Mind Blast on CD. In form Heal/Renew break the form: heal with PW:S. If you don't have PW:S active and can't reapply it, use the wand (no pushback).",
  "3Mana and 5-second rule (DoubleZug)",
  "0• Spirit regen stops 5 s after spending mana (including instant spells), but {not} with free spells (Inner Focus, racials at 0 cost).",
  "0• Cast your spells all together at the start of the pull: long ones first (Holy Fire), then instants.",
  "0• With Spirit Tap and Meditation the 5SR matters less but isn't irrelevant.",
  "3DoT efficiency",
  "0• Let SW:P and Devouring Plague run to the end of their duration: better to pull a second mob than to kill the first one too early (DoubleZug).",
  "0• DoTs/HoTs in Forever update dynamically (no snapshot) and can crit (Warcraft Tavern, DoubleZug).",
  "3Wand in Forever",
  "0• From Oct 15 you need to stand still 0.5 s before the wand fires (ConquestCapped); according to CC it no longer scales with spell power, but Scriblet/KamiLabs (Sep 23) saw it scale ~0.3 conflict: verify after launch.",
  "0Spell power and Spirit first (DoubleZug: Spirit > Spell Power > Intellect > crit/mp5 > Stamina > Hit > Haste; ConquestCapped: spell power first, Spirit equal or higher after 40–50 SP for Spirit Tap; WT: Int/Spell Damage > Stamina/Spirit > Armor). Wands are the main weapon: Lesser Magic Wand (5) -> Greater Magic Wand (13) -> Sizzle Stick (15, WC) -> Gravestone Scepter (18, BFD) -> Wand of Eventide (27, BoE) -> Greater Mystic Wand (30). Melee weapons: staff/weapon with spell power from dungeon quests (Ragefire Chasm at 10, Wailing Caverns at 15; DoubleZug: “keeping the weapon updated is MUCH more important than in Classic”). Maxroll “dungeon chase list” (names): Deadmines Emberstone Staff/Cookie’s Stirring Rod, Shadowfang Keep Odo’s Ley Staff, Stockade Kam’s Walking Stick, Blackfathom Deeps Rod of the Sleepwalker ( stats not verified). Weapon skill: Daggers, Maces, Staves, Wands (WT; trainers: Woo Ping Stormwind, Ilyenia Moonfire Darnassus, Bixi Wobblebonk Ironforge; Horde Sayoc/Hanashi Orgrimmar, Ansekhwa Thunder Bluff, Archibald Undercity).",
  "0• New spells for Priest: Penance (Disc talent, 150 Mana, 12 s CD), Prayer of Mending (Holy talent, 40), Binding Heal (Holy talent 25), Devouring Plague and Fear Ward now base at 20 (Blizzard Watch, Oct 9; WT).",
  "0• Each race has 2 racial spells (10 and 20); Gnome is new; Elune’s Grace/Starshards/Dwarf Chastise/Dark Sacrifice recreated (Blizzard Watch, Oct 9).",
  "0• SW:P and Renew can crit; DoTs update dynamically without snapshot (WT, DoubleZug).",
  "0• Beta Oct 15 (WT/ConquestCapped/wowforeverguides): Improved Power Word: Shield moved to row 3; Improved Fade removed; the wand requires 0.5 s standing still before firing (CC).",
  "0• Beta Oct 1: changes to Devouring Plague, SW:D, Inner Focus, Shadow Weaving (wowforeverguides ).",
  "0• Oct 26: The Human Spirit raised to +10% Spirit (ConquestCapped).",
  "0• Relevant new/changed talents: Wand Specialization (13/25%), Twin Disciplines, Mental Agility, Improved Inner Fire (+charges), Silent Resolve, Holy Binding, Devouring Contagion, Early Demise, Dark Inspiration, Improved Mind Flay (wf client).",
  "0• Spirit Tap: +100% Spirit and +50% regen while casting for 15 s after a non-trivial kill or an enemy death with Vampiric Embrace (wf client).",
  "0• Legacy (Talented) from levels 25/45/60 (wowforeverguides ); Thrill of Adventure and The Quick and the Dead recommended (ConquestCapped).",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): Power Word: Shield can be replaced by one of equal or higher rank, Shadow Word: Death no longer hurts you when it misses, Vampiric Embrace heals can no longer crit, Dark Sacrifice no longer breaks crowd control.",
  "0{Smite} Lvl 1\nHoly damage with 1.5 s cast: your attack until 5 (Rank 2 at 6, 3 at 14, 4 at 22, 5 at 30).",
  "0{Lesser Heal} Lvl 1\nBase heal (Rank 2 at 4, Rank 3 at 10); replaced by Heal at 16.",
  "0{Power Word: Fortitude} Lvl 1\n1 h Stamina buff on you and the group (Rank 2 at 12, 3 at 24, 4 at 36).",
  "0{Shadow Word: Pain} Lvl 4\nYour main DoT (18 s, 24 s with Imp. SW:P); tags mobs on the fly. Rank 2 at 10, 3 at 18, 4 at 26, 5 at 34.",
  "0{Power Word: Shield} Lvl 6\nAbsorbs damage and prevents pushback while active; “Weakened Soul” 15 s. Rank 2 at 12, 3 at 18, 4 at 24, 5 at 30, 6 at 36.",
  "0{Fade} Lvl 8\nReduces threat for 10 s; only useful in a group (Rank 2 at 20, 3 at 30).",
  "0{Renew} Lvl 8\nCan crit in Forever; 15 s HoT, your base heal between pulls (Rank 2 at 14, 3 at 20, 4 at 26, 5 at 32).",
  "0{Mind Blast} Lvl 10\nShadow hit 1.5 s, 8 s CD: open with this on big mobs. Rank 2 at 16, 3 at 22, 4 at 28, 5 at 34.",
  "0{Resurrection} Lvl 10\nResurrects a player out of combat (Rank 2 at 22, 3 at 34).",
  "0{Racial 1 (class quest)} Lvl 10\nRacial spell at 10: Divine Grace (Human), Desperate Prayer (Dwarf), Starshards (Night Elf), Confounding Flash (Gnome), Touch of Weakness (Undead), Hex of Weakness (Troll). See races.",
  "0{Inner Fire} Lvl 12\n+315 armor, 20 charges (consumed with every hit taken): keep it always active, PW:S protects the charges. Rank 2 at 20, 3 at 30.",
  "0{Psychic Scream} Lvl 14\nFear on 2 enemies within 8 yd (8 s), 30 s CD. DON’T skip it (DoubleZug): the Priest's emergency. Watch out for adds.",
  "0{Cure Disease} Lvl 14\nRemoves 1 disease: Forever has some annoying ones (DoubleZug).",
  "0{Heal} Lvl 16\n3 s cast heal (260–300 Rank 1): the “heavy” heal only when you're under shield/fear. Rank 2 at 22, 3 at 28.",
  "0{Dispel Magic} Lvl 18\nRemoves 1 buff from an enemy or 1 debuff from an ally; usually better to just kill faster.",
  "0{Devouring Plague} Lvl 20\nNow base for everyone (was Undead): 24 s DoT for 128 that heals you for the damage; 24 s CD in the client (Blizzard Watch, Oct 9: 1 min). Rank 2 at 28, 3 at 36.",
  "0{Fear Ward} Lvl 20\nNow base for everyone (was Dwarf): 3 min duration, 3 min CD.",
  "0{Flash Heal} Lvl 20\nFast 1.5 s heal for emergencies (Rank 2 at 26, 3 at 32).",
  "0{Holy Fire} Lvl 20\n3.5 s cast: 53–65 Holy + 20 DoT; more efficient than Mind Blast but long (Rank 2 at 24, 3 at 30).",
  "0{Mind Soothe} Lvl 20\nReduces by 10 yd the range from which a humanoid (40) attacks you, 15 s (utility).",
  "0{Shackle Undead} Lvl 20\nShackles an undead for 30 s (useful CC in Tirisfal/Duskwood/Silverpine).",
  "0{Racial 2 (class quest)} Lvl 20\nRacial spell at 20: Feedback (Human), Chastise (Dwarf), Elune’s Grace (Night Elf), Contingency Plan (Gnome), Dark Sacrifice (Undead), Shadowguard (Troll).",
  "0{Mind Vision} Lvl 22\nSee through the target's eyes (utility).",
  "0{Mana Burn} Lvl 24\nBurns mana of an enemy caster (3 s cast); can be skipped in PvE.",
  "0{Binding Heal} Lvl 25\nHoly talent (not in the build): heals target + you. Rank 2 at 32.",
  "0{Divine Spirit} Lvl 30\n1 h Spirit buff (+17 Rank 1): great with Spirit Tap/Meditation; requires a Spirit-friendly party.",
  "0{Mind Control} Lvl 30\nControls a humanoid until 44 (PvE: CC/utility).",
  "0{Prayer of Healing} Lvl 30\n3 s group heal (dungeons only).",
  "0{Shadow Protection} Lvl 30\nShadow resist +30 for 10 min.",
  "0{Shadow Word: Death} Lvl 32\nNew Trainer skill at 32 (Method, WT ): instant Shadow hit, 12 s CD; Early Demise boosts it.",
  "0{Abolish Disease} Lvl 32\nCures diseases over time.",
  "0{Levitate} Lvl 34\nReagent Light Feather: float, fall more slowly, walk on water.",
  "0{Penance} Lvl 30\nNew spell (Disc talent, 150 Mana, 12 s CD; the client lists it as Lv 30): 45 Holy ×3 or 134 heal ×3. Not in the Shadow build: only in Disc/hybrid variants (Penance at 37). Rank 2 at 40, 3 at 50, 4 at 60.",
  "0{Greater Heal} Lvl 40\nBig 3 s heal (819–920 Rank 1); at 40 also Mind Blast Rank 6, Mind Flay Rank 3, Inner Fire Rank 4, PW:Fortitude/Divine Spirit Rank 2; talents Power Infusion (Disc, +20% spell) and Prayer of Mending (Holy).",
  "0{Power Word: Shield (Rank 7)} Lvl 42\nRank 7 at 42, 8 at 48, 9 at 54, 10 at 60; SW:P Rank 6 at 42, 7 at 50, 8 at 58.",
  "0{Prayer of Fortitude} Lvl 48\nGroup Stamina buff (Rank 2 at 60). Prayer of Spirit at 60.",
  "0{Prayer of Spirit} Lvl 60\nGroup Spirit buff; at 60 also Penance Rank 4, Mind Flay Rank 6.",
  "0{Mind Flay} Lvl 22\nShadow talent: 3 s channel, 63 damage, 50% slow (stop fleeing mobs). Filler with Improved Mind Flay + Shadowform.",
  "0{Vampiric Embrace} Lvl 27\nShadow talent: heals the party for 20% of Shadow damage over 30 s, 30 s CD.",
  "0{Silence} Lvl 32\nShadow talent: silences for 5 s and interrupts for 3 s, 225 Mana, 45 s CD.",
  "0{Shadowform} Lvl 42\nShadow talent (capstone): +10% Shadow damage, 50% mana, crit ×2, 15% physical damage; no healing in form.",
  "0{Inner Focus} Lvl 60\nDisc talent: next spell free and +25% crit, 3 min CD.",
  "0{Human Priest:} Alliance. The Human Spirit (+10% Spirit, upd. Oct 26) and Ruthless (+1% crit): great with Spirit Tap/Meditation. Racials: Divine Grace (10, heals ally <50% and removes Weakened Soul, NO self) and Feedback (20). DoubleZug: Human/Gnome are second-best for leveling; CC: “Weak” for leveling.",
  "3Other races for the Priest",
  "0• {Dwarf} (Alliance): Alliance. Desperate Prayer (10, self-heal 146–181, 10 min CD), Chastise ( 20, 2 s root on humanoids); Stoneform / Artisan’s Precision (+1% hit, wowclassicforever.info). CC: “Average”.",
  "0• {Night Elf} (Alliance): Alliance. Starshards (10, 162 Arcane damage over 6 s, 30 s CD ) and Elune’s Grace (20, 50% chance to be hit for 15 s ), Shadowmeld usable in combat, 2% movement, Wisp Spirit, Elune’s Light. DoubleZug: “quite strong for leveling”, his first Alliance pick; CC: “Good”.",
  "0• {Gnome} (Alliance): Alliance ( new for Priest). Confounding Flash (10, confuses 5 enemies for 3 s, 2 min CD ) and Contingency Plan (20, 30 s ward: below 35% absorbs + HoT, 5–10 min CD ); Escape Artist, Expansive Mind, Eureka!. DoubleZug: Human/Gnome are close seconds; CC: “Good”.",
  "0• {Undead} (Horde): Horde. Touch of Weakness (10) and Dark Sacrifice ( 20: lose health, gain mana + Spirit), Cannibalize (usable in combat: very strong sustain), Will of the Forsaken, Touch of the Grave (30% drain on casters). DoubleZug: “Undead/Troll” for Horde leveling; CC: “Best”.",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Horde. Hex of Weakness (10, 43 AP, 20% healing received) and Shadowguard (20, 3 charges 10 min), Berserking (+10% cast speed 15 s), Beast Slaying (“gains a lot of value while leveling”, DoubleZug), Rapid Regeneration. CC: “Best”.",
  "0Skinning + Herbalism (Method, ConquestCapped): less invasive, give gold per rank/water. Enchanting: disenchant greens (tailoring). Cooking: food +5% XP, also for level 1 recipes (DoubleZug). From 25 / 45 / 60: each craft at 150/225/300 gives a Legacy point (ConquestCapped).",
  "0Tailoring + Enchanting (DoubleZug 47 “HIGHLY recommend”, Method, ConquestCapped, Maxroll): crafted Greater Magic Wand, Minor Wizard Oil (cheap, from vendor), 6–8 slot bags, soulbound green/blue gear (Gloves/Boots of Shadow with Merchant’s Favor, KamiLabs ), Enchanted Lute/Banner camp. Alchemy (Minor Arcane Elixir, Elixir of Wisdom, mana/health pots) is a good second, but its recipes must be bought.",
  "2Advice for the Priest",
  "0Launch: craft the Lesser Magic Wand yourself (Method): Enchanting 10 + Tailoring for Brown Linen Robe to disenchant + Runed Copper Rod; alternative: a guild Blacksmith disenchants Copper Shortsword (~80%, ConquestCapped). Light/Medium Armor Kit from Leatherworking (+4/+8 Stamina). First Aid optional: the Priest heals themselves (Method).\nTailoring + Enchanting in leveling. Endgame Tailoring + Engineering (Gfinity: movement speed and defensives from Engineering). Sources .",
  "2Priorities for the Priest",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP up to 5% of a level, once an hour: the most useful for any class (my ranking : no source ranks camps for Priest).",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring priority 2\nUp to +32 Spirit: Spirit is your stat (Spirit Tap doubles Spirit, Meditation, regen). Doesn't stack with Divine Spirit (Maxroll).",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy priority 3\nUp to 29 mana/5 s: helps if you pull more casts (Disc/Meditation, dungeons); less critical with wand + Spirit Tap. Excludes Blessing of Wisdom.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing\n+8% to all stats (excludes Blessing of Kings).",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism\nUp to +25 Intellect (doesn't stack with Arcane Intellect): more mana and crit for SW:P/Renew.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nUp to +56 Stamina (doesn't stack with PW:Fortitude, Maxroll): more survivability on multiple pulls.",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning\n+2% crit (excludes Moonkin Aura): useful now that SW:P and Renew can crit.",
