  "0Mobalytics – Djexde, Rogue Leveling 1-60 – BUILD A · 36 · upd. Nov 5 · 16/35/0 at 60 · Remorseless Attacks 2 (10–11), Efficient Strikes 2, Coup de Grace 3, Deflection 3 (17–19) · Precision · Precision, Riposte (22), Precision 3/3, Endurance 2 (24–25), Lightning Reflexes, Weapon Expertise 2, Aggression; Blade Flurry at 32, Adrenaline Rush at 42",
  "0wowforever.gg – Rogue Combat Leveling (3 Nov tree) · updated 3 Nov 2026, checkpoints every 10 levels · Efficient Strikes 2, Coup de Grace 3, Deflection 3, Precision 3 (at 20) · idem · Riposte, Endurance 2, Improved Sprint 1, Weapon Expertise 2, Aggression 3, Dual Wield Spec 1 (at 30); at 40 Dual Wield Spec 2, Blade Flurry, Hack and Slash 4, Flash of Steel 3, Adrenaline Rush",
  "0wowforever.be – leveling build (client) · client data 1.60.1.70707, read Nov 1 · Remorseless Attacks 2 -> Improved Sinister Strike 2 -> Improved Eviscerate 3 -> Puncturing Wounds 3 (10–19) · Deflection 1/3 at 20 · Deflection 3 -> Riposte (23) -> Precision 3 (24–26) -> Flawless Execution (27) -> Dual Wield Spec 3/5 (28–30); 31 DWS 4, 32 Blade Flurry, 33–34 Opportunity, 35 Hack and Slash",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Nevermore (1–60 guide, 30 Combat build) · upd. Oct 2026, talent images; 60 \"provisional\" · Improved Eviscerate 3, Improved Sinister Strike 2, Puncturing Wounds 3 (without Remorseless Attacks) · Deflection 3 + Riposte · Precision 3, Flawless Execution, Dual Wield Spec 4, Blade Flurry (21 points all in Combat)",
  "0Method – Reholy · upd. Oct 9, 2026 · Remorseless Attacks 2 until 30 · idem · At 30 respec: Dual Wield Spec 4/5 + Blade Flurry (if you don't have Legacy Points); without daggers: Endurance 2 + Lightning Reflexes 1 in place of Puncturing Wounds. After: Hack and Slash 5, Weapon Expertise 2, Aggression 3, Adrenaline Rush",
  "0Mobalytics – DonTheCrown (Combat 0/21/0, 1–30 and 31–60 tabs) · 37 (list) / 34 (page), Verified, Oct 28; video 62k views (Sep 29) · Improved Sinister Strike 2, Improved Eviscerate 3, Precision 2, Deflection 3, Riposte · Riposte, Precision 3/3 · Endurance 2, Improved Sprint 1, Flawless Execution, Dual Wield Spec 4, Blade Flurry. NO Puncturing Wounds, no Remorseless Attacks",
  "0Mobalytics – Rogue's Diary (Combat 1–60 with order, 20/31/0) · 50 · upd. Nov 4 · 16/35/0 at 60 · Remorseless Attacks 2 (10–11), Improved Sinister Strike 2, Improved Eviscerate 3, Precision 3 · respec at 20: Improved Eviscerate 3, Improved Sinister Strike 2, Precision 2, Deflection 3, Riposte · Endurance 2 (21–22), Precision 3, Lightning Reflexes/Improved Sprint, DWS 26–29, Blade Flurry at 30; 31–34 Hack and Slash, 35–36 Weapon Expertise, 37 H&S, 38–39 Aggression, 40 Adrenaline Rush, then Remorseless Attacks, Malice, Ruthlessness, Relentless Strikes, Lethality, Cold Blood, Improved Slice and Dice",
  "0WoW Forever (official channel) – Ultimate Rogue Guide · 17k views, Oct 18 · Combat 0/21/0: Improved Eviscerate 3, Improved Sinister Strike 2 · Deflection 3 · Precision 3, Endurance 2, Riposte, Improved Sprint 1, Flawless Execution, DWS 4, Blade Flurry",
  "3No-dagger variant (Mobalytics 37 and 28 ): Endurance in place of Puncturing Wounds",
  "0If you're holding swords, axes or maces (for example Ruby-Adorned Blade), Puncturing Wounds is of little use: Backstab requires a dagger. DonTheCrown and Rogue's Diary take {Endurance 2/2} instead (Sprint and Evasion every 2 minutes: 'the best leveling talent' for Rogue's Diary) and {Improved Sprint}. Method gives the same advice: 3 points from Puncturing Wounds to {Endurance 2 + Lightning Reflexes 1}.",
  "0wowforever.be and Warcraft Tavern stay on the dagger + Backstab branch because {Blade of Cunning} (level 10 quest) is a dagger, and because Mobalytics/Method say Backstab is much more convenient in groups.",
  "3Assassination (Mutilate) – slower, better after 30",
  "0Warcraft Tavern: 'not recommended as a starting spec', grows with Mutilate (talent at 30, only with two daggers) and Poison. Gaunerh (65k views, Oct 7) says Mutilate at 30 is 'short on Energy'; his Oct 27 video (13k) recommends respeccing to Mutilate around {32} if you have good daggers. Method and Icy Veins keep it as an alternative.",
  "3Subtlety (Ambush / Hemorrhage) – only for curiosity or PvP",
  "0Mobalytics describes it as the PvP spec: solo, mobs look you in the face and Ambush requires Stealth. Warcraft Tavern: the Ambush build 'isn't good in dungeons' until Cutthroat arrives (35, but 'beta builds don't have enough points'). Gaunerh (65k views) finds Hemorrhage/Subtlety 'surprisingly strong' but I didn't read his final conclusion (no transcript).",
  "3Legacy Points and \"Talented\" (+5 levels earlier)",
  "0DonTheCrown: the first 5 Legacy Points in {Thrill of Adventure} (5% of max health per kill). If you level an alt, {Well Rested} unlocks Talented: Riposte, Blade Flurry and Adrenaline Rush 5 levels earlier. Warcraft Tavern: talents arrive up to 5 levels earlier with Talented.",
  "31–9 · Sinister Strike + Eviscerate",
  "0^ability_throw,spell_shadow_ritualofsacrifice,ability_rogue_eviscerate^Throw (pull) -> Sinister Strike -> Sinister Strike -> Eviscerate",
  "0Open with Throw (starting throwing weapon) to tag from range, then Sinister Strike for Combo Points and Eviscerate on the nearly dead mob. With a dagger you can open with Backstab from level 4 (from Stealth), but Warcraft Tavern says not to use Stealth on every mob: it's slow. Evasion at 8 for strong mobs. Gouge (6) to interrupt a cast or escape.",
  "310–19 · Slice and Dice joins the rotation",
  "0^ability_rogue_slicedice,spell_shadow_ritualofsacrifice,ability_backstab,ability_rogue_eviscerate^Slice and Dice -> Sinister Strike -> Backstab (dagger) -> Eviscerate",
  "0With Dual Wield and Slice and Dice (10): Sinister Strike twice, then Slice and Dice, then keep using Sinister Strike and finish with Eviscerate (DonTheCrown). Slice and Dice only takes priority if the fight will last long enough or if you're about to attack another mob right away. Use Kick (12) on casters. From 14 you can use Expose Armor only on mobs that live for its full duration. With a dagger in main hand: Ambush from Stealth (18).",
  "320–31 · Poison, Riposte, Cheap Shot",
  "0^ability_poisons,ability_cheapshot,ability_rogue_slicedice,spell_shadow_ritualofsacrifice,ability_warrior_challange,ability_rogue_eviscerate^Instant Poison -> Cheap Shot -> Slice and Dice -> Sinister Strike -> Riposte -> Eviscerate",
  "0From 20, Instant Poison on both weapons (almost always better than Deadly Poison for mobs that die quickly, DonTheCrown and Rogue's Diary). From 26, Stealth -> Cheap Shot (2 Combo Points) -> Slice and Dice, and if possible gather mobs while entering Stealth. Riposte when it procs (macro with Sinister Strike). From 24, Shank (off-hand, 5 Energy, gives back 15 Energy, 10 sec cooldown) on every cooldown. Rupture isn't needed. Kidney Shot from 30 for dangerous mobs.",
  "332+ · Blade Flurry and multiple mobs",
  "0^ability_warrior_punishingblow,spell_shadow_shadowward,spell_shadow_ritualofsacrifice,ability_rogue_slicedice,ability_rogue_eviscerate^Blade Flurry -> Evasion -> Sinister Strike -> Slice and Dice -> Eviscerate at 5 points",
  "0With 2–4 mobs: Sap to isolate, then Blade Flurry + Evasion (with Endurance both have 2-minute cooldowns), focus Sinister Strike on the strongest mob to reach 5 Combo Points: Eviscerate also hits the second target. From 40, Adrenaline Rush allows pulls of 3–5 mobs (Rogue's Diary). Sprint and Evasion sync up with Blade Flurry (Rogue's Diary).",
  "3Energy, Combo Points and downtime",
  "0^inv_drink_milk_05,inv_misc_bandage_01^Thistle Tea -> Bandage",
  "0Energy 100, now regenerates continuously (1 every 0,1 s = 10 per second, Warcraft Tavern). From 18, Poised: at full Energy and out of combat your first ability costs 10 less Energy, so open the pull at full Energy. Never use a builder at 5 Combo Points, and never a finisher with few points. Don't switch targets while building Combo Points: you lose them. Thistle Tea (+100 Energy, recipe from the quest at 20 or Smudge Thunderwood at Ravenholdt Manor): use it near 0 Energy, ideally inside Blade Flurry. No self-heal: use a bandage (First Aid) after Gouge/Blind/Kidney Shot, but only if there are no DoTs on the mob. Food with +5% XP before pulling.",
  "3Opener and Stealth",
  "0Warcraft Tavern: use Stealth against strong mobs, go in head-on against the rest, otherwise you slow down your leveling. From 26 on, Cheap Shot -> Slice and Dice is DonTheCrown's farming rotation. With a dagger: Ambush (from 18) is better than Garrote or an early Backstab (Method).",
  "3Pick Pocket, Sap, Distract",
  "0 Sap no longer breaks Stealth, and Distract (22) lowers detection for 10 s: you use them to move through mob camps. Pick Pocket before the opener (macro): it can miss and drop you out of Stealth.",
  "3Useful macros (Mobalytics)",
  "0• {Riposte/Sinister Strike}: #showtooltip Sinister Strike / /startattack / /cast Riposte / /cast Sinister Strike (DonTheCrown, Rogue's Diary).",
  "0• {Poison and sharpening stone with one click}: left-click main hand, right-click off-hand (Rogue's Diary).",
  "0Priority: Agility > Attack Power / Strength > Stamina (Rogue's Diary, Warcraft Tavern). Secondary: Expertise > Hit > Crit (Rogue's Diary); DonTheCrown weighs Agility 1,8, AP 1, Strength 1, Hit 18, Crit 23 per point; you need 5–8% Hit early (9% to never miss specials). Agility: 29 -> 1% crit, 14,5 -> 1% dodge. Weapon: Main Hand slow and strong (Sinister Strike uses weapon damage: Cruel Barb 30–57 vs Thief's Blade 17–32), off-hand fast or with more DPS. Method: always use the weapon with the highest DPS in MH; Sinister Strike is always better with a non-dagger. Dagger only for Backstab/Ambush/Mutilate. Weapon upgrades (Rogue's Diary and DonTheCrown): Blade of Cunning (quest 10), Copper Dagger / Copper Shortsword (Blacksmithing 25); Notched Shortsword, Carving Knife, Curved Dagger (world drop BoE at the Auction House: the Int/Spirit variants cost less); Hall of Thanes: Durgen's Crescent Axe; Deadmines (17–26): Cruel Barb, Thief's Blade, Buzz Saw, Dull Sawblade; Wailing Caverns: Stinging Viper, Tail Spike (Wingblade quest Horde); Ruins of Lordaeron: Meathook Slicer, Vileblood Scimitar, Edward's Knife, Plaguefang; Shadowfang Keep: Butcher's Cleaver/Slicer, Meteor Shard; Stockade: Hamhock's Cleaver, Prison Shank (rare); BFD: Darkwater Talwar, Bite of Serra'kis; Excavation Site: Excavated Dagger, Golemsight Long Gun (+6 Agility); Gnomeregan: Toxic Revenger; SM Graveyard: Torturing Poker, Bloody Brass Knuckles, Ironspine's Fist; Ruby-Adorned Blade (class quest, 30). Warcraft Tavern also mentions Assassin's Blade, Shadowfang. Set to look for: Defias Leather. Weapons: Rogues can now use one-handed axes (): Trainer Buliwyf Stonehand in Ironforge; Hanashi/Sayoc in Orgrimmar; Swords: Woo Ping (Stormwind) / Archibald (Undercity); Maces: Buliwyf (Ironforge) / Ansekhwa (Thunder Bluff); Fist: Ilyenia Moonfire (Darnassus) / Sayoc (Orgrimmar). Poison: Instant Poison on both weapons while leveling; now they stack with Sharpening Stones: Rough Sharpening Stone / Coarse Sharpening Stone (cheap on the AH). Camp: Fish Bowl +8% stats.",
  "0• Continuous energy: 1 every 0,1 s, 10 per second (Warcraft Tavern, Oct 2026; official video Oct 18).",
  "0• Poisons: scale with Attack Power, can crit, have more charges (Instant Poison 175, Deadly Poison 180 at max rank) and stack with Sharpening Stones, Weightstones and Windfury Totem (official WoW Forever video Oct 18; Warcraft Tavern; Blizzard class deep dive Rogue/Warlock).",
  "0• Sap no longer breaks Stealth; Distract lowers detection for 10 s; Feint reduces threat by double; Expose Armor counts as 5 Sunder Armor and no longer blocks Sunder (official video Oct 18).",
  "0• The Rogue can learn one-handed axes (Buliwyf Stonehand in Ironforge, Hanashi/Sayoc in Orgrimmar) (Warcraft Tavern, official video).",
  "0• New talents (Combat): Flawless Execution, Hack and Slash, Puncturing Wounds (client: 'New in Forever'). Changed: Deflection 3 ranks (6% Parry), Precision 3 ranks (3% Hit), Dual Wield Specialization +50% off-hand in 2 ranks, Weapon Expertise 2% dodge/parry, Coup de Grace (was Improved Eviscerate, +20%), Efficient Strikes (was Improved Sinister Strike); since 3 Nov also Composure and Flash of Steel, Endurance 60% Sprint/Evasion cooldown, Improved Kick silence 2 s.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): new Shank ability at 24 (off-hand strike for 50%, gives back 15 Energy, 10 sec cooldown; rank 2 at 44), Poised at 18, Instant Poison and Deadly Poison get twice the Attack Power, Flawless Execution takes 15 Energy off Eviscerate, Seal Fate 3 ranks, Lethality 2 ranks.",
  "0• Assassination: Mutilate (row 7, two daggers) and Venom (since 3 Nov a passive tied to Shank), Blood Splatter; Subtlety: Dirty Tricks, Quick Getaway, Boot Knife and Death Mark (31 points). On 3 Nov Murder, Improved Distract, Quietus, Cutthroat and Thousand Cuts were removed; Opportunity is back to 5 ranks.",
  "0• Stat food also gives +5% XP; Thistle Tea restores 100 Energy; dungeons give much less XP (DonTheCrown).",
  "0• Racial changes on Oct 15 and Oct 27 (official video; Rogue's Diary changelog): re-check the racials in-game.",
  "0• Cooking gives access to Camp objects (campfire, Fish Bowl, etc.).",
  "0• Pre-launch data: all numbers from client 1.60.1.70707 and the beta (cap 30). Warcraft Tavern: build 60 'coming at launch'.",
  "0{Sinister Strike} Lvl 1\nMain builder: grants 1 Combo Point. Base of the whole Combat rotation.",
  "0{Eviscerate} Lvl 1\nFinisher: damage scales with Combo Points. Finishes the mob.",
  "0{Stealth} Lvl 1\nInvisibility, but slows you down a lot at low levels (50%). Only use it against dangerous mobs.",
  "0{Backstab} Lvl 4\nBuilder from behind, only with a dagger in main hand (Dagger).",
  "0{Pick Pocket} Lvl 4\nPickpocket from Stealth: extra coins and loot.",
  "0{Gouge} Lvl 6\nIncapacitates the target and stops auto-attack: time to use a bandage.",
  "0{Evasion} Lvl 8\nMuch higher dodge for a few seconds: use it with several mobs on you.",
  "0{Dual Wield} Lvl 10\nPassive: you can use a weapon in the off-hand. (Before this, only one.)",
  "0{Sap} Lvl 10\nNo longer breaks Stealth: incapacitates a humanoid/elite mob to isolate a pull.",
  "0{Slice and Dice} Lvl 10\nFinisher: increases attack speed for a few seconds. Priority in long fights.",
  "0{Sprint} Lvl 10\nIncreases run speed for a few seconds; with Endurance every 2 minutes.",
  "0{Kick} Lvl 12\nInterrupts casts. Use on casters; costs Energy.",
  "0{Parry} Lvl 12\nPassive: you can parry frontal attacks (needed for Riposte).",
  "0{Expose Armor} Lvl 14\nLike 5 Sunder Armor (and no longer blocks Sunder): only use it if the mob lives for its full duration.",
  "0{Garrote} Lvl 14\nOpener from Stealth with bleed (some mobs are immune). Ignores armor.",
  "0{Feint} Lvl 16\nReduces threat (now doubled): for groups.",
  "0{Pick Lock} Lvl 16\nOpens lockboxes. For the Poison quest you need 80 skill (Pick Lock).",
  "0{Ambush} Lvl 18\nOpener from Stealth with a dagger: big damage. Method: better than Garrote or an early Backstab.",
  "0{Poised} Lvl 18\nPassive: at full Energy and out of combat your first ability costs 10 less Energy.",
  "0{Rupture} Lvl 20\nFinisher with a DoT (ignores armor): for mobs with a lot of armor. In Combat, skip it.",
  "0{Poisons (quest)} Lvl 20\nClass quest: unlocks the Poisons skill + Instant Poison and the Thistle Tea recipe. Then Crippling Poison at 20.",
  "0{Distract} Lvl 22\nDistracts a group and lowers their Stealth detection for 10 s.",
  "0{Vanish} Lvl 22\nLeave combat and re-enter Stealth. Reagent: Flash Powder.",
  "0{Mind-numbing Poison} Lvl 24\nSlows casters' casts (recipe from the Trainer).",
  "0{Shank} Lvl 24\nOff-hand strike (50% damage) that gives back 15 Energy: costs 5 Energy, 10 sec cooldown, cannot miss. Rank 2 at 44 (25 Energy).",
  "0{Cheap Shot} Lvl 26\nStun from Stealth with 2 Combo Points (DonTheCrown: great for farming).",
  "0{Kidney Shot} Lvl 30\nFinisher: stun duration scales with Combo Points.",
  "0{Deadly Poison} Lvl 30\nDoT that stacks up to 5; for long fights. For leveling, almost always Instant Poison.",
  "0{Disarm Trap} Lvl 30\nDisarms traps (useful in dungeons).",
  "0{Wound Poison} Lvl 32\nReduces healing received; mostly useful in PvP.",
  "0{Blind} Lvl 34\nDisorients a target (breaks on damage). Reagent: Blinding Powder. Completes the Rogue's kit.",
  "0{Safe Fall} Lvl 40\nPassive: no fall damage. Same level: Apprentice Riding and Dual Talent Specialization.",
  "0{Efficient Strikes} Lvl 12\nSinister Strike costs 5 less Energy (was Improved Sinister Strike).",
  "0{Riposte} Lvl 22\nTriggers after a Parry: 150% weapon damage and Disarm for 6 s. Put in a macro: /cast Riposte /cast Sinister Strike.",
  "0{Blade Flurry} Lvl 32\n+20% attack speed and hits one extra target for 15 s. 2-minute cooldown with Endurance, paired with Evasion.",
  "0{Hack and Slash} Lvl 35\nPassive: Dagger/Fist +5% crit, Sword/Axe 5% extra hit, Mace ignores 15% armor.",
  "0{Flash of Steel} Lvl 37\nShank gives back more Energy and comes back sooner (5 ranks).",
  "0{Adrenaline Rush} Lvl 42\nEnergy regen +100% for 15 s (20 Energy per second): burst for 3–5 mobs.",
  "0{Human Rogue:} Ruthless: +1% crit to everything (Warcraft Tavern says 2% — sources disagree; the tooltip decides), The Human Spirit +10% Spirit, Perception and Will to Survive mostly for PvP. Warcraft Tavern: best Alliance race in PvE. Mobalytics Rogue's Diary: tier B for leveling speed.",
  "3Other races for the Rogue",
  "0• {Dwarf} (Alliance): Stoneform (10% physical damage, removes Bleed/Poison/Disease), Artisan's Precision +1% Hit, Big Game Hunter +5% vs Beast, Find Treasure (extra chests). More PvP than PvE according to Warcraft Tavern; tier C for speed (Rogue's Diary).",
  "0• {Gnome} (Alliance): Eureka! (10% less Energy and +10% damage for 8 s every 2 min), Expansive Mind +5% max Energy (105), Escape Artist, Engineering Specialization. DonTheCrown: 'my favorite Alliance race'; Rogue's Diary: A-tier for leveling; Warcraft Tavern: 'viable but not the best'.",
  "0• {Night Elf} (Alliance): Elune's Light (+10% crit for 15 s, every 3 min, pairs with Blade Flurry and Adrenaline Rush), Quickness (+1% Dodge, +2% run speed), Shadowmeld usable in combat, Wisp Spirit. Warcraft Tavern: second place in PvE; Rogue's Diary A-tier; Method recommends it (Elune's Light).",
  "0• {Skyborne (High Order)} (Alliance): High Order: Wind Blessed (+2% Haste, the tooltip shows 3% in Warcraft Tavern), Walk on Air (gliding), Read Ley Line (+50% HP/mana regen for 15 s), Elemental Insight (+5% vs Elemental). Weak for the Rogue (Warcraft Tavern, DonTheCrown); Rogue's Diary puts it behind the others.",
  "0• {Orc} (Horde): Blood Fury (+10% Attack Power for 15 s, 3 min) is the best burst; Hardiness (20% stun duration), Shatter Curse. Warcraft Tavern: the best Horde race in PvE; Method recommends it; Rogue's Diary tier B for pure leveling (low mobility/healing).",
  "0• {Undead} (Horde): Cannibalize (35% health from a corpse), Touch of the Grave (20% per hit, drains up to 5% of health), Will of the Forsaken. Method recommends it; Rogue's Diary: less downtime = steady leveling.",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Berserking (+10% haste), Rapid Regeneration (50% HP in 6 s, no corpse needed), Regeneration (20% regen in combat), Beast Slaying (+5% vs Beast). Warcraft Tavern: second in Horde PvE; Rogue's Diary: 'less downtime than almost everyone'.",
  "0• {Skyborne Windshaper} (Horde): Windshapers: Wind Blessed (+2% Haste), Walk on Air, Skysight (+15% speed for 15 s every 2 min; with Elemental Convergence 'Charged' +30% for 1 hour). Rogue's Diary puts it in S-tier for leveling ('nothing comes close'); Warcraft Tavern considers it weak for the Rogue. Sources disagree ; verify in-game.",
  "0Skinning + Mining (or Herbalism) for gold: all the mobs are beasts you can skin, and Mining/Herbalism are the best farms at 60 (Rogue's Diary , DonTheCrown: drop Leatherworking for Mining after 50). Enchanting as a third 'lazy' route for gold in cities.",
  "0Skinning + Leatherworking (Method, Warcraft Tavern, DonTheCrown): budget gear with Agility (Skulker's Leather Belt, Brawler's Leather Belt, Dark Leather Boots, Handstitched Leather Pants/Belt, Embossed Leather Gloves/Cloak), Light Armor Kit, Camp Tent and Camp Chair. DPS alternative: Engineering (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "2Advice for the Rogue",
  "0Secondaries always: Cooking (food +5% XP; Thistle Tea up to ~60 skill), First Aid (bandage with Gouge/Blind/Kidney Shot) and Fishing at 20 for the Fish Bowl. Rogue's Diary: those who only want speed take no professions apart from Cooking/First Aid/Fishing 20. Buy consumables (Elixir of Minor Agility/Strength/Force) at the Auction House: cheap.\nSkinning + Leatherworking: leather from beasts while you do quests (Gfinity). PvP: Engineering + Mining . Sources .",
  "0• {The Horn of Xelthos} · inside the dungeon, solo",
  "2Priorities for the Rogue",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing priority 1\nThe best for a Rogue: +8% to all primary stats (like Blessing of Kings). Fishing 20. Rogue's Diary calls it the best value for money; Method recommends it.",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 2\nRested XP (5% of a level, once an hour, only if you don't already have Rested). For leveling it's very strong; with Skinning + Leatherworking it's the choice of Method and Warcraft Tavern.",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning priority 3\n+2% crit (like Leader of the Pack / Moonkin Aura). Skinning pairs with Leatherworking.",
  "0{Lodestone} · Mining\nAttack Power buff (like Blessing of Might). Ask a miner in your group to set up the camp (Method).",
  "0{Sharpening Wheel} · Blacksmithing\nStrength (like Strength of Earth Totem): fine, but not worth taking Blacksmithing for this.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nLike Mark of the Wild (doesn't stack with a Druid): armor, stats and resists; less useful if you already have a Druid.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nStamina (doesn't stack with Power Word: Fortitude): useful but secondary; you'll learn First Aid anyway.",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring\nSpirit (like Divine Spirit): only for regenerating HP out of combat.",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism\nIntellect: useless for the Rogue (DonTheCrown).",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy\nMana/5: useless (Energy), as DonTheCrown and Warcraft Tavern write.",
  "0{Reagent Bot} · Engineering\nBuy reagents in the field; it doesn't sell the Poison reagents, DonTheCrown writes.",
