  "^spell_shadow_auraofdarkness^Trainer: Bane of Doom",
  "Bane of Doom, Ritual of Doom (Daio the Decrepit, Blasted Lands), Dreadsteed. WGE data = Classic baseline .",
  "Improved Corruption:Affliction;Improved Corruption:Affliction;Improved Corruption:Affliction;Improved Corruption:Affliction;Improved Corruption:Affliction;Suppression:Affliction;Suppression:Affliction;Suppression:Affliction;Suppression:Affliction;Suppression:Affliction;Grim Reach:Affliction;Grim Reach:Affliction;Improved Drains:Affliction;Improved Drains:Affliction;Improved Drains:Affliction;Nightfall:Affliction;Nightfall:Affliction;Fel Concentration:Affliction;Fel Concentration:Affliction;Fel Concentration:Affliction;Soul Siphon:Affliction;Soul Siphon:Affliction;Soul Siphon:Affliction;Pandemic:Affliction;Pandemic:Affliction;Shadow Mastery:Affliction;Shadow Mastery:Affliction;Shadow Mastery:Affliction;Shadow Mastery:Affliction;Shadow Mastery:Affliction;Pandemic:Affliction;Unholy Power:Demonology;Unholy Power:Demonology;Unholy Power:Demonology;Unholy Power:Demonology;Unholy Power:Demonology;Demonic Energies:Demonology;Demonic Energies:Demonology;Malevolence:Affliction;Malevolence:Affliction;Malevolence:Affliction;Malevolence:Affliction;Malevolence:Affliction;Fel Vitality:Demonology;Fel Vitality:Demonology;Fel Vitality:Demonology;Improved Bane of Agony:Affliction;Improved Bane of Agony:Affliction;Soul Harvest:Affliction;Soul Harvest:Affliction;Siphon Life:Affliction",
  "1Talents: Affliction 1–60",
  "0{Choice:} Affliction (drain tank with Voidwalker/Succubus) is the most recommended leveling spec: instant DoTs, Life Tap and Drain Life keep HP and Mana up with no downtime. The talent order is Mobalytics – Crix's (Verified, {337 }, upd. Nov 5, the most-saved Warlock guide): Pandemic at 33–34 and at 40, Siphon Life and Wrack only as free points; it lines up with Warcraft Tavern, Maxroll, wowforeverbuilds and Kargoz (drain tank from 22–30). wowforever.be and Method (Pandemic/Malevolence first, Oct 17) are the minority order, listed in alternatives. Final 41/10/0, close to Icy Veins/Skidrow's 40/11/0.",
  "0{Improved Corruption} 5/5 · lvl 10–14",
  "0{Suppression} 5/5 · lvl 15–19",
  "0{Grim Reach} 2/2 · lvl 20–21",
  "0{Improved Drains} 3/3 · lvl 22–24",
  "0{Nightfall} 2/2 · lvl 25–26",
  "0{Fel Concentration} 3/3 · lvl 27–29",
  "0{Soul Siphon} 3/3 · lvl 30–32",
  "0{Pandemic} 2/3 · lvl 33–34",
  "0{Shadow Mastery} 5/5 · lvl 35–39",
  "0{Pandemic} 3/3 · lvl 40",
  "0{Unholy Power} 5/5 · lvl 41–45",
  "0{Demonic Energies} 2/2 · lvl 46–47",
  "0{Malevolence} 5/5 · lvl 48–52",
  "0{Fel Vitality} 3/3 · lvl 53–55",
  "0{Improved Bane of Agony} 2/2 · lvl 56–57",
  "0{Soul Harvest} 2/2 · lvl 58–59",
  "0{Siphon Life} 1/1 · lvl 60",
  "0Mobalytics – Crix (Verified, 41/10/0) · 337 (the most-saved Warlock guide) · upd. Nov 5 · Improved Corruption 5 (10–14), Suppression 5 (15–19) · Grim Reach 1/2 · Grim Reach 2/2, Improved Drains 3, Nightfall 2, Fel Concentration 3, Soul Siphon from 30; 33–34 Pandemic, 35–39 Shadow Mastery, 40 Pandemic; then Unholy Power, Demonic Energies, Malevolence, Fel Vitality, Improved Bane of Agony; 58–60 free points (Soul Harvest, Siphon Life).",
  "0wowforever.be (client 70707) = Method – Roguery · client data · Method updated Oct 17 · Suppression 4, Improved Corruption 5, Suppression 1 · Pandemic 1/3 · Pandemic 3, Improved Bane of Agony 2, Malevolence 5, Siphon Life 30; 31–33 Fel Concentration, 34 Soul Siphon, 35–39 Shadow Mastery, 40 Wrack. Solo until 40.",
  "0Mobalytics – Kargoz (Affliction 1–60) · 8 · YouTube video 154k views, Oct 3 · 'Wand' build until 22 (DoT + Suppression + Improved Corruption) · Respec to drain tank at 22 · Dedicated drain tank; final 31/7/13 ( WebSearch snippet only)",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Zephan · guide 1–60; talent images from Oct 10; the text still cites Malediction (obsolete) · Improved Corruption 5 + Suppression 4 · Malediction (old)/Improved Bane of Agony/Nightfall · Wand until 29, at 30 respec: Improved Drains, Fel Concentration, Improved Life Tap, Soul Siphon",
  "0Maxroll – Xerwo · updated Oct 30 · Improved Corruption 5, Suppression 4, Unholy Power · Unholy Power 2/5 (Succubus as pet) · Unholy Power 5, Demonic Energies 2, Improved Life Tap 2, Improved Drains 3 (30); does not take Wrack",
  "0wowforeverbuilds (Affliction 1–60) · 6,3k views · updated Oct 24 · Improved Corruption 5, Soul Harvest 2, Grim Reach 2, Suppression 1 · Pandemic 1/3 · Improved Drains 3, Fel Concentration 3, Nightfall 2, Malevolence from 29; Siphon Life 34, Wrack 40",
  "0WoW Forever Guides – Harenil · updated Oct 21 · client 70009 · Improved Corruption 5, Improved Life Tap 2, Improved Drains 3 · Soul Harvest 2 · Fel Concentration 3, Grim Reach 2 + 3 in Affliction; Siphon Life/Soul Siphon 30–34; Wrack 40",
  "0YouTube – Skidrow / Back From AFK · 25,6k views (Oct 5) / 11,3k views (Oct 27) · – · – · Final 40/11/0 (Skidrow) and 35/16/0 (Back From AFK): confirms Affliction with little Demonology",
  "3Alternative order wowforever.be / Method (minority)",
  "0More DoT-crit, drain only from 31: {10–13} Suppression, {14–18} Improved Corruption, {19} Suppression, {20–22} Pandemic, {23–24} Improved Bane of Agony, {25–29} Malevolence, {30} Siphon Life, {31–33} Fel Concentration, {34} Soul Siphon, {35–39} Shadow Mastery, {40} Wrack. Chosen from wowforever.be (client) and Method (Roguery, Oct 17), but Mobalytics Crix (109 ) and almost all the other guides bring Drain forward: we didn't choose that because before 30 Warcraft Tavern says Wand does more damage than Drain Life, and investing in Pandemic/Malevolence without crit pays off little. No source tests it beyond 30.",
  "3Why not Pandemic earlier?",
  "0Pandemic (+100% crit damage of DoTs at 3/3) is worth little without crit: Warcraft Tavern advises against it for leveling. We place it at 34 (1 point) and at 60 (2/3), after Shadow Mastery/Malevolence.",
  "3Demon: Voidwalker or Succubus?",
  "0• {Voidwalker} (10): tank, Torment/Suffering; Sacrifice as an emergency shield. For multiple pulls and mobs that hit hard.",
  "0• {Succubus/Incubus} (20): ~1,5× damage, doesn't hold threat: in drain tanking you take the hits yourself (Tavern, Maxroll).",
  "0• {Imp}: only for Blood Pact in a group.",
  "0• {Felhunter} (30): Spell Lock/Devour Magic, useful vs casters and in PvP.",
  "3Demonology",
  "0Slower until 25; then comfortable: Demonic Brand (Searing Pain marks the target) makes the Succubus/Felhunter hold threat. Core: Suppression 4, Unholy Power 5, Fel Vitality 3, Demonic Energies 2, Master Summoner 2, Demonic Aegis 2, Demonic Brand 3, Demonic Knowledge 3 (Method), Decimation for free Soul Fire. Mobalytics Kargoz (10 , Oct 21) describes it as great for dungeon cleave. Sources: Method, Warcraft Tavern.",
  "3Destruction",
  "0The hardest solo: long casts, mana. Method build: Suppression 4, Bane 5, Aftermath, Ruin, Conflagrate (25), Agonizing Flames, Fire and Brimstone, Bane of Havoc, Shadow and Flame, Incinerate (40). Strong in dungeons with Conflagrate and Shadowburn. Voidwalker in the open world.",
  "3Main trainers",
  "0{Alliance:} Coldridge Valley (Alamar Grimm 28.6,66.2 · demon: Wren Darkspring), Kharanos (Gimrizz Shadowcog 47.2,53.6), Northshire (Drusilla La Salle), Goldshire (Maximillian Crowe 44.4,66.0), Ironforge Forlorn Cavern (Alexander Calder 50.8,6.4), Stormwind Mage Quarter (Demisette Cloyce, Sandahl, Ursula Deline 39.4,85.0; demon: Spackle Thornberry). {Horde:} Valley of Trials (Nartok 40.6,68.4), Razor Hill (Dhugru Gorelust 54.2,41.2), Orgrimmar Cleft of Shadow (Grol'dar, Mirket, Zevrost), Deathknell (Maximillion), Brill (Rupert Boch), Undercity Magic Quarter (Kaal Soulreaper, Luther Pickman, Richard Kerwin), Stonard (Kartosh). Source: Warcraft Tavern; NPCs verified on the Wowhead Forever map.",
  "3Warlock dungeons",
  "0Hall of Thanes 13–18, Ragefire Chasm 13–18, Ruins of Lordaeron 15–20, Wailing Caverns 17–24, The Deadmines 17–26, Shadowfang Keep 22–30, Blackfathom Deeps 24–32, The Stockade 24–32, Excavation Site 24–29, Gnomeregan 29–38 (Wowhead Forever map). Gear: Hall of Thanes (Golemheart Stave, Ephemeral Choker, Robes of the Disgraced Thane), Ragefire (Robe of Evocation, Crystalline Cuffs), Deadmines (Emberstone Staff, Cookie's Stirring Rod) – Maxroll. Dungeon quest XP is 50% from Oct 1.",
  "31–9 · Imp + Immolate + Wand",
  "0^spell_fire_immolation,spell_shadow_abominationexplosion,spell_shadow_shadowbolt,ability_marksmanship^Immolate -> Corruption (4) -> Shadow Bolt -> Wand",
  "0Summon the Imp, open with Immolate (buy it at level 1 from the Trainer, 10 copper), then Corruption from 4. Finish with Wand or auto-attack until you have the Wand. Shadow Bolt costs too much: use it to finish. Sell the starting gear to pay for Immolate. Life Tap from 6 (then eat), Bane of Agony from 8 to tag.",
  "310–19 · Voidwalker + DoT + Wand",
  "0^spell_shadow_summonvoidwalker,spell_shadow_curseofsargeras,spell_shadow_abominationexplosion,spell_fire_immolation,ability_marksmanship^Pet attack -> Bane of Agony -> Corruption -> Immolate -> Wand",
  "0Pet attack, then Bane of Agony (tags, the demon takes the threat), Corruption (instant at 14 with Improved Corruption 5/5), Immolate if the mob lives >8 s. Finish with the Wand, which does more damage than Drain Life until 29. Life Tap between pulls. Drain Soul for the last hit when you need Soul Shards.",
  "320–29 · Succubus and Drain",
  "0^spell_shadow_summonsuccubus,spell_shadow_curseofsargeras,spell_shadow_abominationexplosion,spell_shadow_lifedrain02,spell_shadow_burningspirit^Pet attack -> Bane of Agony -> Corruption -> Drain Life -> Life Tap",
  "0From 20 you can use the Succubus (more damage but doesn't hold threat: you take the hits). With Grim Reach, Improved Drains and Fel Concentration (20–29) use Drain Life when you need health; otherwise Wand. Warcraft Tavern's rule: more Health than Mana -> Life Tap; more Mana than Health -> Drain Life. Shadow Bolt only with the Nightfall proc.",
  "330+ · Drain tanking",
  "0^spell_shadow_summonsuccubus,spell_shadow_curseofsargeras,spell_shadow_abominationexplosion,spell_shadow_requiem,spell_shadow_lifedrain02^Pet attack -> Bane of Agony -> Corruption -> Siphon Life -> Drain Life",
  "0From 30, Drain Life Rank 3 + Soul Siphon (+12% per DoT on the target) make Drain your filler: DoTs, then Drain Life until death; Wand only at full HP or on an almost dead mob. Siphon Life and Wrack only if you pick them as free points (58–60).",
  "3Multiple pulls",
  "0^spell_shadow_possession,spell_shadow_abominationexplosion,spell_shadow_summonvoidwalker,spell_shadow_lifedrain02^Fear -> DoT on the 1st -> Demon on the 2nd -> Drain",
  "0After 22: DoT the first mob and Fear, the demon holds the second; return to the first when it's back. With Fel Concentration 3/3 you can drain while being hit. Use a focus target for DoTs. If Fear runs toward another group, break it with Curse of Recklessness.",
  "3AoE",
  "0^spell_shadow_abominationexplosion,spell_shadow_curseofsargeras,spell_fire_incinerate,spell_shadow_rainoffire^Corruption on all -> Bane of Agony -> Hellfire (30) -> Rain of Fire (20)",
  "03+ mobs: DoTs on all and Hellfire/Rain of Fire (Maxroll), but watch your HP. Only Destruction has scalable AoE. Prefer the Voidwalker for big pulls.",
  "3Health/Mana management",
  "0Health and mana are a single resource: {Life Tap} converts HP into Mana, {Drain Life} gives them back. Keep Demon Skin/Armor up. Stamina matters a bit more than for other casters. First Aid: bandage between pulls or while a mob is feared, then Life Tap. Always keep a Healthstone (separate cooldown). Sources: Warcraft Tavern, Method.",
  "3Soul Shard",
  "0Needed for Voidwalker, Succubus/Incubus, Felhunter, Healthstone, Soulstone, Ritual of Summoning, Shadowburn. While your demon tanks, channel {Drain Soul Rank 1} to make shards . Bags: Small Soul Pouch (14 slots, Succubus quest), Box of Souls (16, Felhunter quest); the Soul Shard Bag now goes in the reagent slot (Warcraft Tavern, forg.gg).",
  "3Useful macros (GuideMMO, 15k views, Oct 31)",
  "0• #showtooltip /castsequence reset=combat/target Immolate, Bane of Agony, Corruption",
  "0• /cast [nochanneling] Drain Life",
  "0• /cast [@mouseover] Fear",
  "0A comment on the video warns: don't put Pet Attack in the same macro as an offensive spell; keep Pet commands on separate keys (scroll wheel). The Move command is new .",
  "3When to go to the Trainer",
  "0Rank levels: Corruption 4/14/24/34, Life Tap 6/16/26/36, Drain Life 14/22/30/38, Bane of Agony 8/18/28/38, Shadow Bolt 6/12/20/28/36. Demon Grimoires (Imp/Voidwalker/Succubus/Felhunter) are bought from the Demon Trainer and are expensive (Method). Levels from the Wowhead Forever tooltips.",
  "0Leveling priority: Spell Power/Shadow Damage > Wand DPS (until 30) > Intellect/Spirit > Stamina (Warcraft Tavern; Maxroll: Spellpower, Intellect, Spirit; Spirit scales Life Tap). The main-hand is a 'stat stick': Spell Power matters, not its damage. Wands: Novice's Practice Wand (1), Lesser Magic Wand (5, ~11,3 DPS), Greater Magic Wand (13, ~17,5 DPS), Gravestone Scepter (Blackfathom Deeps, 29 DPS), Greater Mystic Wand (30). Weapons: Staff of Soran'ruk or Orb of Soran'ruk (quest 20), Staff of the Shade (Razorfen Kraul, rare drop), Golemheart Stave (Hall of Thanes), Emberstone Staff and Cookie's Stirring Rod (Deadmines) (Maxroll). Wands no longer benefit from Spell Power .",
  "0• DoTs (Corruption, Bane of Agony, Siphon Life, Drain...) can crit: Pandemic and Malevolence increase their value (Method Oct 17; wowforeverbuilds Oct 24).",
  "0• Bane of Agony (level 8) replaces Curse of Agony: instant and tags the mob. Curse and Bane are separate: one of each per target (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• Life Tap scales with Spirit: converts (30 + Spirit) HP into Mana (client Wowhead Forever tooltip).",
  "0• Drain Soul can give a Soul Shard on each tick; a non-trivial mob killed = guaranteed shard (Warcraft Tavern, WoW Forever Guides on client 70009).",
  "0• Soul Shard Bag in the reagent slot; Small Soul Pouch 14 slots (was 12), Box of Souls 16 slots (forg.gg).",
  "0• Fear now has 20 yd (was 24 in beta): Blizzard forum via wowforeverbuilds. Still one target, 10 s.",
  "0• Incubus as a separate demon from the Succubus (Sayaad) with its own quest chain (forg.gg Oct 9).",
  "0• The Meeting Stone no longer summons: only Ritual of Summoning (Method, Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0• New/changed talents in client 70707: Improved Corruption (Changed), Suppression (Changed: +1% Hit and 4% threat per rank), Pandemic, Malevolence, Soul Harvest, Improved Drains, Wrack (New), Soul Siphon, Fel Concentration, Siphon Life (Changed), Demonic Energies, Demonic Brand, Decimation (New).",
  "0• Grim Reach (2 ranks) replaced Malediction 5/5 in the Oct 15 notes; Soul Harvesting was renamed Soul Harvest on Oct 1 (WoW Forever Guides, Harenil Oct 21).",
  "0• Voidwalker: Torment +threat for 5 levels after each new Rank, then fixed; from 25 to 30 it loses mobs more often until Torment Rank 3 (30). Sacrifice scales with 10% of spell healing (notes Sep 24).",
  "0• Wands no longer scale with Spell Power: Wand DPS matters until 30 (Warcraft Tavern, WoW Forever Guides).",
  "0• Legacy (unconfirmed, wowforeverbuilds Oct 24): Talented (5 points) gives talents from level 5 instead of 10; Well Rested; Thrill of Adventure (5% HP/mana per kill).",
  "0• Not found: Dark Pact is not in the beta tables (WoW Forever Guides ).",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): demons get 2 health per point of your Stamina instead of 7.5 (a less sturdy Voidwalker), Wrack deals more (86 per second at 60), Shadow and Flame up to 20%, Spellstones raise only Shadow damage, and Drain Soul gives a Soul Shard much less often when the mob does not die.",
  "0{Demon Skin} Lvl 1\nArmor buff (+40) and +3 HP/5 s for 30 min: keep it always up (Demon Armor from 20).",
  "0{Summon Imp} Lvl 1\nThe first demon, from the racial class quest (level 1–4). Firebolt at range and Blood Pact from 4 (Stamina to the group).",
  "0{Shadow Bolt} Lvl 1\nRank 2 at 6, Rank 3 at 12, Rank 4 at 20, Rank 5 at 28, Rank 6 at 36. Expensive: before 14 use the Wand.",
  "0{Immolate} Lvl 1\nFrom the Trainer for 10 copper: learn it right away. Rank 2 at 10, Rank 3 at 20, Rank 4 at 30. Only on mobs that live >8 s.",
  "0{Corruption} Lvl 4\nShadow DoT 12 s, 2 s cast until Improved Corruption 5/5 (14). Rank 2 at 14, Rank 3 at 24, Rank 4 at 34.",
  "0{Curse of Weakness} Lvl 4\nReduces attack power: useful against melee mobs that hit hard. Rank 2 at 12, Rank 3 at 22.",
  "0{Life Tap} Lvl 6\nConverts HP into Mana (30 + Spirit): Spirit really matters. Rank 2 at 16, Rank 3 at 26.",
  "0{Bane of Agony} Lvl 8\nReplaces Curse of Agony: instant, tags the mob and does little damage at first (the demon takes the threat). 72 dmg in 24 s; Rank 2 at 18, Rank 3 at 28.",
  "0{Fear} Lvl 8\nRange 20 yd (was 24 in beta). 10 s, 1 target, damage can break it. Rank 2 at 32.",
  "0{Drain Soul} Lvl 10\nEach tick has a chance to give a Soul Shard; a non-trivial mob killed with Drain Soul always gives a shard. Rank 2 at 24.",
  "0{Create Healthstone} Lvl 10\nEmergency heal (Minor: 120 HP) with its own cooldown. Costs a Soul Shard. Rank 2 at 22, Rank 3 at 34.",
  "0{Summon Voidwalker} Lvl 10\nLevel 10 class quest (see Milestones). Torment/Suffering/Sacrifice: your tank.",
  "0{Health Funnel} Lvl 12\nChannels HP to the demon. With Demonic Energies you'll use less of it.",
  "0{Drain Life} Lvl 14\nChanneled 5 s: 10 HP/s from the target (Rank 2 at 22, Rank 3 at 30 = drain tanking Rank).",
  "0{Curse of Recklessness} Lvl 14\nLess armor and the mob doesn't flee at low HP. Rank 2 at 28. Now it's a Curse (one per Warlock, in addition to Bane).",
  "0{Unending Breath} Lvl 16\nUnderwater breathing for 10 min: needed for underwater quests.",
  "0{Searing Pain} Lvl 18\nShort cast, high threat. Only for Demonology with Demonic Brand; otherwise it takes the mob off your demon.",
  "0{Create Soulstone} Lvl 18\nIn-combat resurrection on yourself or an ally (Rank 2 at 30).",
  "0{Summon Succubus} Lvl 20\nLevel 20 class quest: the demon that does the most damage (~1,5× Voidwalker). Without Demonology talents it doesn't hold threat.",
  "0{Summon Incubus} Lvl 20\nMale version of the Succubus with its own quest chain (same abilities).",
  "0{Demon Armor} Lvl 20\nImproved version of Demon Skin (Rank 2 at 30, Rank 3 at 40).",
  "0{Ritual of Summoning} Lvl 20\nThe only way to summon players: needs 2 companions and 1 Soul Shard (the Meeting Stone no longer summons).",
  "0{Curse of the Elements} Lvl 20\n30 Magic resistance and +4% Magic damage taken for 5 min (Rank 2 at 30). The client gives it at 20 (Classic: 32) .",
  "0{Rain of Fire} Lvl 20\nChanneled AoE, the only one with true area damage (Rank 2 at 34).",
  "0{Eye of Kilrogg} Lvl 22\nFlying exploration eye.",
  "0{Drain Mana} Lvl 24\nDrains mana from casters (Rank 2 at 34).",
  "0{Sense Demons} Lvl 24\nTracks demons on the minimap.",
  "0{Curse of Tongues} Lvl 26\nSlows casters' casting (Rank 2 at 50).",
  "0{Detect Invisibility} Lvl 26\nSee invisible mobs (Rank 2 at 38).",
  "0{Banish} Lvl 28\nRemoves a Demon or Elemental from combat; damage doesn't interrupt it.",
  "0{Create Firestone} Lvl 28\nFire weapon stone; for Destruction/Demonology.",
  "0{Summon Felhunter} Lvl 30\nLevel 30 class quest (Seeking Strahad, Ratchet). Spell Lock (36), Devour Magic.",
  "0{Subjugate Demon} Lvl 30\n(was Enslave Demon) Controls a demon up to level 45; costs 1 Soul Shard.",
  "0{Hellfire} Lvl 30\nAoE around you that also damages you: manage your HP.",
  "0{Siphon Life} Lvl 30\nAffliction talent-spell (150 mana, 30 yd, 30 s): heals 11 HP every 3 s. Unlocked by the talent.",
  "0{Shadow Ward} Lvl 32\nAbsorbs Shadow damage (Rank 2 at 42).",
  "0{Create Spellstone} Lvl 36\nWeapon stone: Spell Haste and Shadow damage (Maxroll).",
  "0{Summon Felsteed} Lvl 40\nMount from class quest (Trainer in capital -> Strahad Farsan, Ratchet).",
  "0{Wrack} Lvl 40\nCapstone Affliction, channeled 6 s.",
  "0{Howl of Terror} Lvl 40\nAoE Fear.",
  "0{Death Coil} Lvl 42\nInstant escape: the target flees and it heals you for the damage dealt.",
  "0{Soul Fire} Lvl 48\nLong cast, high damage (Decimation makes it free). Rank 2 at 56.",
  "0{Inferno} Lvl 50\nLevel 50 class quest: Infernal (Niby the Almighty, Felwood).",
  "0{Bane of Doom} Lvl 60\nNew Bane from 60; Ritual of Doom and Dreadsteed from 60 (post-launch).",
  "0{Nightfall (proc)} Lvl 26\nShadow Trance: the next Shadow Bolt is instant. Spend it right away.",
  "0{Siphon Life} Lvl 60\nDoT that heals you; use it on mobs that live at least 2/3 of its duration (Warcraft Tavern).",
  "0{Wrack (not in build)} Lvl 40\nChanneled 6 s: +10% to your other Shadow DoTs.",
  "0{Amplify Curse (not in build)} Lvl 20\nNext Curse of Weakness/Bane of Agony +50%: optional choice (Affliction row 3).",
  "0{Curse of Exhaustion (not in build)} Lvl 25\n30% slow for 12 s, the Warlock's only slow (requires Amplify Curse).",
  "0{Human Warlock:} Human (Alliance): Ruthless (+crit, 2% according to Method), The Human Spirit (+Spirit, scales Life Tap), Will to Survive, Perception. Method: tier S. Sword Specialization was removed (the Warcraft Tavern guide is outdated on this).",
  "3Other races for the Warlock",
  "0• {Gnome} (Alliance): Gnome (Alliance): Expansive Mind (+5% mana), Eureka! (10% mana and +10% damage on non-periodic spells for 8 s: useless for Affliction), Escape Artist, Engineering Specialization. Method: tier B, the weakest for Affliction.",
  "0• {Orc} (Horde): Orc (Horde): Command (+5% Pet damage, Warcraft Tavern ), Blood Fury (+Spell Power), Shatter Curse (removes Curse/Bane and reduces Magic damage), Hardiness (20% stun duration). Method: tier A; Maxroll recommends the Orc as Horde.",
  "0• {Undead} (Horde): Undead (Horde): Cannibalize (7% HP+MP per second for 10 s on Humanoid/Undead corpses : less food/drink), Touch of the Grave (damage that heals you, including the DoTs' initial hit), Will of the Forsaken (removes Fear/Charm/Sleep, not immune), Underwater Breathing. Method: tier B, great for self-sustain.",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Troll (Horde, new Warlock ): Berserking (+10% haste, doesn't apply to DoTs), Rapid Regeneration (channel that heals, great with Life Tap), Regeneration (HP regen in combat), Beast Slaying (+5% damage to Beasts, useful in the Barrens). Method: tier C. Starts in the Valley of Trials like the Orc.",
  "0Herbalism + Skinning (or Mining): sells well at the Auction House and each Rank pays off; Skinning also gives the Camp Chair. Cooking (food with XP buff + needed for the Basic Campfire) and First Aid (bandage + Life Tap) for everyone. Sources: Warcraft Tavern, Method.",
  "0Tailoring + Enchanting: agreed by Method, Warcraft Tavern, Maxroll . Tailoring makes BoP gear with Shadow/Fire Damage (Filigreed Shadow Gown for Affliction, Filigreed Flame Gown for Destro/Demo; Shadow Gown and Shadow Gloves with Merchant's Favor) and the Faction Banner (Spirit); Enchanting makes Lesser/Greater Magic Wand, staves and disenchants crafted pieces.",
  "2Advice for the Warlock",
  "0For power: Tailoring + Enchanting on the main. For gold: Herbalism + Skinning with a bank alt doing Tailoring/Enchanting. Cooking, First Aid and Fishing for everyone.\nTailoring + Enchanting in leveling. Economy and raids: Herbalism + Alchemy (Gfinity). Sources .",
  "0• {The Orb of Soran'ruk} · inside the dungeon",
  "2Priorities for the Warlock",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP (up to 5% of a level, 1 time/hour): the best overall for leveling; the Warlock has little downtime and benefits from it.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing priority 2\n+8% to all stats: Stamina (more HP = more Life Tap), Intellect and Spirit together. Great for the Warlock.",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring priority 3\nSpirit (up to +32 in the Mage guide): in the client Life Tap scales with Spirit . Maxroll recommends it with Tailoring.",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism\nIntellect (up to +25): bigger mana pool. Does not stack with Arcane Intellect.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nStamina (up to +56): more HP for Life Tap and drain tanking. Does not stack with Power Word: Fortitude.",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning\n+2% crit: DoTs can crit (Malevolence, Pandemic). Good, not essential.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nArmor/stats/resistances: little for a cloth caster. Maxroll mentions it mainly because Enchanting gives Wands.",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy\nmana/5: not very useful, Life Tap and Drain Life already give you all the mana.",
