  "0wowforever.be – leveling build (client 1.60.1.70707) · client data · 10–14 Thundering Strikes 5/5 · 15–17 Mental Dexterity 3/3 · 18–19 Improved Ghost Wolf 2/2 · Shamanistic Focus · 21–23 Elemental Weapons · 24 Ancestral Knowledge · 25 Stormstrike · 26–29 Flurry · 30 Spirit Weapons",
  "0Mobalytics – Shaman Leveling Guide 1-60 (Tiqqle) · 175 · Verified · upd. Nov 6 · 10–14 Thundering Strikes · 15–17 Mental Dexterity · 18–19 Ancestral Knowledge · Shamanistic Focus · 21–23 Elemental Weapons · 24 Ancestral Knowledge · 25 Stormstrike · 26–27 Improved Ghost Wolf · 28–29 Flurry · 30 Improved Stormstrike · then Resto: 32–36 Tidal Focus, 37–39 Mindfulness, 40–41 Totemic Focus, 42 Water Shield",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Shaman Leveling (Shadostruct) · Oct 2026 · beta build, image (26 points) · level order not given · — · Final build: Thundering Strikes 5, Mental Dexterity 3, Improved Ghost Wolf 2, Improved Lightning Shield 1, Shamanistic Focus 1, Elemental Weapons 3, Stormstrike 1, Flurry 5, Mental Quickness 2, Improved Stormstrike 2, Maelstrom Weapon 1",
  "0Method – Shaman Leveling Guide (Erik) · updated Oct 23 · Improved Ghost Wolf 2/2 before 20 · Ghost Wolf · Stormstrike at 25; Windfury Weapon at 30; full order not given",
  "0Icy Veins – Enhancement Shaman Leveling (WebSearch snippet only) · snippet, page not read · Starts Restoration (Mindfulness, Water Shield) for Mana · Water Shield · Respec at 25 for Stormstrike; Improved Stormstrike core; Spirit Weapons",
  "0Mobalytics – Shaman Leveling 1-60 (NickTew) · 67 · Creator · upd. Nov 4 · Thundering Strikes 5/5, Mental Dexterity 3/3 · — · 6/34/11 at 60: like Tiqqle, eleven points in Restoration for Water Shield",
  "3Water Shield first (Restoration 10–20, then Enhancement)",
  "0{Sources:} Mobalytics Tiqqle «1-60 Water Shield First» (same build as A at 60, different order), Icy Veins (snippet ), Gaunerh \"3 Builds to Level 35\" (14k views, Oct 28).",
  "0• First the eleven Restoration points (Tidal Focus, Mindfulness, Totemic Focus) and {Water Shield} at 20: more Mana in the early levels.",
  "0• Then Enhancement: Stormstrike only at 36 instead of 25.",
  "0• No respec: at 60 it's the same build as A.",
  "3Elemental",
  "0Tavern: more mana-hungry and no melee as a fallback. Lava Burst was removed on 3 Nov (Call of Thunder replaces it) and Lightning Overload is new . Mobalytics has an Elemental 1-30 guide by Tiqqle (10 ). Less suited to solo leveling.",
  "3Restoration",
  "0Tavern: suboptimal for leveling; at 40 there's Dual Spec and you can keep a Restoration spec for dungeons. Doomsong Forever guide (8.8k views, Oct 20) for Restoration 1–60.",
  "3Other 60 builds (not read in full)",
  "0Skidrow (84k views, Oct 1): Enhancement 18/33/0 (17/34/0 with Orc + Arcanite Reaper). Back From AFK (11k views, Oct 28): 51-point route. Defcamp & Melderon (83k, Sep 14): Enhancement build with an Elemental or Restoration sub-spec.",
  "31–9 · Lightning Bolt + Rockbiter",
  "0^spell_nature_rockbiter,spell_nature_lightning,spell_nature_earthshock,inv_sword_04^Rockbiter Weapon -> Lightning Bolt -> Earth Shock (from 4) -> Melee",
  "0Rockbiter Weapon on the weapon. Open with Lightning Bolt from max range; from 4, cast Earth Shock right as the Bolt finishes (the GCD is already ready). Then finish in melee. From 4, the Call of Earth quest gives you Stoneskin Totem and the Earth Totem in Bag (needed for Earthbind at 6 and Stoneclaw at 8). Lightning Shield from 8. (Tavern, Method)",
  "310–19 · Flame Shock + Searing Totem",
  "0^spell_nature_lightning,spell_fire_flameshock,spell_fire_searingtotem,inv_sword_04,spell_nature_earthshock^Lightning Bolt (pull) -> Flame Shock -> Searing Totem -> Melee -> Earth Shock",
  "0Pull with Lightning Bolt, Flame Shock (refresh it only when it's about to expire), Searing Totem, melee and Earth Shock when it's ready. Fire Nova (12) when the Totem is active and mobs are close. Searing Totem comes with Call of Fire (quest from 10, but the mobs arrive at 14: Tavern suggests grouping or waiting). Before 20 get Improved Ghost Wolf 2/2. Method: you usually pull one mob at a time.",
  "320–24 · Ghost Wolf and cheap shocks",
  "0^spell_fire_flameshock,spell_fire_searingtotem,spell_nature_earthshock,spell_frost_frostshock^Flame Shock -> Searing Totem -> Earth Shock -> Frost Shock (slow)",
  "0Shamanistic Focus (20) cuts the cost of Shock and Lightning Shield by 45%: now you can spam shocks. Frost Shock to slow fleeing mobs; Earth Shock to interrupt casts. Instant Ghost Wolf to move. Rockbiter Weapon Rank 4 at 24 (+194 AP, +20% with Elemental Weapons 3/3).",
  "325–30 · Stormstrike",
  "0^ability_shaman_stormstrike,spell_nature_earthshock,spell_fire_flameshock,spell_fire_searingtotem^Stormstrike (8 s) -> Earth Shock -> Flame Shock -> Searing Totem",
  "0Stormstrike on every cooldown, then Earth Shock (or Lightning Bolt) with the +20%. Keep up Flame Shock and Searing Totem. Flurry (28–29) speeds up your hits after a crit. At 30 switch to Windfury Weapon and a 2H (Method); Improved Stormstrike from 31 for Mana.",
  "3Multiple pulls / AoE",
  "0^spell_nature_strengthofearthtotem02,spell_fire_selfdestruct,spell_fire_sealoffire,spell_nature_chainlightning^Earthbind Totem -> Magma Totem (26) -> Fire Nova -> Chain Lightning (32)",
  "02–3 mobs: Fire Nova (burst, the threat goes to you and not the Totem) with Searing Totem active. 3+ mobs: Magma Totem (26). Earthbind to stop fleeing mobs or to kite. Stoneclaw Totem only to buy a few seconds.",
  "0^inv_drink_08,spell_nature_manaregentotem,spell_nature_magicimmunity^Drink -> Mana Spring (26) -> Healing Wave",
  "0Mana is the Shaman's limit (Tavern). Keep Drink of the right level and drink between pulls; use Shamanistic Focus, Improved Stormstrike and Maelstrom Weapon. After a pull heal with Healing Wave if you have Mana, otherwise First Aid. Lightning Shield always active.",
  "3Totems: you need the items in Bag",
  "0To cast a Totem you need the element's item {in Bag} (Earth Totem from the quest at 4, Fire Totem at 10, Water Totem at 20, Air Totem at 30). Without the Fire Totem you have neither Searing Totem nor Fire Nova. (Tavern)",
  "3Why Rockbiter until 30",
  "0Method: Rockbiter Weapon gives a lot of AP at these levels and is much better than Flametongue and Frostbrand. From 30 switch to Windfury Weapon with a 2H (Elemental Weapons gives +40% to its bonus).",
  "3Tank with 1H + shield (optional)",
  "0Method: you can tank dungeons with 1H + shield; Rockbiter and Earth Shock generate threat. wowforever.be (classes): Enhancement is designed for 2H only. For solo leveling: 2H.",
  "3Elemental rotation (alternative)",
  "0• Lightning Shield, Searing Totem/Magma Totem, Mana Spring Totem.",
  "0• Lightning Bolt as filler.",
  "0Tavern: more serious Mana problems and balance still in flux.",
  "0Divergent priorities : Method (Erik) Agility > Strength > Stamina > Intellect; Tavern Hit/Expertise > Strength > Intellect > Critical Strike > Spell Damage > Agility. In Forever Mental Dexterity turns Intellect into AP and Mental Quickness into spell damage, so Strength + Intellect makes sense. Weapon: 2H only (wowforever.be, no dual wield); Rockbiter until 30, then Windfury. Call of Air: Tavern mentions Rage of the Storm (2H Mace, ilvl 40, +12 Intellect +15 Stamina from warcraftdb) for Enhancement ; Lightning's Grasp (Elemental) and Tidebringer's Claw (Resto) for the others. Dwarf weapon trainers in Ironforge: Buliwyf Stonehand (fist, 1H/2H axes, 2H mace), Bixi Wobblebonk (daggers); base mace and staff (Tavern). Dwarf's Mace Specialization was removed (Oct 26).",
  "0• Alliance Shaman: Dwarf only; new trainers Teo Hammerstorm, Ingrid Dunwald, Eldrun Stormbreaker (wowforever.be, wmd.json ).",
  "0• New Enhancement talents: Mental Dexterity, Shamanistic Focus, Mental Quickness, Improved Stormstrike, Maelstrom Weapon, Rage of the Farseer; Elemental: Lightning Overload, Earthbound (Lava Burst removed on 3 Nov, Call of Thunder is back); Resto: Water Shield, Riptide, Mindfulness (client wowforever.be).",
  "0• Stormstrike is a talent at 25 (Tavern); Rage of the Farseer is the personal \"Bloodlust\" at 40 (Method).",
  "0• Totem twisting removed; Call of the Elements, Call of the Ancestors, Totemic Recall, Totemic Projection (Totemic Call since 3 Nov) and Astral Recall arrive, with a 15 min cooldown (Tavern).",
  "0• Improved Ghost Wolf: Ghost Wolf is instant and usable indoors (Method, Tavern).",
  "0• Enhancement is 2H only, no dual wield (wowforever.be, Skidrow).",
  "0• Talents: 51 points from level 10, milestones at 11/21/31 points, a new one at 16; respec at the Trainer in a capital; Dual Spec at 40 (wowforever.be).",
  "0• Racials Oct 26–27 (Blizzard via Warcraft Tavern): Dwarf Artisan's Precision, Orc without Axe Spec/Savage, Troll Berserking 15 s, Orc Blood Fury 2 min.",
  "0• Tavern: the builds are designed for the Beta cap 30; the 60 builds will arrive at launch. Pre-launch data.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): Earth Shock, Flame Shock and Frost Shock go back to Classic damage; Lightning Bolt deals more; Stormstrike 150% weapon damage and 6 sec cooldown; Maelstrom Weapon triggers twice as often; Mental Dexterity up to 150% of Intellect as Attack Power; Riptide heals over time only, 12 sec cooldown.",
  "0{Lightning Bolt} Lvl 1\nYour ranged attack to open the pull (14–17 damage Rank 1). Rank 2 at 8, 3 at 14, 4 at 20, 5 at 26, 6 at 32.",
  "0{Rockbiter Weapon} Lvl 1\nWeapon imbue: +50 AP and more threat (Rank 1). It stays your imbue until 30 (Method: much better than Flametongue/Frostbrand). Rank 2 at 8 (+79 AP), 3 at 16 (+118), 4 at 24 (+194).",
  "0{Healing Wave} Lvl 1\nSlow direct heal (37–47 Rank 1) between pulls. Rank 2 at 6, 3 at 12, 4 at 18, 5 at 24, 6 at 32. levels from the Wowhead Forever tooltip.",
  "0{Earth Shock} Lvl 4\nInstant: damage, interrupt, taunt. Cast it as soon as Lightning Bolt finishes. Rank 2 at 8, 3 at 14, 4 at 24, 5 at 36.",
  "0{Stoneskin Totem} Lvl 4\nReduces Physical damage (4 Rank 1). Comes with the Call of Earth class quest (which gives the Earth Totem in Bag). Rank 2 at 14, 3 at 24.",
  "0{Earthbind Totem} Lvl 6\nAoE slow 10 yd for 45 s: kiting and mobs that flee. With the Earthbound talent it roots them for 5 s.",
  "0{Stoneclaw Totem} Lvl 8\n50-health totem that taunts nearby mobs for 15 s: buys you a few seconds.",
  "0{Lightning Shield} Lvl 8\nAlways active (3 orbs). With Shamanistic Focus it costs 45% less. Rank 2 at 16, Rank 3 at 24.",
  "0{Flame Shock} Lvl 10\nFire shock with a 12 s DoT: refresh it only when it's about to expire. Rank 2 at 18, Rank 3 at 28.",
  "0{Searing Totem} Lvl 10\nLearned with the Call of Fire class quest: a totem that attacks for you (9–11 Fire Rank 1). Rank 2 at 20, 3 at 30. Requires the Fire Totem in Bag.",
  "0{Flametongue Weapon} Lvl 10\nFire imbue: Rockbiter is better for now. Rank 2 at 18, Rank 3 at 26.",
  "0{Strength of Earth Totem} Lvl 10\n+7 Strength to the group (Rank 1), +14 at Rank 2 (24): you use it yourself (Tavern: keep it up in combat).",
  "0{Fire Nova} Lvl 12\nAoE around the Fire Totem, also good on a single target (Method: your AoE burst). Rank 2 at 22, Rank 3 at 32. Requires an active Fire Totem.",
  "0{Purge} Lvl 12\nRemoves 1 magic buff at range, instant.",
  "0{Ancestral Spirit} Lvl 12\nOut-of-combat resurrection.",
  "0{Cure Poison} Lvl 16\nRemoves 1 Poison from an ally.",
  "0{Tremor Totem} Lvl 18\nRemoves Fear, Charm and Sleep from the group.",
  "0{Ghost Wolf} Lvl 20\n+40% speed. With Improved Ghost Wolf 2/2 (from 27) it's instant and works indoors: your \"mount\" until 40 (Method: the best from 20 to 39).",
  "0{Frost Shock} Lvl 20\n50% slow at range (68–73 Frost Rank 1) to escape or keep mobs away. Rank 2 at 34.",
  "0{Frostbrand Weapon} Lvl 20\nFrost imbue with a 25% slow. Rank 2 at 28. Less useful than Rockbiter for now.",
  "0{Healing Stream Totem} Lvl 20\nComes with the Call of Water class quest: heals the group (5 every 2 s Rank 1).",
  "0{Lesser Healing Wave} Lvl 20\nFast, expensive heal (151–172): for emergencies.",
  "0{Call of the Elements} Lvl 20\nDrops up to 4 totems from your Totem Bar with one key (totem twisting no longer exists).",
  "0{Totemic Recall} Lvl 20\nRecalls the totems and gives you back Mana.",
  "0{Totemic Call} Lvl 22\nBrings your active totems to where you stand (30 sec cooldown). It used to be called Totemic Projection.",
  "0{Cure Disease} Lvl 22\nRemoves 1 Disease from an ally.",
  "0{Poison Cleansing Totem} Lvl 22\nRemoves Poison from the group in pulses.",
  "0{Frost Resistance Totem} Lvl 24\nFrost resistance (Fire Totem slot): for specific zones/dungeons.",
  "0{Magma Totem} Lvl 26\nPulsing AoE (20 Fire every 2 s for 20 s) for pulls of 3+ mobs.",
  "0{Mana Spring Totem} Lvl 26\nRestores Mana (4 every 2 s Rank 1) to you and the group: stay put to camp or in dungeons.",
  "0{Fire Resistance Totem} Lvl 28\nFire resistance (Water Totem slot).",
  "0{Flametongue Totem} Lvl 28\nIncreases the group's spell damage (Fire Totem).",
  "0{Windfury Weapon} Lvl 30\nFrom 30 you switch to 2H + Windfury Weapon: 20% chance of 2 extra attacks (Method).",
  "0{Grounding Totem} Lvl 30\nAbsorbs one enemy spell every 10 s.",
  "0{Nature Resistance Totem} Lvl 30\nNature resistance.",
  "0{Call of the Ancestors} Lvl 30\nSecond Totem Bar: another set of 4 totems with one key.",
  "0{Reincarnation} Lvl 30\nPassive: you rise from death (requires an Ankh in Bag).",
  "0{Astral Recall} Lvl 30\nSecond Hearthstone with a 15 min cooldown (Tavern); same home. level 30 from the tooltip.",
  "0{Chain Lightning} Lvl 32\n31–60: Lightning Bolt that chains (85–97 Rank 1).",
  "0{Windfury Totem} Lvl 32\n31–60: Windfury for the whole group (Tavern: huge).",
  "0{Frost Shock (Rank 2)} Lvl 34\n31–60: 126–135 Frost.",
  "0{Earth Shock (Rank 5)} Lvl 36\n31–60: 135–142 Nature.",
  "0{Dual Talent Specialization} Lvl 40\n31–60: two specs (Tavern); Apprentice Riding at 40. With the second spec you can keep Restoration for dungeons.",
  "0{Chain Heal} Lvl 40\n31–60: bouncing heal (Wowhead Forever tooltip).",
  "0{Stormstrike (Rank 2)} Lvl 40\n31–60: new Rank from the Wowhead Forever tooltip (ID 17364).",
  "0{Stormstrike} Lvl 25\nInstant, melee, 6 s cooldown, costs 8% of base Mana: +20% to the next Lightning Bolt/Chain Lightning/Earth Shock for 12 s.",
  "0{Improved Ghost Wolf} Lvl 27\nWith 2/2 Ghost Wolf is instant and usable indoors (row 4: at 26–27).",
  "0{Improved Stormstrike} Lvl 31\nStormstrike gives Mana regen and resets on every Dodge/Parry.",
  "0{Water Shield} Lvl 42\nWater shield: gives back Mana when you get hit (11 points in Restoration, like Tiqqle).",
  "0{Maelstrom Weapon} Lvl 46\nStacks on melee hits: Lightning Bolt faster and cheaper (spend it at 5 stacks).",
  "0{Rage of the Farseer} Lvl 51\n+30% attack speed per 25 s, cooldown 3 min.",
  "0{Dwarf Shaman:} The only Alliance race. Stoneform (10% Physical for 8 s + removes Bleed/Poison/Disease), Artisan's Precision +1% Hit, Big Game Hunter +5% damage to Beasts, Find Treasure. Weapon spec removed. Trainers: Teo Hammerstorm (Anvilmar), Ingrid Dunwald (Kharanos), Eldrun Stormbreaker (Ironforge) client.",
  "3Other races for the Shaman",
  "0• {Orc} (Horde): Blood Fury +10% AP and Spell Power for 15 s, 2 min cooldown (reduced Oct 27): the best burst for Enhancement. Shatter Curse, Hardiness 20% stun duration, Command useless. Axe Specialization and Savage removed Oct 26. Rankedboost (snippet): top race for Shaman.",
  "0• {Tauren} (Horde): War Stomp (stuns multiple enemies, 2 s), Plainsrunning up to +60% speed (2% per stack, not while mounted), Endurance +5% Health (hit and crit removed Oct 26), Cultivation. New trainer: Palah Thunderhoof (Camp Gev'rek).",
  "0• {Troll} (Horde): Berserking +10% cast and attack speed for 15 s (increased Oct 27), Rapid Regeneration (50% Health over time), Beast Slaying +5% to Beasts, Regeneration 10% in combat. Rankedboost (snippet): A.",
  "0• {Skyborne Windshaper} (Horde): Horde (Windshaper), Zephras Isle: Walk on Air (slow fall), Skysight +15% speed 15 s (30% with Charged for 1 h near an elemental convergence), Wind Blessed +2% Haste, Elemental Insight +5% damage to Elementals. Trainer: Windshaper Boro (Thendal Village 42.8, 23.6). Rankedboost (snippet): B.",
  "0• {Skyborne (High Order)} (Alliance): Horde (Windshaper), Zephras Isle: Walk on Air (slow fall), Skysight +15% speed 15 s (30% with Charged for 1 h near an elemental convergence), Wind Blessed +2% Haste, Elemental Insight +5% damage to Elementals. Trainer: Windshaper Boro (Thendal Village 42.8, 23.6). Rankedboost (snippet): B.",
  "0Mining + Herbalism or Skinning (Mobalytics gold tier list: S = Cooking, Fishing, Mining, Herbalism, Skinning, Alchemy, Enchanting). Mining and Herbalism also give Camp Tent / Mana Well / Incense Candle among the camp objects.",
  "0Method: Leatherworking + Skinning (Dark Leather Boots ~10, Brawler's Leather Hood ~20). Tavern: Enchanting for the Polished Driftwood Icon (BoP, a bonus you can't find elsewhere), Engineering + Mining for explosives, Cooking essential.",
  "2Advice for the Shaman",
  "0My recommendation: Leatherworking + Skinning for leveling gear; Cooking (Well Fed +5% XP) and First Aid for everyone. Alternatives: Mining + Engineering or Enchanting.\nSkinning + Leatherworking in leveling (Gfinity). Restoration and Elemental: Herbalism + Alchemy . Sources .",
  "2Priorities for the Shaman",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP up to 5% of a level, once an hour: the most useful for everyone. Leatherworking also gives gear (Method).",
  "0{Mana Well} · Alchemy priority 2\nUp to 29 mana/5 s: Mana is the Shaman's limit (Tavern).",
  "0{Incense Candle} · Herbalism priority 3\nUp to +25 Intellect: with Mental Dexterity and Mental Quickness, Intellect is worth AP and spell damage. my assessment from the talent tooltips.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing\n+8% to all stats: great for a melee character using AP, Intellect and crit.",
  "0{Camp Chair} · Skinning\n+2% crit: synergy with Thundering Strikes and Flurry.",
  "0{Enchanted Lute} · Enchanting\nArmor, stats, resistance. Tavern still recommends Enchanting anyway.",
  "0{Faction Banner} · Tailoring\nUp to +32 Spirit: little for an Enhancement.",
  "0{First Aid Kit} · First Aid\nUp to +56 Stamina: only useful if you tank with a shield.",
