  "1Race: Gnome",
  "0{Gnome Mage:} Expansive Mind (+Intellect) and Escape Artist to free yourself from roots.",
  "0{Escape Artist}\nInstant, 2 min cooldown: frees you from every movement impairing effect and gives immunity for 3 sec. client",
  "0{Eureka!}\nNew, instant, 2 min cooldown, for 8 sec: resource cost -10% and +10% damage (Mage: all damaging abilities; Warlock: non-periodic damaging; Priest: non-periodic damaging or healing). Varies by class. client",
  "0{Expansive Mind}\nChanged (passive): Maximum Mana +5% (Warrior: Maximum Rage +5%). In Classic it was +5% Intellect. client",
  "0{Engineering Specialization}\nChanged (passive): -20% failure/backfire of Engineering devices (Classic: +skill). client",
  "0Priest is a new combination (): Confounding Flash (AoE CC) and Contingency Plan (life-saving cooldown). Arcane Resistance removed. For the Mage, Eureka! + Expansive Mind help with mana; the Dun Morogh route is the v7 one.",
  "0• {Human} (Alliance): Extra Spirit (The Human Spirit) to regenerate mana.",
  "Class letter: Sten Stoutarm, Anvilmar.",
  "Confounding Flash (10): Gnome racial quest. Pick it up from Maxan Anvol (Kharanos) or High Priestess Mims (Ironforge). Reward: Confounding Flash (confuses up to 5 enemies for 3 s, 2 min cooldown).",
  "Contingency Plan (20): Gnome racial quest. Pick it up from High Priestess Laurena (Stormwind) or High Priestess Mims (Ironforge). Reward: Contingency Plan (30 s ward).",
  "0{Gnome Priest:} Alliance ( new for Priest). Confounding Flash (10, confuses 5 enemies for 3 s, 2 min CD ) and Contingency Plan (20, 30 s ward: below 35% absorbs + HoT, 5–10 min CD ); Escape Artist, Expansive Mind, Eureka!. DoubleZug: Human/Gnome are close seconds; CC: “Good”.",
  "Class letter: Sten Stoutarm, Anvilmar.",
  "0{Gnome Rogue:} Eureka! (10% less Energy and +10% damage for 8 s every 2 min), Expansive Mind +5% max Energy (105), Escape Artist, Engineering Specialization. DonTheCrown: 'my favorite Alliance race'; Rogue's Diary: A-tier for leveling; Warcraft Tavern: 'viable but not the best'.",
  "^spell_shadow_ragingscream^Trainer: Demon Skin, Summon Imp, Shadow Bolt, Immolate",
  "Class letter: Sten Stoutarm, Anvilmar.",
  "^spell_shadow_abominationexplosion^Trainer: Corruption, Curse of Weakness",
  "Beginnings (Gnome, level 4): talk to Alamar Grimm in Anvilmar. Bring 3 Feather Charm to Alamar. Reward: Summon Imp .",
  "^spell_shadow_burningspirit^Trainer: Life Tap",
  "^spell_shadow_curseofsargeras^Trainer: Bane of Agony, Fear",
  "^spell_shadow_haunting^Trainer: Drain Soul, Create Healthstone, Summon Voidwalker",
  "The Slaughtered Lamb (Gnome): talk to Lago Blackwrench in Ironforge and report back to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind. Then Gakin's chain: Surena's Choker, then The Binding (Bloodstone Choker, Voidwalker).",
  "^spell_shadow_lifedrain^Trainer: Health Funnel",
  "^spell_shadow_lifedrain02^Trainer: Drain Life, Curse of Recklessness",
  "0{Gnome Warlock:} Gnome (Alliance): Expansive Mind (+5% mana), Eureka! (10% mana and +10% damage on non-periodic spells for 8 s: useless for Affliction), Escape Artist, Engineering Specialization. Method: tier B, the weakest for Affliction.",
  "0• {Human} (Alliance): Human (Alliance): Ruthless (+crit, 2% according to Method), The Human Spirit (+Spirit, scales Life Tap), Will to Survive, Perception. Method: tier S. Sword Specialization was removed (the Warcraft Tavern guide is outdated on this).",
  "Class letter: Sten Stoutarm, Anvilmar.",
  "0{Gnome Warrior:} Escape Artist (removes slow/root + 3 s immunity), Eureka! (8 s: reduced costs and +10% damage), Expansive Mind +5% max Rage (little use with normalized Rage), Engineering Specialization (-20% backfire).",
