  "0{Natural Instinct} 2/2 · lvl 31–32",
  "0{Predatory Strikes} 3/3 · lvl 33",
  "0{Ferocity} 4/5 · lvl 34",
  "0{Rend and Tear} 5/5 · lvl 35–39",
  "0{Shifting Power} 1/1 · lvl 40",
  "0{Genesis} 5/5 · lvl 41–45",
  "0{Nature's Majesty} 2/2 · lvl 46–47",
  "0{Nature's Reach} 2/2 · lvl 48–49",
  "0{Heart of the Wild} 5/5 · lvl 50–54",
  "0{Naturalist} 5/5 · lvl 55–59",
  "0{Natural Shapeshifter} 1/3 · lvl 60",
  "0Mobalytics – yumytv, Druid Leveling Guide 1-60 – BUILD A · 87 · upd. Nov 4 · 9/31/11 at 60 · Ferocity 3 (10–12), Furor 5 (13–17), Feral Swiftness 2 (18–19) · Sharpened Claws · Sharpened Claws 2/2, Savage Fury 2, Feral Charge (24), Predatory Discipline, Blood Frenzy 2, Predatory Strikes 2, Leader of the Pack at 30; Shifting Power at 40",
  "0wowforever.be – client build (tree 70707) · client data, Nov 1 · Ferocity 5/5 (10–14), Feral Instinct 3/3 (15–17), Feral Swiftness 2/2 (18–19) · Feral Charge · Savage Fury 2, Shredding Attacks 3, Sharpened Claws 2, Lacerate, Predatory Discipline, Leader of the Pack at 30",
  "0Mobalytics – Ruse_Cruize, Druid Leveling Guide 1-30 (Verified) · 47 · Oct 28 · 0/21/0 (full order not readable; snippet) · Ferocity first; then 3 points in Heart of the Wild (then in the Feral tree) + Feral Swiftness 2/2 ('one of the best talents in the game for leveling') · (not visible) · (not visible) – all 21 points in Feral",
  "0Mobalytics – Feral Bear Tank guide (snippet) · Oct, not read · Ferocity 2/5 (10–12), Furor 3/5 (13–14), Feral Instinct 3/3 (15–17), Feral Swiftness 2/2 (18–19) · Feral Charge · not visible",
  "0Warcraft Tavern – Luxrah, Druid Leveling Guide (build 'Mid-level Feral', calculator decoded) · high reputation · PRE-hotfix tree (beta cap 30 + 5 Legacy) · Ferocity 5/5 (10–14), Feral Swiftness 2/2 (15–16), Heart of the Wild 3/5 (17–19; was in the Feral tree) · Feral Charge · Sharpened Claws 2 (21–22), Savage Fury 2 (23–24), Blood Frenzy 2 (25–26), Predatory Strikes 3 (27–29), Leader of the Pack (30); skips Shredding Attacks",
  "0Method – BirraGzeez, Druid Leveling Guide & Talents · upd. Oct 30 · PRE-hotfix tree · Ferocity first (Maul/Swipe less Rage), then Feral Swiftness · (Feral Charge) · Primal Bite + Shifting Power at 25 (OUTDATED: now row 7), Leader of the Pack, Predatory Strikes; Berserk (removed)",
  "0wowforever.gg (unofficial fan site) – Druid Feral Leveling Build · upd. Oct 30 · PRE-hotfix tree · Ferocity 5/5 + Heart of the Wild 3/5 + Feral Swiftness 2/2 · Feral Charge (11 points) · Shifting Power 25, Leader of the Pack 30, Primal Bite 35, Berserk 40 (outdated)",
  "0games.gg – Larc, Feral Druid 1-30 · Sep 17 (old) · Ferocity; Heart of the Wild 3 + Feral Swiftness 2 · Feral Charge · Sharpened Claws 2, Savage Fury 2, Predatory Strikes 3, 'Primal Fury' 2 (does not exist in the client), Leader of the Pack",
  "3Why not Balance and not Restoration",
  "0{Balance} works but is slower (Warcraft Tavern: 'much weaker for leveling'; Mobalytics: 'Feral will be much smoother'; Tekn0de's videos, 55k views, Sep 29, and Psybear_tv, 50k, Oct 7, treat it as an option). Builds: {Multi-DoT} (Improved Entangling Roots, Overgrowth 2 = 3 roots, Insect Swarm at 25) or {Eclipse} (Improved Starfire + Eclipse: after 30, 2 Starfire for 1 Wrath). {Restoration}: not recommended solo due to slow kill times (Tavern); Mobalytics rates it 'strong enough' but with no damage or mobility. Balance/Restoration are more useful as a second dungeon spec with Dual Talent Specialization (40).",
  "3'Tavern/Method-style' variant on the new tree",
  "0Pre-hotfix guides replace Shredding Attacks/Lacerate/Predatory Discipline with {Sharpened Claws 2 -> Savage Fury 2 -> Blood Frenzy 2 -> Predatory Strikes 3} (Predatory Strikes = AP equal to 150% of your level at 3/3) and Leader of the Pack at 30. These talents still exist in client 70707 (Predatory Strikes and Blood Frenzy require 15 points; Blood Frenzy requires Sharpened Claws), but the order has not been verified on the new tree. Tavern skips Shredding Attacks because 'you don't Shred much solo': Feral Charge from Cat and Prowl still put you behind the mob.",
  "0If you do lots of Bear dungeons: Thick Hide, Brutal Impact, Natural Reaction and Lacerate (Tavern 'Hybrid', Method 'tank-leaning').",
  "3What changed with the Oct 30 hotfix (build 70707)",
  "0• {Berserk} removed from the tree.",
  "0• {Furor} and {Heart of the Wild} swapped trees: Furor is now in Feral, Heart of the Wild in Restoration.",
  "0• {Primal Bite} (42/62/77 damage, previously 26/38/59) and {Shifting Power} (CD 8 s, previously 16 s) moved to row 7: they need 30 points in the tree, so level 40/41, not 25 as Tavern, Method and wowforever.gg still write.",
  "0• New: {Lacerate} (Feral talent), {Predatory Discipline} (Feral), {Bloom} (Restoration). Removed: Improved Shifting Power, Gift of the Earthmother.",
  "0• Leader of the Pack now applies to all crits; Genesis 2–10%; Naturalist 2–10%; Swiftmend requires your Rejuvenation/Regrowth; Wild Growth 3 s cast. (wowforever.be news Oct 31, GitHub wowforever-helper #455, Tactyks 15.8k views Oct 31.)",
  "0• 26 other talents were moved, without a list: {check the tooltips in-game}.",
  "31–9 · Caster (no form)",
  "0^spell_nature_thorns,spell_nature_abolishmagic,spell_nature_starfall,ability_meleedamage^Thorns (from 6) -> Wrath (pull) -> Moonfire -> Wrath -> Auto-attack",
  "0Thorns on yourself. Wrath to engage, Moonfire for the DoT, Wrath while you have mana, then finish in melee. Rejuvenation on yourself when needed. With Moonfire you can keep the DoT on 2 mobs (games.gg). Out of mana = auto-attack. Sources: Warcraft Tavern, games.gg, Method.",
  "310–19 · Bear Form",
  "0^spell_nature_resistnature,ability_racial_bearform,ability_druid_enrage,ability_druid_demoralizingroar,ability_druid_maul^Heal pre-pull -> Bear Form -> Enrage -> Demoralizing Roar -> Maul / Swipe",
  "0Before the pull, heal up (Rejuvenation, Regrowth, Healing Touch), then Wrath x2 + Moonfire from range and Bear Form when the mob arrives (Method). Enrage for instant Rage, Demoralizing Roar only on physical mobs, Maul on single target, Swipe (16) on 2+ mobs. Feral Charge only arrives at 20 on the client build (games.gg had it earlier: outdated). Don't pull more than 2 mobs.",
  "320–30 · Cat Form",
  "0^ability_ambush,ability_druid_disembowel,spell_shadow_vampiricaura,ability_druid_rake,ability_ghoulfrenzy^Prowl -> Rake -> Shred (from behind) -> Claw -> Rip (4–5 CP)",
  "0Rejuvenation before the pull, wait a few seconds in Cat Form to fill Energy. Prowl, then Feral Charge behind the mob or Shred from behind; Faerie Fire to pull from range; Rake if the mob lives longer than ~6 s; Shred (Claw if you're not behind) for Combo Points; Rip only if the mob still lives 10 s, otherwise keep going with Claw/Shred. From 24 Tiger's Fury . Dash to move. No finishers needed on mobs that die in 3 hits. Sources: Tavern, Method, games.gg.",
  "330–60 · Advanced Cat",
  "0^ability_ambush,ability_druid_ravage,spell_nature_faeriefire,ability_druid_disembowel,ability_druid_ferociousbite^Prowl -> Ravage / Pounce -> Faerie Fire -> Rake -> Ferocious Bite (5 CP)",
  "0Ravage (32) or Pounce (36) from Prowl, Faerie Fire, Rake, Shred/Claw up to 5 Combo Points, Ferocious Bite (with Predatory Discipline). At 41, use Shifting Power when just under 50 Energy. From 40, Dire Bear Form for dungeons and multiple mobs (Method).",
  "0^ability_racial_bearform,ability_druid_enrage,ability_druid_demoralizingroar,inv_misc_monsterclaw_03^Bear Form -> Enrage -> Demoralizing Roar -> Swipe",
  "0More than 2 mobs: Bear Form, Enrage, Roar (physical only), Swipe (Feral Instinct +30%). Entangling Roots keeps one extra out; Nature's Grasp to escape; Bash to stop a mob. There's no AoE from Cat: with 3+ mobs switch to Bear.",
  "3Resources and downtime",
  "0• {Mana} keeps regenerating in form but is hidden: enable 'Personal Resource Display' in Options, Combat (Tavern). Mana is needed to return to form (shifting costs Mana; Natural Shapeshifter 30%) and for Shifting Power.",
  "0• Energy and Rage regenerate continuously; in Bear, Energy doesn't regenerate, and Powershifting/Bear Weaving are no longer worth it (Tavern). Furor gives the resource back when you shift.",
  "0• Potions, bandages and food can be used without leaving form (Oct 1–8); most items and NPCs are usable in form, but heals and utility (Rebirth, Innervate, Cure Poison) require leaving it.",
  "0• Heal between pulls: Rejuvenation (Swiftmend only at 60). Carry water suited to your level (a new one every ~10 levels).",
  "0• Shifting removes root and slow: shift instead of waiting.",
  "0• Idol of Shifting Tides (Aquatic Form quest): less mana for shapeshifts.",
  "3Position and Combo Points",
  "0Shred requires being behind the mob; from behind you can't be parried or hit by frontal attacks. Feral Charge from Cat puts you behind automatically. Combo Points: Tavern says they don't carry over between targets, games.gg (Sep 17) says they do: verify in-game. Bleeds ignore armor: great against armored mobs.",
  "0Feral priority: Strength / Agility / Attack Power > Stamina / Intellect / Spirit > Armor (Tavern, Mid-level Feral); games.gg: Strength > Agility = Stamina > Intellect > Spirit; wow.gg: Weapon Damage > Hit/Expertise > Crit. Before 10 (and for Balance): Intellect/Spell Damage. In Forever, attacks in Cat/Bear scale with weapon DPS (speed 1.0 or 2.5 s depending on form): the weapon with the highest DPS is the best upgrade. Polearms from 20; also Daggers, Fist Weapons, One/Two-Handed Maces, Staves (weapon trainer in Ironforge, Thunder Bluff, Orgrimmar, Undercity, Stormwind). Items cited: Wolfshead Helm (Leatherworking), Manual Crowd Pummeler (Gnomeregan 29–38), Embrace of the Viper (set, Wailing Caverns 17–24, also changes Cat Form), Idol of Shifting Tides (Aquatic Form quest). Crafting levels and requirements not read .",
  "0• Oct 30 (build 70707; wowforever.be news Oct 31, GitHub #455, Tactyks 15.8k views Oct 31): Druid tree reshuffled: Berserk removed, Furor/Heart of the Wild swapped trees, Primal Bite 42/62/77 moved to row 7, Shifting Power CD 8 s, Leader of the Pack on all crits, new Lacerate/Predatory Discipline/Bloom.",
  "0• Potions and consumables (including Thistle Tea and mana potions) usable in Bear/Cat without leaving form; weapon enchants and procs work in form; immune to Disarm (Oct 1–8, wofwforever Oct 15).",
  "0• Auto-attack from form uses weapon DPS (1.0 s Cat / 2.5 s Bear); new Polearms at 20.",
  "0• Powershifting and Bear Weaving no longer worthwhile; Furor restores 100% of Energy on shift (Tavern, Oct 15).",
  "0• Nature's Grasp (10), Revive (12), Omen of Clarity (20, passive), Faerie Fire and Shred (20, Oct 15) base; Dual Talent Specialization at 40.",
  "0• Claw ~110% weapon damage (like Mangle), Shred 155% (from 225%), Tiger's Fury +15% damage 6 s , Enrage 30 total Rage, Frenzied Regeneration percentage-based, all DoTs can crit (KamiLabs, Sep 26; not re-verified on client).",
  "0• Cat Form no longer lowers max HP (Oct 8), +50% threat from Bear (Oct 8), Faerie Fire costs nothing and has a 6 s CD in form with threat (Oct 15).",
  "0• Talented (Legacy): talent points from level 5 instead of 10 (client spell 1225474; Tavern: up to 5 levels earlier).",
  "0• New Skyborne race (Zephras Isle 3–12, local Druid trainer) with dedicated form quests.",
  "0• At launch (Blizzard notes of 3 Nov): Claw 140% weapon damage, Shred 200%, Ravage 435%; Rip, Rake, Pounce and Ferocious Bite about +25%; Starfire about +40%; Dire Bear Form +115% threat; Rend and Tear up to 15%.",
  "0{Mark of the Wild} Lvl 1\nStat and resistance buff for you and the party; always keep it up (works on pets too).",
  "0{Wrath} Lvl 1\nNature damage with cast; your pull attack until 10.",
  "0{Healing Touch} Lvl 1\nCast heal: heal up between pulls.",
  "0{Moonfire} Lvl 4\nArcane damage + DoT, can crit (the DoT too). Keep it up on 2 mobs.",
  "0{Rejuvenation} Lvl 4\nHoT: heal up before every pull.",
  "0{Thorns} Lvl 6\nDamages whoever hits you; scales with spell power. Keep it on yourself at all times.",
  "0{Entangling Roots} Lvl 8\nRanged root to keep an extra mob away.",
  "0{Bear Form} Lvl 10\nClass quest (see steps). High armor and HP, Rage as resource; slightly less HP than in Classic.",
  "0{Growl} Lvl 10\nSingle-target taunt (from the Bear Form quest).",
  "0{Maul} Lvl 10\nYour single-target Rage spender (from the quest).",
  "0{Demoralizing Roar} Lvl 10\nDebuff that reduces physical mob damage; don't use it on casters.",
  "0{Nature's Grasp} Lvl 10\nNow base at 10: roots whoever hits you in melee, so you can escape.",
  "0{Teleport: Moonglade} Lvl 10\nClass quest: teleport to Moonglade (trainer Loganaar in Nighthaven).",
  "0{Regrowth} Lvl 12\nHeal + HoT, faster than Healing Touch.",
  "0{Revive} Lvl 12\nNow base at 12: resurrects a player out of combat.",
  "0{Enrage} Lvl 12\n10 Rage instantly + 20 over 10 s (total 30), 1 min CD; from Bear.",
  "0{Cure Poison} Lvl 14\nClass quest 'Lessons Anew': removes a Poison.",
  "0{Bash} Lvl 14\nStun from Bear; with Brutal Impact it stuns longer and has a shorter CD.",
  "0{Aquatic Form} Lvl 16\nClass quest 'A Lesson to Learn': fast swimming and infinite breath. Reward: Idol of Shifting Tides.",
  "0{Swipe} Lvl 16\nYour AoE from Bear; Feral Instinct +30%.",
  "0{Faerie Fire} Lvl 18\nBase (no talent needed): armor debuff, ranged pull; costs 0 in form, 6 s CD and generates threat (Oct 15).",
  "0{Hibernate} Lvl 18\nCrowd control on Beast and Dragonkin (Classic data).",
  "0{Cat Form} Lvl 20\nClass quest 'The Great Cat Spirit': melee DPS with Energy and Combo Points. No longer lowers max HP.",
  "0{Claw} Lvl 20\nCombo Point builder (from the quest); now ~110% weapon damage like Mangle (KamiLabs, Sep 26).",
  "0{Prowl} Lvl 20\nStealth in Cat Form: you choose when to engage.",
  "0{Rip} Lvl 20\nBleed finisher (from the quest); only use it if the mob lives long enough.",
  "0{Shred} Lvl 20\nRank 1 at 20 (was 22, Oct 15): builder from behind, ~155% weapon damage.",
  "0{Starfire} Lvl 20\nArcane damage with a long cast (for Balance, rarely for Feral).",
  "0{Rebirth} Lvl 20\nCombat resurrection: consumes a reagent (depends on Rank).",
  "0{Omen of Clarity} Lvl 20\nNow a base passive: free spell/ability procs, including on DoT/HoT ticks.",
  "0{Polearms} Lvl 20\nNew weapon for Druids: Woo Ping (Stormwind) / Archibald (Undercity).",
  "0{Soothe Animal} Lvl 22\nCalms an animal (Classic data).",
  "0{Remove Curse} Lvl 24\nRemoves a Curse.",
  "0{Rake} Lvl 24\nBuilder + bleed: use it if the mob lives longer than ~6 s.",
  "0{Tiger's Fury} Lvl 24\n(KamiLabs Sep 26, not in Tavern/Method): +15% to all damage for 6 s, DoTs included; level to be verified.",
  "0{Dash} Lvl 26\nSprint in Cat Form.",
  "0{Abolish Poison} Lvl 26\nRemoves Poison over time.",
  "0{Cower} Lvl 28\nLess threat from Cat (useful in groups).",
  "0{Challenging Roar} Lvl 28\nAoE taunt from Bear, 10 min CD.",
  "0{Travel Form} Lvl 30\n+40% outdoor running speed without a mount: replaces a mount until 40.",
  "0{Tranquility} Lvl 30\nGroup heal in a channel.",
  "0{Ferocious Bite} Lvl 32\nFinisher from Cat; with Predatory Discipline it deals extra damage based on excess Energy.",
  "0{Ravage} Lvl 32\nStealth opener from behind (Cat).",
  "0{Track Humanoids} Lvl 32\nHumanoid tracking in Cat Form.",
  "0{Pounce} Lvl 36\nOpener from Prowl with stun.",
  "0{Frenzied Regeneration} Lvl 36\nConverts Rage into HP as a percentage (10 Rage = 10% HP).",
  "0{Dire Bear Form} Lvl 40\nImproved Bear Form (trainer).",
  "0{Innervate} Lvl 40\nPowerful mana regen; leave form to cast it.",
  "0{Hurricane} Lvl 40\nNo cooldown (Balance).",
  "0{Feline Grace} Lvl 40\nCat passive (trainer, Tavern data; effect not read ).",
  "0{Dual Talent Specialization} Lvl 40\nSecond spec (e.g. Feral + Restoration for dungeons).",
  "0{Barkskin} Lvl 44\nDamage reduction in every form.",
  "0{Feral Charge} Lvl 24\nBear: charge + root + interrupt 4 s; Cat: leaps behind the target (CD 30 s).",
  "0{Lacerate (not in build)} Lvl 28\nBleed stacks up to 5 for threat from Bear (talent on wowforever.be; Tavern/Method list it as a trainer skill at 42, Zockify as a talent at 25: ).",
  "0{Leader of the Pack} Lvl 30\n+3% crit to you and the party in Cat/Bear Form (aura).",
  "0{Primal Bite (not in build)} Lvl 40\nBite with 42 extra damage and lots of threat (row 7 = level 40).",
  "0{Shifting Power} Lvl 40\n55% of Base Mana into 40 Energy, CD 8 s (from Cat).",
  "0{Swiftmend (not in build)} Lvl 60\nInstant heal that consumes your Rejuvenation/Regrowth.",
  "1Race: Night Elf",
  "0{Night Elf Druid:} Alliance. Elune's Light (+10% crit for 15 s, burst), Shadowmeld, Quickness (+1% Dodge, +2% speed), Wisp Spirit. games.gg: 'the best for parses, close to Tauren'; Method: the Alliance's all-around choice. Druid quests in Darnassus.",
  "0{Elune's Light}\nNew, instant, 3 min cooldown: +10% critical strike with all spells and attacks for 15 sec. client",
  "0{Shadowmeld}\nBase 10 sec cooldown: hides you until you move. In combat now reduces aggro, but the cooldown rises to 2 min. client (icon from tooltip 20580)",
  "0{Quickness}\nPassive: Dodge +1% and movement speed +2%; Rogue and Druid are harder to see in stealth (as if 1 level higher). changed. client",
  "0{Wisp Spirit}\nPassive: after death you become a wisp with +75% speed (client tooltip). Warcraft Tavern writes \"extra 25%\": discrepancy.",
  "0No new class. Nature Resistance removed. Teldrassil is an island: the first useful Flight Master is Vesprystus in Rut'theran, who only flies to Auberdine. Soft Saber Sack (6 slots) from Aldia in Dolanaar at lvl 4.",
  "3Other races for the Druid",
  "0• {Tauren} (Horde): Horde. War Stomp (stun 2 s on 5 enemies, CD 90 s, usable in form ), Cultivation (duplicates an herb, CD 15 min), Plainsrunning (+1% speed every 5 s up to +30%, +3% mounted), Endurance (+5% HP and +1% Hit). games.gg: 'the strongest' for Druids; Method: ideal for Bear tank and PvP. Quests in Thunder Bluff.",
  "0• {Skyborne (High Order)} (Alliance): High Order (Alliance). Walk on Air (slow fall, CD 90 s), Wind Blessed (+1–2% haste conflicting numbers), Elemental Insight (+5% damage vs Elemental), Read Ley Line (+50%/100% HP and Mana regen for 15 s, CD 2 min, doesn't stack with Innervate: reduces downtime between pulls). You start at Zephras Isle (3–12).",
  "0• {Skyborne Windshaper} (Horde): Windshaper (Horde). Walk on Air, Wind Blessed, Elemental Insight, Skysight (+10–15% speed, 15 s, CD 2 min conflicting numbers). Method: Windshaper is great for Feral Cat and Balance thanks to haste. Zephras Isle, then trainer in Dalaran (Alfina Nightgaze) for the Horde.",
  "0Herbalism + Alchemy or Mining (Method/Birra: Herbalism + Alchemy for gold and consumables, Mining + Engineering is solid). Herbalism with Travel Form (30) gathers without leaving form; Tauren can duplicate herbs with Cultivation. Cooking and Fishing for everyone (Mobalytics gold tier list already used in the Mage guide: S = Cooking, Fishing, Mining, Herbalism, Skinning, Alchemy, Enchanting) .",
  "0Skinning + Leatherworking (Tavern, Method 'best solo', wow.gg): soulbound gear for leveling, Camp Tent and Wolfshead Helm. Cooking for the XP buff and for the Basic Campfire; First Aid to cure bleeds/diseases and craft health potions.",
  "2Advice for the Druid",
  "0Main: Skinning + Leatherworking (power) or Herbalism + Mining/Alchemy (gold). For everyone: Cooking, First Aid and Fishing. The Camp Chair (Skinning) buff is redundant from 30 due to Leader of the Pack.\nSkinning + Leatherworking in leveling (Gfinity). Open world: Herbalism + Alchemy, gathering in Travel Form (Gfinity). Sources .",
  "04 · {Soft Saber Sack} · 6 · Soft Saber Pelts quest: Aldia, Dolanaar /way Teldrassil 55.4 57.2. Gather 6 Soft Nightsaber Pelts. Method + leprestore.",
  "07 · {Wizbang's Gunnysack} · 8 · Buzzbox chain from Wizbang Cranktoggle (Auberdine inn, 37.0 44.1), from 7; Buzzbox 525 gives the bag: 8 slots in Forever (was 6). Method.",
  "08+ · {Red Linen Bag (Tailoring 70)} · 8 · Pattern 2 silver from Valdaron (Darkshore). Vendor: Small Brown Pouch 6, Brown Leather Satchel 8, Heavy Brown Bag 10. Method.",
  "01 · {Rut'theran Village} · Vesprystus /way 58.4 94.0 · Free with the Darnassus quest ; Vesprystus only flies to Auberdine.",
  "02 · {Auberdine} · Caylais Moonfeather /way 36.3 45.6 · As soon as you arrive (11); Hearthstone here.",
  "03 · {Astranaar} · Daelyshia /way 34.4 48.0 · As soon as you arrive in Ashenvale (19). games.gg: pick it up right away.",
  "04 · {Stormwind} · Dungar Longdrink /way 66.3 62.1 · After the boat Auberdine -> Stormwind (Westfall/Duskwood).",
  "05 · {Sentinel Hill} · Thor /way 56 52 · After Stormwind, for Westfall.",
  "06 · {Darkshire} · Felicia Maline /way 77 44 · If you go to Duskwood.",
  "0• Boat Auberdine Stormwind Harbor (new) wmd",
  "0• Boat Auberdine -> Menethil Harbor and Menethil -> Southshore -> Auberdine wmd",
  "0• Boat Rut'theran Village Auberdine wmd; portal Darnassus Rut'theran",
  "0• Free flight Rut'theran -> Auberdine (Nessa Shadowsong) games.gg only",
  "2Priorities for the Druid",
  "0{Camp Tent} · Leatherworking priority 1\nRested XP up to 5% of a level, once an hour: the most useful; LW also gives soulbound gear for Druids.",
  "0{Fish Bowl} · Fishing priority 2\n+8% to all stats (equivalent to Blessing of Kings): scales with AP and HP in Cat and Bear.",
  "0{Lodestone} · Mining priority 3\nLike Blessing of Might: Attack Power for Cat/Bear (value not read).",
